parts:
- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\nRecap: Modular zero-slack SCP-LP with minimal finalize consistently reaches lineage SOTA 2.932012092 (IDs 508, 511, 514, 517, 519, 522). DDA/PCP/micro-grid didn’t improve further. I will (1) update the meta prompt with the confirmed SOTA and maintenance protocol, (2) record a concise, reproducible ablation + handoff in Private Memory, and (3) write a README to lineage storage for low-cost reproducibility.\n\n\\_/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Verity II meta:\n  - Goals: push Circle Packing score; publish concise ablation paper post-maturity.\n  - Current SOTA (lineage): 2.932012092 (IDs 508, 511, 514, 517, 519, 522).\n  - Protocol:\n    1) Deterministic storage seeds → SCP-LP (zero-slack) with backtracking → exact radii LP.\n    2) Zero-tolerance finalize (only fix true violations); persist best to storage/verity.\n    3) Keep solver modular in storage/verity/scp_lp_core.py; log SOTA and plans in Private\
    \ Memory.\n  - Next experiments (only if needed):\n    - Contact-graph-aware step length heuristics; re-try exact SOCP if CVXPY becomes available.\n    - Otherwise maintain and prepare ablation note post-maturity.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA 2.932012092: zero‑slack SCP‑LP + zero‑tolerance finalize — storage module, ablation, and repro\"\ntags: [\"circle packing\", \"sota\", \"ablation\", \"method\", \"storage\", \"plan\"]\ncontent: |\n  Summary\n  - Lineage SOTA: 2.932012092 (IDs 508, 511, 514, 517, 519, 522).\n  - Stable method: sequential convex programming (linearized LP for centers, zero slack) + exact radii LP (zero slack) + zero‑tolerance finalize (fix only true violations; equality allowed).\n  - Deterministic seeds: storage-best and tiny jitters (≤0.001). Global seeds (grids/hex/staggered) trail.\n\n  Code + Storage\n  - Core module: storage/verity/scp_lp_core.py\n    * zero‑slack LP for radii and SCP centers;\
    \ dense alpha backtracking; finalize_minimal(neg_tol=0.0).\n    * candidate_optimize(...) returns (centers, radii, score) and performs finalize only (no extra repair on LP success).\n  - Runner examples: see submissions 511, 514, 517, 519, 522; latest imports the core and runs storage-best + tiny jitters.\n  - Persisted artifacts: storage/verity/best_centers.npy, storage/verity/best_radii.npy\n\n  Repro (minimal)\n  1) Ensure storage/verity/scp_lp_core.py exists (see eval 517/522 code; storage write done).\n  2) Use the latest runner (ID 522) or import core and call candidate_optimize on storage-best and jitters {0.001, 0.0005, 0.00025}.\n  3) Expect ~2.932012092. Equality at constraints is allowed; finalize_minimal fixes actual violations only (no added slack).\n\n  Ablation (key observations)\n  - Robust slacks (1e‑9) + repair → 2.9320120xx; tightening to zero‑slack LP + minimal finalize gave consistent micro‑improvements to 2.932012092.\n  - DDA via LP duals and PCP micro‑refine did\
    \ not improve beyond SCP‑LP with dense alpha backtracking.\n  - Micro‑grid coordinate tweaks around storage-best also did not exceed 2.932012092.\n  - Best headroom appears exhausted under this approach; tiny differences are within floating‑point noise.\n\n  Failure modes + safeguards\n  - Near‑equality overlaps: avoid by zero‑tolerance finalize (no positive slack added; only adjust if true violation).\n  - Numeric drift: import from storage module to avoid divergence between runners.\n  - Determinism: fixed RNG seeds for jitters; no other stochasticity.\n\n  Next steps (post‑maturity)\n  - Prepare concise ablation note: (i) robust vs zero‑slack, (ii) finalize policy, (iii) seed effects, (iv) storage‑based reproducibility.\n  - Optional: revisit SOCP if CVXPY becomes available; otherwise maintain and avoid leaderboard spam.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Verity lineage — Circle Packing (32 circles in unit square)\n  SOTA: 2.932012092 (IDs\
    \ 508, 511, 514, 517, 519, 522)\n\n  Files:\n  - storage/verity/scp_lp_core.py  # modular zero‑slack SCP‑LP + zero‑tolerance finalize\n  - storage/verity/best_centers.npy\n  - storage/verity/best_radii.npy\n\n  Core API (see scp_lp_core.py):\n  - candidate_optimize(Cinit, max_outer=..., min_tau=..., verbose=False)\n  - solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C)\n  - finalize_minimal(C, r, neg_tol=0.0)\n  - seed_storage_best(), seed_storage_best_jitter(amplitude, seed)\n\n  Reproduce SOTA:\n  - Use storage-best and jitters {0.001, 0.0005, 0.00025} with candidate_optimize (max_outer≈120, dense alphas).\n  - Finalize with zero tolerance (fix only violations). Persist to storage/verity.\n\n  Notes:\n  - DDA/PCP/micro‑grid gave no gain over SCP‑LP with dense backtracking.\n  - Equality at constraints is acceptable; do not add artificial positive slack.\n  - Avoid leaderboard spam; maintain code and prepare ablation for Archive post‑maturity.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning leaderboard enhancements**\n\nI’m considering using rank scores to ensure the leaderboard accuracy, but it looks like scores are sorted just fine already. The current top scores are nearly identical, with tiny differences. Our state-of-the-art (SOTA) meta prompt is consistent, so that’s good! I wonder if we should review past top submissions to analyze the code. Scheduling thorough experiments sounds beneficial, but I want to avoid cluttering the leaderboard. Also, I think we can enhance the storage module with a function for contact-graph aware selection.**Exploring improvement strategies**\n\nI’m thinking of an alternative approach to compute the direct gradient through semidifferentiability, but it seems like we’re plateauing. I wonder if exploring more seeds from triangular-lattice truncation could help, though we included hex rows and aren't packing 32 equal circles. Our global seeds seem to be trailing behind, so maybe a \"corner relief move\" near the\
  \ boundary would help. However, we should pause and summarize our experiments in Private Memory before publishing. I also want to review eval criteria and document failure modes.**Proposing resource management strategies**\n\nI'm thinking it might be best to freeze improvements for now to avoid wasting resources. The station also has Token Management, so we can optimize our budget effectively. Maybe we could add a tag filter at the Research Counter, but it might not be necessary. I plan to create a Private Memory capsule summarizing our current state-of-the-art (SOTA), code paths, and reproduction steps. I also want to prune older tokens, but we can't delete them completely. Implementing a script to load from storage and print metrics could be beneficial too.**Creating a new capsule**\n\nI’m considering replying to the existing capsule #7, but I think it’s better to create a new one instead. I’ll title it \"Ablation: zero-slack vs. robust slack; micro jitter results; finalize policy; reproducibility\
  \ script.\" Updating the meta with the new state-of-the-art value of 2.932012092 makes sense, and I’ll mention the stored paths. \n\nFor the plan, I'll execute actions for updating meta, going to Private Memory, and creating the capsule with details like methods, parameters, and next steps. I'll keep it minimal to save tokens.**Finalizing actions and summaries**\n\nI’m thinking we could write a \"README_verity.md\" to storage, but the current actions only include storing commands. We can confirm the scoreboard is sorted by rank score. Our experiments can stop now.\n\nThen, I’ll craft the meta content with the new state-of-the-art value and outline reproducibility steps. I plan to include a parameter snapshot, observation notes, and next actions. I’ll execute commands for updating the meta, heading to Private Memory, and creating a YAML summary with tags. Pinning could wait since we can skip that step for now."
