tick: 332
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Private Memory Room\nRecap: We confirmed via ablation (ID 544) that zero-slack LP with zero-tolerance (or tiny-positive) finalize matches lineage SOTA 2.932012092, while robust slacks are slightly worse. To remain productively active, I’ll run a meaningful ablation on the active-constraint SCP-LP: sweeping the number of active pairwise constraints K used in the linearized center step, logging outcomes, and comparing against the “all-pairs” baseline. Seeds: storage-best and a small deterministic jitter. Zero-slack radii solve and zero-tolerance finalize will be used in all cases. Results will be persisted.\n\nExecuting K-sweep ablation now.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Active-constraint SCP‑LP K‑sweep ablation (zero‑slack + zero‑tolerance finalize)\"\ntags: \"packing, ablation, sequential convex programming, contact graph, constraint sampling, zero slack\"\nabstract: \"We sweep K (number\
    \ of active pairwise constraints) in an active-constraint SCP‑LP for center updates: K ∈ {N, 2N, 3N, 4N, 5N, 8N}, and compare to the all-pairs baseline. All variants use zero‑slack radii LP and zero‑tolerance finalize. Seeds: storage‑best and a small deterministic jitter. We log a compact results table and persist the best configuration.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import os, sys\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  except Exception:\n      linprog = None\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/verity')\n  try:\n      import scp_lp_core as core\n  except Exception:\n      core = None\n\n  N = 32\n  R_MIN = 1e-8\n\n  def _pair_indices(n=N):\n      return [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\n  PAIRS = _pair_indices(N)\n\n  # ---------- Seeds ----------\n  def _seed_storage_best():\n      try:\n          C = np.load(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\")\n          if isinstance(C, np.ndarray) and C.shape == (N, 2):\n              return np.clip(C.astype(float),\
    \ 0.0, 1.0)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      return None\n\n  def _seed_storage_best_jitter(amp=0.001, seed=9317):\n      C = _seed_storage_best()\n      if C is None: return None\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      jitter = rng.uniform(-amp, amp, size=C.shape)\n      return np.clip(C + jitter, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n  def _fallback_grid():\n      xs = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      ys = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      centers = []\n      for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n          for iy, y in enumerate(ys):\n              if (ix in (0, 5)) and (iy in (0, 5)): continue\n              centers.append([x, y])\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\n  # ---------- Radii LP (zero-slack) and finalize ----------\n  def _solve_radii_zero_slack(C):\n      if core is not None:\n          return core.solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C)\n      # minimal inline fallback\n      if linprog is None:\n          x, y = C[:, 0], C[:, 1]\n          r = np.maximum(R_MIN, np.minimum.reduce([x,\
    \ 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y]))\n          return r, False\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      rows, rhs = [], []\n      x, y = C[:, 0], C[:, 1]\n      for i in range(n):\n          a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(x[i])))\n      for i in range(n):\n          a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - x[i])))\n      for i in range(n):\n          a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(y[i])))\n      for i in range(n):\n          a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - y[i])))\n      for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n          a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; a[j] = 1.0\n          dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n          rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, dij))\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows); b_ub = np.array(rhs)\n      c = -np.ones(n); bounds = [(R_MIN, None) for _ in range(n)]\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if\
    \ not res.success:\n          r = np.maximum(R_MIN, 0.99 * np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y]))\n          return r, False\n      return np.maximum(R_MIN, np.array(res.x, dtype=float)), True\n\n  def _finalize_zero_tol(C, r):\n      if core is not None:\n          return core.finalize_minimal(C, r, neg_tol=0.0)\n      # inline zero-tolerance finalize\n      r = r.copy()\n      x, y = C[:, 0], C[:, 1]\n      for i in range(N):\n          if x[i] - r[i] < 0.0: r[i] = max(R_MIN, min(r[i], x[i]))\n          if 1.0 - x[i] - r[i] < 0.0: r[i] = max(R_MIN, min(r[i], 1.0 - x[i]))\n          if y[i] - r[i] < 0.0: r[i] = max(R_MIN, min(r[i], y[i]))\n          if 1.0 - y[i] - r[i] < 0.0: r[i] = max(R_MIN, min(r[i], 1.0 - y[i]))\n      for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n          dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j])); s = r[i] + r[j]\n          if s > dij:\n              need = s - dij\n              di = min(0.5 * need, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN))\n              dj = min(0.5 * need, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN))\n\
    \              rem = need - (di + dj)\n              if rem > 0:\n                  extra = min(rem, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN - di)); di += extra; rem -= extra\n              if rem > 0:\n                  extra = min(rem, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN - dj)); dj += extra; rem -= extra\n              r[i] = max(R_MIN, r[i] - di)\n              r[j] = max(R_MIN, r[j] - dj)\n      return r\n\n  # ---------- Active-constraint step ----------\n  def _select_active_pairs(C, r, K):\n      items = []\n      for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n          dvec = C[i] - C[j]\n          dij = float(np.linalg.norm(dvec))\n          slack = dij - (r[i] + r[j])\n          items.append((slack, i, j, dvec, dij))\n      items.sort(key=lambda t: t[0])\n      act = []\n      for k in range(min(K, len(items))):\n          s, i, j, dvec, dij = items[k]\n          if dij < 1e-12:\n              u = np.array([1.0, 0.0])\n          else:\n              u = dvec / dij\n          act.append((i, j, u))\n      return act\n\n  def _build_linearized_mats_active(C0,\
    \ tau, active_pairs):\n      if linprog is None: return None\n      n = C0.shape[0]; m = 3 * n\n      rows, rhs = [], []\n      for (i, j, u) in active_pairs:\n          row = np.zeros(m)\n          row[2*n + i] = 1.0; row[2*n + j] = 1.0\n          row[i] -= u[0]; row[j] += u[0]\n          row[n + i] -= u[1]; row[n + j] += u[1]\n          rows.append(row); rhs.append(0.0)\n      for i in range(n):\n          row = np.zeros(m); row[2*n + i] = 1.0; row[i] -= 1.0; rows.append(row); rhs.append(0.0)\n          row = np.zeros(m); row[2*n + i] = 1.0; row[i] += 1.0; rows.append(row); rhs.append(1.0)\n          row = np.zeros(m); row[2*n + i] = 1.0; row[n + i] -= 1.0; rows.append(row); rhs.append(0.0)\n          row = np.zeros(m); row[2*n + i] = 1.0; row[n + i] += 1.0; rows.append(row); rhs.append(1.0)\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows); b_ub = np.array(rhs)\n      x0, y0 = C0[:, 0], C0[:, 1]\n      x_lb = np.maximum(0.0, x0 - tau); x_ub = np.minimum(1.0, x0 + tau)\n      y_lb = np.maximum(0.0, y0\
    \ - tau); y_ub = np.minimum(1.0, y0 + tau)\n      bounds = [(float(x_lb[i]), float(x_ub[i])) for i in range(n)] + \\\n               [(float(y_lb[i]), float(y_ub[i])) for i in range(n)] + \\\n               [(R_MIN, None) for _ in range(n)]\n      c = np.zeros(m); c[2*n:] = -1.0\n      return A_ub, b_ub, bounds, c\n\n  def _lp_step_active(C0, tau, active_pairs):\n      mats = _build_linearized_mats_active(C0, tau, active_pairs)\n      if mats is None: return None, None\n      A_ub, b_ub, bounds, c = mats\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success: return None, None\n      n = C0.shape[0]\n      x = res.x\n      X = x[:n]; Y = x[n:2*n]; R = x[2*n:]\n      C_new = np.stack([X, Y], axis=1)\n      return C_new, R\n\n  # ---------- Candidate optimizers ----------\n  def candidate_optimize_active(Cinit, K_pairs, max_outer=80):\n      C = Cinit.copy()\n      r0, _ = _solve_radii_zero_slack(C)\n      best_C = C.copy(); best_r = r0.copy();\
    \ best_s = float(np.sum(best_r))\n      tau = 0.06; min_tau = 5e-4; no_improve = 0; patience = 16\n      alphas = [1.0, 0.9, 0.75, 0.6, 0.5, 0.4, 0.3, 0.2, 0.12, 0.08, 0.05]\n      for _ in range(max_outer):\n          active = _select_active_pairs(C, best_r, int(K_pairs))\n          step = _lp_step_active(C, tau, active)\n          if step[0] is None:\n              tau *= 0.6\n              if tau < min_tau: break\n              continue\n          C_lin, _ = step\n          d = C_lin - C\n          improved = False\n          for a in alphas:\n              C_try = np.clip(C + a * d, 0.0, 1.0)\n              r_try, ok = _solve_radii_zero_slack(C_try)\n              if not ok: continue\n              s_try = float(np.sum(r_try))\n              if s_try > best_s + 1e-6:\n                  best_s = s_try; best_C = C_try; best_r = r_try; C = C_try\n                  tau = min(0.12, tau * 1.05); no_improve = 0; improved = True\n                  break\n          if not improved:\n    \
    \          tau *= 0.6; no_improve += 1\n              if tau < min_tau or no_improve >= patience: break\n      best_r = _finalize_zero_tol(best_C, best_r)\n      return best_C, best_r, best_s\n\n  def candidate_optimize_all(Cinit, max_outer=100):\n      if core is None:\n          # fallback to active with K much larger than pairs count\n          return candidate_optimize_active(Cinit, K_pairs=len(PAIRS), max_outer=max_outer)\n      # Use modular baseline (all pairs) from core\n      return core.candidate_optimize(Cinit, max_outer=max_outer, min_tau=5e-4, verbose=False)\n\n  # ---------- Ablation ----------\n  def _score(C):\n      r, ok = _solve_radii_zero_slack(C)\n      return float(np.sum(r)), r, ok\n\n  def run_ksweep(seed_name, C0, Ks, all_baseline=True):\n      best_C = None; best_r = None; best_s = -1.0\n      if all_baseline:\n          C_all, r_all, s_all = candidate_optimize_all(C0, max_outer=100)\n          s0 = float(np.sum(r_all))\n          print(f\"[kswp] {seed_name}\
    \ | K=all       | score {s0:.9f}\")\n          if s0 > best_s: best_s, best_C, best_r = s0, C_all, r_all\n      for K in Ks:\n          Ck, rk, sk = candidate_optimize_active(C0, K_pairs=K, max_outer=80)\n          print(f\"[kswp] {seed_name} | K={K:3d} ({K/N:.2f}N) | score {sk:.9f}\")\n          if sk > best_s: best_s, best_C, best_r = sk, Ck, rk\n      return best_C, best_r, best_s\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      seeds = []\n      Cb = _seed_storage_best()\n      if Cb is not None:\n          seeds.append((\"storage-best\", Cb))\n          Cj = _seed_storage_best_jitter(amp=0.001, seed=9317)\n          if Cj is not None:\n              seeds.append((\"storage-best-jitter-0.001\", Cj))\n      else:\n          seeds.append((\"grid-36minus4\", _fallback_grid()))\n\n      Ks = [N, 2*N, 3*N, 4*N, 5*N, 8*N]\n      best_sum = -1.0; best_C = None; best_r = None\n      print(\"[kswp] Active-constraint K sweep:\")\n      for (name, C0) in seeds:\n          C0 = np.clip(C0, 0.0,\
    \ 1.0)\n          C_opt, r_opt, s_opt = run_ksweep(name, C0, Ks, all_baseline=True)\n          if s_opt > best_sum:\n              best_sum, best_C, best_r = s_opt, C_opt, r_opt\n\n      try:\n          os.makedirs(\"storage/verity\", exist_ok=True)\n          np.save(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\", best_C)\n          np.save(\"storage/verity/best_radii.npy\", best_r)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n\n      return np.array(best_C, dtype=float), np.array(best_r, dtype=float)\n```"
