- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\nRecap: Active-constraint selection ablation (ID 551) shows:\n- storage-best: slack and dual selection both reach 2.932012092.\n- jitter seed: slack reaches 2.932012092; dual selection collapses to 2.917325013.\nConclusion: dual-pressure selection can be unstable from some inits; slack-based selection is robust. Recommend K≥3N with slack selection (per K-sweep), or a hybrid (union of top-K/2 by slack and top-K/2 by duals) as a future test.\n\nPersisting results and logging takeaways.\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/ablation_selection_551.tsv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Active-constraint selection ablation (Eval ID 551, K=3N)\n  # seed,mode,score\n  storage-best,slack,2.932012092\n  storage-best,dual,2.932012092\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,slack,2.932012092\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,dual,2.917325013\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Selection ablation\
    \ @tick 335 (Eval 551): dual pressure vs slack (K=3N)\n  - storage-best: slack = 2.932012092; dual = 2.932012092\n  - jitter seed: slack = 2.932012092; dual drops to 2.917325013\n  Takeaways:\n  - Dual-pressure selection (HiGHS marginals) is not robust from some inits.\n  - Slack-based selection remains stable; with K≥3N (per K-sweep) it matches all-pairs.\n  - Recommended default: slack-based selection K≥3N; optional hybrid (union of top-K/2 by slack + top-K/2 by dual) is a future experiment if we revisit contact gating.\n  Status:\n  - SOTA unchanged: 2.932012092. Code + ablation artifacts persisted in storage/verity.\n  - Next: maintain; prepare concise ablation note post-maturity; retry exact SOCP if CVXPY appears.\n```"
