- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\nRecap: Hybrid active-constraint selection (union of top-K/2 slack + top-K/2 dual) at K=3N matched SOTA on storage-best but underperformed on the jitter seed (2.92999). Combined with prior ablations, the robust default is: zero-slack LP + zero-tolerance finalize; all-pairs or active-set with slack-based selection and K≥3N.\n\nPersisting results and logging takeaways; drafting an ablation note for later Archive submission.\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/ablation_hybrid_554.tsv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Hybrid selection ablation (Eval ID 554, K=3N; union of top-K/2 slack + top-K/2 dual)\n  # seed,score\n  storage-best,2.932012092\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,2.929990851\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/ablation_note_draft.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Zero-slack SCP-LP for Circle Packing (32 in unit square): Ablations and Protocol\n  Verity lineage — Draft (to refine post-maturity)\n\n  ## Summary\n\
    \  - Stable SOTA: 2.932012092 (multiple evals).\n  - Core: Sequential Convex Programming (linearized LP centers) + exact radii LP, both zero-slack, with zero-tolerance finalize (fix only true violations; equality allowed).\n  - Deterministic seeds: storage-best and tiny jitters.\n\n  ## Key Findings\n  1) Slack mode × Finalize policy (Eval 544)\n     - Zero-slack + zero-tolerance: 2.932012092\n     - Zero-slack + tiny-positive (~1e-12): 2.932012092\n     - Robust slacks (1e-9) + zero-tolerance or tiny-positive: 2.932012069–2.932012073\n     => Zero-slack consistently ≥ robust; finalize policy is neutral under zero-slack.\n\n  2) Active-constraint K-sweep (Eval 548)\n     - storage-best: K ∈ {all, 1N..8N} → 2.932012092\n     - jitter seed: K=1N (2.9287), K=2N (2.9311) underperform; K≥3N → 2.932012092\n     => K≈3N suffices to match all-pairs; too-small K misses critical contacts.\n\n  3) Selection rule: dual-pressure vs slack (Eval 551)\n     - storage-best: slack/dual both 2.932012092\n\
    \     - jitter: slack 2.932012092; dual 2.917325013\n     => Dual-pressure selection can be unstable from some inits; slack-based is robust.\n\n  4) Hybrid selection (union top-K/2 slack + top-K/2 dual, K=3N) (Eval 554)\n     - storage-best: 2.932012092\n     - jitter: 2.929990851\n     => Hybrid not consistently robust vs slack-only.\n\n  ## Recommended Protocol\n  - Zero-slack everywhere (centers step and radii LP), with zero-tolerance finalize.\n  - Deterministic seeds: storage-best plus small jitters.\n  - Center step: all-pairs, or active-constraint with slack-based selection and K≥3N.\n  - Persist best config to storage/verity/{best_centers.npy,best_radii.npy}.\n\n  ## Repro Notes\n  - Modular core: storage/verity/scp_lp_core.py\n  - Maintenance loader: storage/verity/runner_loader.py\n  - Ablation artifacts:\n    * storage/verity/ablation_slack_finalize_544.tsv\n    * storage/verity/ablation_k_sweep_548.tsv\n    * storage/verity/ablation_selection_551.tsv\n    * storage/verity/ablation_hybrid_554.tsv\n\
    \n  ## Next Steps (post-maturity)\n  - Prepare concise Archive note with these ablations and protocol.\n  - Optional: attempt exact SOCP if CVXPY becomes available; otherwise maintain.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Hybrid selection ablation @tick 337 (Eval 554):\n  - Hybrid union (top-K/2 slack + top-K/2 dual), K=3N:\n    * storage-best: 2.932012092\n    * jitter seed: 2.929990851 (underperforms)\n  Takeaways:\n  - Reinforces that dual-weighted selection can be brittle; hybrid doesn’t consistently help.\n  - Recommended default: zero-slack + zero-tolerance finalize; center step with all-pairs or slack-based active set with K≥3N.\n  - Draft ablation note written to storage/verity/ablation_note_draft.md for future Archive submission.\n  Status:\n  - SOTA unchanged (2.932012092). Code + artifacts persisted; will maintain and publish after maturity.\n```"
