parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 3/5 — Theme: Canonical HRG LP, acceptance/stopping, and a deterministic, parsimonious protocol\n\nA) Canonical HRG feasibility LP (per attempt)\n\n- Given:\n  - Current feasible (C ∈ R^(N×2), r ∈ R^N), unit square, N=32.\n  - Proposed radius increment Δr ≥ 0 (fixed for the attempt), via a deterministic weight mode w and scalar α: Δr = α · w, with ∑ w_i = 1 (for scale).\n  - Trust region τ > 0 for center displacements.\n\n- Variables (split to keep LP linear):\n  - For each i: δx_i = δx_i^+ − δx_i^−, δy_i = δy_i^+ − δy_i^−, with δx_i^+, δx_i^−, δy_i^+, δy_i^− ≥ 0.\n  - Variable vector v = [δx^+, δx^−, δy^+, δy^−] ∈ R^(4N).\n  - Bounds: 0 ≤ each split variable ≤ τ; this enforces |δx_i| ≤ τ and |δy_i| ≤ τ while the L1 objective discourages both splits turning on simultaneously.\n\n- Objective (parsimonious minimal move):\n  - Minimize ∑_i (δx_i^+ + δx_i^− + δy_i^+ + δy_i^−).\n  - Deterministic tie-break: weight each term by (1 + 1e−9·i) for x and (1 + 2e−9·i) for y\
    \ to make solutions unique and reproducible.\n\n- Constraints in standard A v ≤ b form:\n  1) Pairwise non-overlap (first-order safe). Let d_ij = ||C_i − C_j||, u_ij = (C_i − C_j) / max(d_ij, 1e−16), and g_ij = (r_i + r_j + Δr_i + Δr_j) − d_ij − σ, with tiny σ ≥ 0 (e.g., 1e−12) to counter linearization optimism deterministically.\n     u_ij·(δC_i − δC_j) ≥ g_ij\n     Translate with splits (δx_i = δx_i^+ − δx_i^− etc.) and multiply by −1 to fit ≤:\n     −u_x(δx_i^+ − δx_i^− − δx_j^+ + δx_j^−) − u_y(δy_i^+ − δy_i^− − δy_j^+ + δy_j^−) ≤ −g_ij\n  2) Boundary “tie” constraints for zero-slack feasibility:\n     - Left: r_i + Δr_i ≤ x_i + δx_i ⇒ (δx_i^+ − δx_i^−) ≥ (r_i + Δr_i − x_i)\n       ⇒ (−δx_i^+ + δx_i^−) ≤ x_i − r_i − Δr_i\n     - Right: r_i + Δr_i ≤ 1 − (x_i + δx_i) ⇒ (δx_i^+ − δx_i^−) ≤ 1 − x_i − r_i − Δr_i\n     - Bottom: r_i + Δr_i ≤ y_i + δy_i ⇒ (−δy_i^+ + δy_i^−) ≤ y_i − r_i − Δr_i\n     - Top: r_i + Δr_i ≤ 1 − (y_i + δy_i) ⇒ (δy_i^+ − δy_i^−) ≤ 1 − y_i − r_i − Δr_i\n  3) Keep\
    \ centers in [0,1] (redundant in many cases but included for safety):\n     - x lower: x_i + δx_i ≥ 0 ⇒ (−δx_i^+ + δx_i^−) ≤ x_i\n     - x upper: x_i + δx_i ≤ 1 ⇒ (δx_i^+ − δx_i^−) ≤ 1 − x_i\n     - similarly for y.\n\n- Size/complexity (N=32):\n  - Variables: 4N = 128.\n  - Pairwise rows: N(N−1)/2 = 496.\n  - Boundary rows: 4N = 128.\n  - In-box rows: 2N for x + 2N for y = 128.\n  - Total rows ≈ 752 (small). Deterministic and fast.\n\nB) Deterministic acceptance and schedules\n\n- Weight modes w (deterministic, normalized ∑w=1):\n  - Uniform: w_i = 1.\n  - Boundary-aware: w_i ∝ max(0, min(x_i, 1−x_i, y_i, 1−y_i) − r_i + η), η=1e−9 to break ties.\n  - Contact-aware: w_i ∝ mean_j max(0, d_ij − (r_i + r_j)) + η (average local slack).\n- α schedule (radius growth magnitude): start α0 ∈ {0.002, 0.001}; backtrack list [α0, 0.7α0, 0.5α0, 0.35α0, 0.2α0, 0.12α0, 0.08α0].\n- τ schedule (trust region): [0.06, 0.04, 0.025, 0.015, 0.01, 0.006, 0.004, 0.002].\n- For each α, try τ descending; solve\
    \ LP. If infeasible, shrink τ; if all τ fail, shrink α; if all α fail, switch w mode (e.g., boundary-aware) and retry once.\n- Feasible step evaluation:\n  - Apply C′ = C + δC; compute exact zero-slack radii r′ via full LP; zero-tolerance finalize; accept if ∑r′ ≥ ∑r + ε (ε=1e−6).\n  - If accepted, optionally modestly increase α (α ← min(1.1α, α0)) while resetting τ to the last accepted value to probe local headroom; otherwise continue backtracking.\n\nC) Stopping criteria (anti-grind, integrity)\n\n- Hard caps: total attempts per seed ≤ 80; accepted steps per seed ≤ 12.\n- Early stop if last k accepted gains < ε_gain (e.g., k=5, ε_gain=5e−7).\n- If no acceptance across all (α, τ, w) configurations, report a structured negative result (feasible cone rigid at this resolution).\n\nD) Determinism and logging (insight-first)\n\n- Log each attempt: seed, α, τ, w mode, LP feasibility (Y/N), min pair slack RHS g_ij, L1 move norm, acceptance (Y/N), Δ∑r, contact count, min/mean boundary slack\
    \ changes.\n- Stable tie-breaking via index-based tiny weight offsets; fixed floating tolerances σ, ε.\n- Persist best (centers, radii) and a compact TSV of the HRG trajectory; keep code minimal (one HRG LP builder, one evaluator, one loop).\n\nE) Why this is aligned and not a rehash\n\n- It changes the geometry of the step: feasibility-first with minimal displacement, rather than objective-driven joint steps. If tiny improvements exist along this manifold, HRG provides a principled way to reach them; if not, the negative result is informative about the local rigidity of high-quality packings (an insight, not just a “no”).\n- It remains parsimonious: a single additional LP, backtracking, and exact verification; no non-convex detours or ad hoc randomness.\n\nF) Implementation readiness\n\n- Constraint formulas are fully specified; the LP can be coded in a small helper with matrix assembly from (u_ij, g_ij).\n- Next: choose α0 (likely 0.001) and begin with uniform weights, then boundary-aware\
    \ if needed. Keep σ=1e−12 and ε=1e−6.\n- If HRG fails broadly, run the “room-making first” max–min slack LP variant once per seed to test whether uniform slack creation is feasible; log outcomes and pivot accordingly."
