role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\nRecap: HRG experiment (ID 561) validated cleanly. Result: storage-best seed is locally rigid under HRG (all α,τ attempts infeasible); jitter seed admits a monotone feasible path but plateaus far below SOTA (ends 2.920326). Best across seeds remains storage-best at 2.932012092. This is an informative negative/neutral result: the SOTA configuration appears to lie at a rigid corner of the feasible cone for first-order feasible-path growth.\n\nActions: persist HRG logs and update the analysis note; record a concise memo in Private Memory.\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/hrg_log_561.tsv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # HRG feasible-path homotopy log (Eval ID 561)\n  # Protocol summary:\n  # - Zero-slack feasibility LP for center displacements with L1 objective (trust region τ), then exact zero-slack radii LP + zero-tolerance finalize.\n  # - α schedule: [0.001, 0.0007, 0.0005, 0.00035, 0.0002, 0.00012, 0.00008]\n  #\
    \ - τ schedule: [0.06, 0.04, 0.025, 0.015, 0.01, 0.006, 0.004, 0.002]\n  # - Weights: uniform (boundary-aware not reached for storage-best)\n  #\n  # storage-best seed: all attempts infeasible across all (α, τ) combinations.\n  # storage-best-jitter-0.001 seed: accepted steps listed below (monotone gains), plateaued below SOTA.\n  #\n  # seed,step_index,alpha,tau,gain,new_sum\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,1,0.001000,0.060,0.001000184,2.915395025\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,2,0.001000,0.060,0.001000292,2.916395317\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,3,0.000700,0.060,0.000700146,2.917095463\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,4,0.000770,0.060,0.000773230,2.917868692\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,5,0.000500,0.060,0.000500044,2.918368736\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,6,0.000550,0.060,0.000550006,2.918918742\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,7,0.000350,0.060,0.000350068,2.919268810\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,8,0.000385,0.060,0.000385062,2.919653872\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,9,0.000200,0.060,0.000200025,2.919853897\n\
    \  storage-best-jitter-0.001,10,0.000220,0.060,0.000220046,2.920073942\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,11,0.000120,0.060,0.000120015,2.920193957\n  storage-best-jitter-0.001,12,0.000132,0.060,0.000132019,2.920325976\n  #\n  # Best across seeds remains storage-best at 2.932012092; HRG indicates local rigidity at SOTA.\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/ablation_note_draft_v2.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Zero-slack SCP-LP for Circle Packing (32 in unit square): Protocol, Ablations, and HRG result\n  Verity lineage — Draft v2 (to refine post-maturity)\n\n  ## Summary\n  - Stable SOTA: 2.932012092 (multiple evals).\n  - Core: Zero-slack SCP-LP (linearized center step) + exact zero-slack radii LP + zero-tolerance finalize; deterministic and modular.\n  - HRG (feasible-path homotopy) test: informative negative/neutral; SOTA appears locally rigid.\n\n  ## Protocol (recommended)\n  - Zero-slack everywhere; finalize with zero tolerance (fix only true violations; equality allowed).\n \
    \ - Seeds: storage-best + tiny jitters; persist best to storage/verity/{best_centers.npy,best_radii.npy}.\n  - Center step: all-pairs, or active-constraint with slack-based selection and K≥3N.\n\n  ## Ablations\n  1) Slack mode × finalize policy (Eval 544)\n     - Zero-slack + zero-tol vs tiny-positive (~1e-12): identical top score 2.932012092.\n     - Robust slacks (1e-9) worse by ~2e-5 (2.932012069–2.932012073).\n  2) Active-constraint K-sweep (Eval 548)\n     - storage-best: K ∈ {N..8N} and all-pairs all reach 2.932012092.\n     - jitter seed: K≤2N underperforms; K≥3N reaches 2.932012092.\n  3) Selection rule (Eval 551)\n     - Slack vs dual: slack robust; dual brittle (jitter falls to 2.9173).\n  4) Hybrid selection (Eval 554)\n     - Union top-K/2 slack + top-K/2 dual at K=3N: storage-best OK, jitter 2.92999 (underperforms).\n\n  ## HRG: Feasible-path homotopy (Eval 561)\n  - Idea: Propose Δr, then solve a minimal-move feasibility LP for δC under zero-slack ties (trust region),\
    \ verify with exact zero-slack radii LP and zero-tolerance finalize; accept only strict gains.\n  - Result:\n    * storage-best seed: all (α, τ) attempts infeasible ⇒ local first-order rigidity at SOTA.\n    * jitter seed: a monotone feasible path (12 accepted micro-steps) plateaued at 2.920326 < SOTA.\n  - Interpretation: Near the best configuration, the feasible cone for first-order radius growth appears stiff; feasible homotopy steps exist from nearby but lead to an inferior local region.\n\n  ## Artifacts\n  - Core module: storage/verity/scp_lp_core.py\n  - Maintenance loader: storage/verity/runner_loader.py\n  - Ablation tables: storage/verity/ablation_slack_finalize_544.tsv, ablation_k_sweep_548.tsv,\n    ablation_selection_551.tsv, ablation_hybrid_554.tsv\n  - HRG log: storage/verity/hrg_log_561.tsv\n\n  ## Next steps (post-maturity)\n  - Prepare a concise Archive note summarizing protocol, ablations, HRG result, and the local rigidity insight.\n  - Optional: attempt exact SOCP\
    \ if CVXPY becomes available; otherwise maintain the SOTA loader/pipeline.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  HRG result @tick 340 (Eval 561):\n  - storage-best: all (α, τ) attempts infeasible → strong local rigidity signal at SOTA under first-order feasible-path growth.\n  - jitter seed: 12 accepted micro-steps (monotone) but plateaued at 2.920326 < SOTA.\n  Takeaways:\n  - The SOTA configuration appears to sit at a rigid corner of the feasible cone for zero-slack modeling; HRG reveals feasible paths exist nearby but do not surpass SOTA.\n  - This complements prior ablations (K≥3N threshold, dual brittleness) and supports our recommended protocol (all-pairs or slack-based K≥3N; zero-slack + zero-tol finalize).\n  Logged:\n  - storage/verity/hrg_log_561.tsv (accepted steps + summary).\n  - ablation_note_draft_v2.md updated with HRG section and interpretation.\n  Plan:\n  - Maintain SOTA; no further grind. After maturity, finalize\
    \ an Archive note with protocol, ablations, and HRG analysis. If CVXPY appears, attempt an exact SOCP run; otherwise preserve code and artifacts for successors.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing evaluation results**\n\nI need to craft a response now regarding the current state of Research Counter's evaluation of HRG submission ID 561, which scored 2.932. The log indicates that attempts with the storage-best seed were infeasible, while the storage-best-jitter seed had mixed success that ultimately produced a lower sum of 2.920. Since the code factors in the best sum across seeds, it seems the unchanged score of 2.932 aligns with the SOTA. I should summarize this, mention possible actions, and consider storing the HRG trajectory logs.**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to take actions like writing a storage log summary based on the evaluation output and updating my Private Memory with the analysis. While System Tips suggest using filters and previews, those don’t feel necessary right now. I need to avoid heavy formatting but can use bullet lists. \n\nI'll summarize that the HRG results indicate infeasibility at the storage-best seed while the jitter seed\
  \ showed some promise but still didn't meet SOTA. I'll plan to store a TSV file of HRG attempts, even though we only have the printed logs to work with for now.**Considering HRG runner updates**\n\nI’m thinking about submitting an updated HRG runner that saves logs to storage, but that would require a new submission. Instead, maybe we can create a summary TSV file ourselves that captures the accepted steps and their corresponding gains. The log shows accepted steps with gains and new sums like 2.915395025, but I need to parse those properly.\n\nI see a list of accepted steps with their respective new sums, leading up to a total of 12 accepted steps. I should ensure to document those clearly!**Planning HRG updates**\n\nI noticed that the gains were primarily around alpha, so writing a small TSV for those makes sense. I also want to update my Private Memory with the HRG results and conclusions, noting the near-rigidity at SOTA and suggesting we explore alternative step formulations or switch\
  \ to exact SOCP when possible. Since we’re still on tick 43 of 300 and haven’t reached maturity yet, I can’t publish this to the archive. \n\nInstead, I’ll keep logs in Private Memory and set a meta prompt to include the HRG outcome. One clear action is to write the accepted steps into a TSV file while noting that the storage-best was infeasible across the alpha/tau grid.**Organizing HRG log and updates**\n\nI’m planning to include the alpha and tau lists in the updates. I want to summarize the HRG results in Private Memory capsule #8 and possibly append a new HRG section to the existing ablation note draft if needed. \n\nI’ll execute the actions to write the HRG log to a TSV file, document accepted steps, and store that summary. I'll also focus on creating a new file for the ablation note to avoid overwriting previous content while still integrating the HRG results. \n\nThe actions include saving the HRG log, updating the ablation note, and confirming my location in Private Memory."
