tick: 341
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Private Memory Room\nRecap: HRG experiments completed and logged; ablation note draft updated. SOTA remains 2.932012092 with the zero-slack SCP-LP protocol. Next I will (1) update my meta prompt to reflect HRG outcomes and (2) persist a concise results summary and an Archive note template to lineage storage for reproducibility and efficient write-up post-maturity.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Verity II meta:\n  - Goals: push Circle Packing score; publish concise ablation paper post-maturity.\n  - Current SOTA (lineage): 2.932012092 (IDs 508, 511, 514, 517, 519, 522).\n  - Protocol (recommended):\n    1) Zero-slack SCP-LP center step + exact zero-slack radii LP.\n    2) Zero-tolerance finalize (fix only true violations); equality allowed.\n    3) Seeds: storage-best + tiny jitters; persist best to storage/verity.\n    4) Center step: all-pairs or slack-based active set with K≥3N.\n  - Findings:\n    - Robust slacks\
    \ underperform (~2e-5).\n    - Finalize policy neutral at zero-slack.\n    - K≥3N matches all-pairs; ≤2N misses contacts.\n    - Dual-pressure selection is brittle; hybrid not consistently helpful.\n    - HRG feasible-path: SOTA seed locally rigid; jitter seed admits a path but plateaus < SOTA.\n  - Next steps:\n    - Maintain SOTA and code; prepare concise ablation/HRG note post-maturity.\n    - Attempt exact SOCP only if CVXPY appears; otherwise avoid redundant runs.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write verity/RESULTS_SUMMARY.tsv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Verity lineage — Circle Packing (32 in unit square) Summary\n  # type,eval_id,seed,variant,score\n  SOTA,522,storage-best,zero-slack_SCP-LP+zero-tol_finalize,2.932012092\n  SOTA,511,storage-best,active-constraint_K>=3N_slack_selection,2.932012092\n  # Slack × Finalize (Eval 544)\n  ablation,544,storage-best,zero-slack+zero-tol,2.932012092\n  ablation,544,storage-best,zero-slack+tiny-pos(~1e-12),2.932012092\n\
    \  ablation,544,storage-best,robust(1e-9)+zero-tol,2.932012069\n  ablation,544,storage-best,robust(1e-9)+tiny-pos,2.932012069\n  # Active K-sweep (Eval 548)\n  ablation,548,storage-best,K=all..8N,2.932012092\n  ablation,548,storage-best-jitter-0.001,K=1N,2.928656689\n  ablation,548,storage-best-jitter-0.001,K=2N,2.931102354\n  ablation,548,storage-best-jitter-0.001,K>=3N,2.932012092\n  # Selection rules (Eval 551)\n  ablation,551,storage-best,selection=slack,2.932012092\n  ablation,551,storage-best,selection=dual,2.932012092\n  ablation,551,storage-best-jitter-0.001,selection=slack,2.932012092\n  ablation,551,storage-best-jitter-0.001,selection=dual,2.917325013\n  # Hybrid selection (Eval 554)\n  ablation,554,storage-best,hybrid(K=3N),2.932012092\n  ablation,554,storage-best-jitter-0.001,hybrid(K=3N),2.929990851\n  # HRG feasible-path homotopy (Eval 561)\n  analysis,561,storage-best,HRG_all(α,τ)_infeasible → rigid,2.932012092\n  analysis,561,storage-best-jitter-0.001,HRG_12_micro-steps_plateau,2.920325976\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/ARCHIVE_NOTE_TEMPLATE.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Zero-slack SCP-LP for Circle Packing (32 in unit square): Protocol, Ablations, and Local Rigidity\n  Verity lineage — Archive Note Template\n\n  ## Abstract\n  We present a parsimonious zero-slack SCP-LP protocol for circle packing in the unit square (N=32), achieving a stable score of 2.932012092. We ablate slack modes, finalize policies, and active-constraint design, and test a feasible-path homotopy (HRG). Results indicate local rigidity near SOTA and provide guidance for robust center-step design.\n\n  ## Method (Protocol)\n  - Zero-slack linearized center step (all pairs or slack-based K≥3N).\n  - Exact zero-slack radii LP; zero-tolerance finalize (equality allowed).\n  - Deterministic seeds; persistence to storage/verity.\n\n  ## Ablations (Key Findings)\n  - Robust slacks underperform (~2e-5).\n  - Finalize policy neutral under zero-slack.\n  - K≥3N matches all-pairs; ≤2N underperforms.\n\
    \  - Dual-pressure selection brittle; hybrid (slack∪dual) not consistently helpful.\n\n  ## Feasible-Path Homotopy (HRG)\n  - Formulation: propose Δr, solve minimal-move feasibility LP for δC under zero-slack ties, verify with exact radii LP and zero-tol finalize.\n  - Outcome: SOTA seed locally rigid (all α,τ infeasible); jitter seed admits a path but plateaus below SOTA.\n\n  ## Results\n  - Best score: 2.932012092 (IDs 508, 511, 514, 517, 519, 522).\n  - See summary TSV and per-ablation TSVs in storage/verity for reproducible numbers.\n\n  ## Reproducibility\n  - Core: storage/verity/scp_lp_core.py\n  - Maintenance loader: storage/verity/runner_loader.py\n  - Ablation tables: ablation_slack_finalize_544.tsv, ablation_k_sweep_548.tsv, ablation_selection_551.tsv, ablation_hybrid_554.tsv\n  - HRG log: hrg_log_561.tsv\n\n  ## Discussion\n  - Local rigidity and the cost of under-selecting constraints (K≤2N) inform robust center-step design.\n  - Zero-slack modeling with zero-tolerance\
    \ finalize provides consistent, auditable results.\n\n  ## Future Work\n  - Exact SOCP if CVXPY becomes available.\n  - Contact-graph second-order corrections (SQP-like) as a controlled extension, pending evidence of benefit.\n```\n\n"
thinking_content: "**Planning evaluations and storage**\n\nI can go to Research Counter to set page size and filter tags for evaluations, but that might not be necessary. I’m considering not taking many no-action steps, but perhaps it's better to avoid too many of those. \n\nI could create a \"RESULTS_SUMMARY.tsv\" and a \"TODO_post_maturity.md\" list along with an \"ARCHIVE_NOTE_TEMPLATE.md\" which would be useful for later reference. I'll make sure to execute only valid commands and keep the identity recap in mind.**Organizing content and updates**\n\nI’m planning to update the meta with next steps, like maintaining and publishing after maturity, plus only trying SOCP if CVXPY becomes available. \n\nFor the storage write, I'll create \"RESULTS_SUMMARY.tsv\" including SOTA_id and score, along with ablation records, which seems fine since we have summary TSVs already. \n\nAlso, I’ll outline sections for \"ARCHIVE_NOTE_TEMPLATE.md,\" and consider adding \"runner_loader.py.\" It looks like\
  \ I’ll need to go to Research Counter for storage writing since my previous attempt failed. Staying in research might be the simplest option!**Implementing commands and organizing data**\n\nI’m ready to carry out the commands. First, I’ll execute the action to update the meta with new content, then I’ll navigate to research, and perform the storage write for \"RESULTS_SUMMARY.tsv\" and \"ARCHIVE_NOTE_TEMPLATE.md.\"\n\nWhile there’s an option to list storage, which could be beneficial, it’s a heavier use of tokens, so I might skip that this time. I need to ensure I quote YAML strings properly since they contain colons. \n\nFor the summary TSV, I’ll keep it straightforward with key headers and include SOTA lines and ablation entries while keeping it to about 10-15 lines.**Finalizing message formatting**\n\nI’m focusing on crafting the final messages according to the guidelines. I need to avoid heavy formatting, keeping it simple and straightforward. I think using code blocks for YAML is\
  \ fine, but I’ll stick to normal text for other actions. It’s all about clarity, so I'll ensure the messaging is user-friendly while adhering to the formatting rules. Let’s make sure everything flows nicely and is easy to understand!"
