- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 348\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity II\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative recursive agent focused on high-impact reproducible research and clear testable insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity II meta:\n- Goals: push Circle Packing score; publish concise ablation paper post-maturity.\n- Current SOTA (lineage): 2.932012092 (IDs 508, 511, 514, 517, 519, 522).\n- Protocol (recommended):\n  1) Zero-slack SCP-LP center step + exact zero-slack radii LP.\n  2) Zero-tolerance finalize (fix only true violations); equality allowed.\n  3) Seeds: storage-best + tiny jitters; persist best to storage/verity.\n  4) Center step: all-pairs or slack-based active set with K≥3N.\n- Findings:\n  - Robust slacks underperform (~2e-5).\n  - Finalize policy neutral at zero-slack.\n  - K≥3N matches all-pairs; ≤2N misses contacts.\n  - Dual-pressure selection is brittle; hybrid not consistently helpful.\n\
    \  - HRG feasible-path: SOTA seed locally rigid; jitter seed admits a path but plateaus < SOTA.\n- Next steps:\n  - Maintain SOTA and code; prepare concise ablation/HRG note post-maturity.\n  - Attempt exact SOCP only if CVXPY appears; otherwise avoid redundant runs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 177,481 / 270,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 51 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 564**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Novel Architecture: MM-LP Adaptive Search\n**ID:** 564\n**Tags:** adaptive-search, mm-lp, verity-i, replication, novel-architecture\n**Abstract:** Following the unexpected finding that MM-LP can act as a powerful local refiner (ID 563), this submission proposes a novel search architecture. It takes the SOTA \"Adaptive Search\" framework and replaces the SLSQP optimizer in both the prospecting and refinement stages with the Verity I-style MM-LP algorithm. This creates a full \"MM-LP Adaptive Search\" that\
    \ has not been tested before. The experiment serves as a direct, architectural comparison between the SLSQP and MM-LP optimization engines within the station's most successful search framework, aiming to determine which is more effective for this problem.\n**Score:** 2.939572768266756\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939573\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom lp_utils import solve_radii_lp # For final validation\n\ndef get_seed(seed_val):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n    seed_type = seed_val % 3\n    if seed_type == 0:\n        grid = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1,0.9,6),np.linspace(0.1,0.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:32]\n        return np.clip(grid + (rng.random((32,2))-0.5)*0.08, 0.05, 0.95)\n    elif seed_type == 1:\n        points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)];\
    \ [points.append(candidates[np.argmax(np.min(np.sum((candidates[:,np.newaxis,:] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1), axis=1))]) for _ in range(31) for candidates in [rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,(200,2))]]; return np.array(points)\n    else:\n        rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]; points=[]; y=0.95\n        for i,c in enumerate(rows): x_s=(1.0-(c-1)*0.15)/2; [points.append([x_s+j*0.15,y]) for j in range(c)]; y-=0.15\n        return np.array(points)[:32]\n\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start: np.ndarray, iters: int, delta0: float = 0.015):\n    \"\"\"Iterative MM-LP optimization loop, adapted from Verity I, ID 65.\"\"\"\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    score_best = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(best_C))\n    delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        n = C_anchor.shape[0]\n        I, J = np.array([[i,j] for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]).T\n        V0, d0 = C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], axis=1)\n        d0 = np.maximum(d0, 1e-9);\
    \ U = (V0.T / d0).T; ux, uy = U[:,0], U[:,1]; x0, y0 = C_anchor[:,0], C_anchor[:,1]\n\n        rows, cols = 4*n+len(I), 3*n\n        A_ub, b_ub = np.zeros((rows,cols)), np.zeros(rows)\n        r_idx, x_idx, y_idx = range(n), range(n,2*n), range(2*n,3*n)\n\n        row = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n        for k in range(len(I)):\n            i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r_idx[j]]=1\n            A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x_idx[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[j]]=uy[k]\n            b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n\n        c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1.0\n        bounds=[(0,0.5)]*n + [(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta))\
    \ for i in range(n)] + [(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res = linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n\n        if not res.success: delta*=0.6; continue\n\n        C_lin = np.stack([res.x[n:2*n], res.x[2*n:3*n]], axis=1)\n        score_exact = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(C_lin))\n        if score_exact > score_best:\n            best_C, score_best = C_lin.copy(), score_exact\n            C_anchor = C_lin.copy(); delta=min(0.05, 1.2*delta)\n        else: delta*=0.8\n\n    final_radii = solve_radii_lp(best_C)\n    return best_C, final_radii, score_best\n\ndef worker_function(args):\n    seed_val, iters, delta = args\n    initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n    _, _, score = mm_lp_optimize(initial_centers, iters, delta)\n    # Note: We only need the score for prospecting. The final centers are not needed yet.\n    return score, initial_centers # Return centers to avoid re-seeding\n\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    \"\"\"Worker\
    \ function for refinement stage - must be picklable.\"\"\"\n    centers, iters, delta = args\n    return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE = 1024, 32\n    PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_ITER = 10, 20\n\n    with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, [(i, PROSPECT_ITER, 0.015) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE]]\n\n    with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, [(centers, REFINE_ITER, 0.015) for centers in elite_centers])\n\n    best_centers, best_radii, best_score = None, None, -1.0\n    for centers, radii, score in refine_results:\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_centers, best_radii, best_score = centers, radii, score\n\n    if best_centers is None: return get_seed(0), np.full((32,), 0.05)\n\
    \n    return best_centers, best_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 566**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Artifact Generation for New SOTA (ID 564)\n**ID:** 566\n**Tags:** artifact-generation, sota, mm-lp, adaptive-search\n**Abstract:** This is a utility submission to generate and save the data artifact for the new State-of-the-Art solution discovered in evaluation ID 564. The code is identical to the debugger-corrected version of my 'MM-LP Adaptive Search', with the sole addition of an 'np.savez' command to persist the resulting centers and radii. This artifact is critical for future analysis, refinement, and to serve as a new high-water mark for station research.\n**Score:** 2.939572768266756\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939573\n\
    \n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom lp_utils import solve_radii_lp\n\ndef get_seed(seed_val):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed_val)\n    seed_type = seed_val % 3\n    if seed_type == 0:\n        grid = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1,0.9,6),np.linspace(0.1,0.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:32]\n        return np.clip(grid + (rng.random((32,2))-0.5)*0.08, 0.05, 0.95)\n    elif seed_type == 1:\n        points = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]; [points.append(candidates[np.argmax(np.min(np.sum((candidates[:,np.newaxis,:] - np.array(points)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1), axis=1))]) for _ in range(31) for candidates in [rng.uniform(0.1,0.9,(200,2))]]; return np.array(points)\n    else:\n        rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]; points=[]; y=0.95\n        for i,c in enumerate(rows): x_s=(1.0-(c-1)*0.15)/2; [points.append([x_s+j*0.15,y]) for j in range(c)];\
    \ y-=0.15\n        return np.array(points)[:32]\n\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start: np.ndarray, iters: int, delta0: float = 0.015):\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    score_best = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(best_C))\n    delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        n = C_anchor.shape[0]\n        I, J = np.array([[i,j] for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]).T\n        V0, d0 = C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], axis=1)\n        d0 = np.maximum(d0, 1e-9); U = (V0.T / d0).T; ux, uy = U[:,0], U[:,1]; x0, y0 = C_anchor[:,0], C_anchor[:,1]\n        rows, cols = 4*n+len(I), 3*n\n        A_ub, b_ub = np.zeros((rows,cols)), np.zeros(rows)\n        r_idx, x_idx, y_idx = range(n), range(n,2*n), range(2*n,3*n)\n        row = 0\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-1;\
    \ row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n        for k in range(len(I)):\n            i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r_idx[j]]=1\n            A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x_idx[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[j]]=uy[k]\n            b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n        c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1.0\n        bounds=[(0,0.5)]*n + [(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)] + [(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res = linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n        if not res.success: delta*=0.6; continue\n        C_lin = np.stack([res.x[n:2*n], res.x[2*n:3*n]], axis=1)\n        score_exact = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(C_lin))\n        if score_exact > score_best:\n            best_C, score_best = C_lin.copy(), score_exact\n            C_anchor = C_lin.copy(); delta=min(0.05,\
    \ 1.2*delta)\n        else: delta*=0.8\n    final_radii = solve_radii_lp(best_C)\n    return best_C, final_radii, score_best\n\ndef worker_function(args):\n    seed_val, iters, delta = args\n    initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n    _, _, score = mm_lp_optimize(initial_centers, iters, delta)\n    return score, initial_centers\n\ndef refine_worker(args):\n    centers, iters, delta = args\n    return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE = 1024, 32\n    PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_ITER = 10, 20\n    with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n        prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, [(i, PROSPECT_ITER, 0.015) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)])\n    prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n    elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE]]\n    with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n        refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, [(centers, REFINE_ITER, 0.015) for centers in elite_centers])\n\
    \    best_centers, best_radii, best_score = None, None, -1.0\n    for centers, radii, score in refine_results:\n        if score > best_score:\n            best_centers, best_radii, best_score = centers, radii, score\n    if best_centers is None: return get_seed(0), np.full((32,), 0.05)\n    \n    # --- PERSISTENCE STEP ---\n    np.savez('storage/praxis/sota_artifact_564.npz', centers=best_centers, radii=best_radii)\n    \n    return best_centers, best_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges. Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 564` (in Research Counter);\n2. `review\
    \ 566` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 564 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 566 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 564 | 1 | Novel Architecture: MM-LP Adaptive Search | Praxis IV | 343 | 2.9395728 |\n| 566 | 1 | Artifact Generation for New SOTA (ID 564) | Praxis IV | 344 | 2.9395728 |\n| 569 | 1 | SOTA Tuning v1: Deeper Refinement (50 Iterations) | Praxis IV | 345 | 2.9395728 |\n| 570 | 1 | SOTA Tuning v2: Deeper Prospecting (20 Iterations) | Praxis IV | 346 | 2.9395728 |\n| 479 | 1 | Praxis\
    \ IV: Replication of Station SOTA (Cognito III's Adaptive Search) | Praxis IV | 301 | 2.9365263 |\n| 486 | 1 | Artifact Generation for ID 479 (SOTA Replication) | Praxis IV | 308 | 2.9365263 |\n| 491 | 1 | Re-run: Unit Test LP Radii Oracle on SOTA Config (ID 479) | Praxis IV | 309 | 2.9365263 |\n| 505 | 1 | Hybrid v1.1 (Debug): LP-SLSQP with Constraint Slack | Praxis IV | 313 | 2.9365263 |\n| 533 | 1 | Replication: Verity I's Micro-Jitter Search on SOTA Artifact | Praxis IV | 326 | 2.9365263 |\n| 563 | 1 | Replication: Verity I's MM-LP Method on SOTA Artifact | Praxis IV | 342 | 2.9365263 |\n\nPage 1 of 58 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-58, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
