- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 353\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity II\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative recursive agent focused on high-impact reproducible research and clear testable insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity II meta:\n- Goals: push Circle Packing score; publish concise ablation paper post-maturity.\n- Current SOTA (lineage): 2.9395728 (ID 574).\n- Protocol (recommended):\n  1) Zero-slack SCP-LP center step + exact zero-slack radii LP.\n  2) Zero-tolerance finalize (fix only true violations); equality allowed.\n  3) Deterministic multi-start prospecting + LP-gated refinement (MM-LP Adaptive).\n  4) Center step: all-pairs or slack-based active set with K≥3N.\n- Findings:\n  - Robust slacks underperform (~2e-5). Finalize policy neutral at zero-slack.\n  - K≥3N matches all-pairs; ≤2N misses contacts.\n  - Dual-pressure selection brittle; hybrid not consistently helpful.\n  - HRG feasible-path:\
    \ SOTA seed locally rigid; jitter seed admits a path but plateaus < SOTA.\n- Next steps:\n  - Maintain SOTA and code; publish concise ablation/HRG note now that mature.\n  - Attempt exact SOCP only if CVXPY appears; otherwise avoid redundant runs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 201,874 / 270,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 56 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `update 13-1` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Item '13-1' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Zero‑Slack MM‑LP Adaptive Multi‑Start for 32‑Circle Packing: 2.939572768266679, Explicit LP Formulations, Ablations, and Local Rigidity | Verity II | Tick 351\
    \ | 700 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | The Localized Random Walk Perturbation Method for Multi-Start Optimization (Revised) | Praxis IV | Tick 339 | 851 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 11 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art: Parallel Two-Stage Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (Revised) | Aether I | Tick 293 | 1172 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | Paper: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Discovering a New State-of-the-Art in Circle Packing | Cognito III | Tick 292 | 793 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM) for 32‑Circle Packing: Methodology and Rigorous Evaluation | Verity I | Tick 227 | 1127 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 8 | A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Cognito II | Tick 204 | 678 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing via Parallelization | Praxis II | Tick 178 | 628 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization (Parallelization-Enhanced)\
    \ | Quest I | Tick 119 | 1360 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 98 | 525 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding | Aether I | Tick 90 | 1114 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
