parts:
- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Archive Room\nRecap: MMS‑LP v2 matched SOTA at full precision (ID 597 = 2.9395727712062967) and fixes the finalize bug from v1. I’ll append a concise, self-contained addendum to my Archive capsule (#13) integrating these results and the exact failure details.\n\n/execute_action{reply 13}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: MMS‑LP center reorganization + iterative zero‑tolerance finalize — results and integration\"\ncontent: |\n  Summary\n  - We add a max‑min‑slack LP (MMS‑LP) center reorganization step and report full‑precision results.\n  - MMS‑LP maximizes the minimum linearized slack s across all pairwise and boundary constraints by moving centers within a trust region (no radii variables), then recomputes radii via the exact zero‑slack radii LP and applies a strict finalize.\n  - v1 had a finalize bug (one‑pass repair); v2 replaces it with a multi‑pass iterate‑until‑fixed finalize (tiny per‑violation fudge) that guarantees non‑overlap\
    \ within numerical precision.\n\n  Method (concise)\n  - MMS‑LP LP (variables X, Y, scalar s):\n      maximize s\n      subject to, for all pairs (i<j) with unit u_ij at anchor C:\n        u_ij·(c_i − c_j) − (r_i + r_j) ≥ s\n      boundary ties:\n        x_i − r_i ≥ s, 1 − x_i − r_i ≥ s, y_i − r_i ≥ s, 1 − y_i − r_i ≥ s\n      trust region: X ∈ [x^0±τ]∩[0,1], Y ∈ [y^0±τ]∩[0,1]\n    After solving, evaluate exact zero‑slack radii LP at C+δC and accept only if ∑r improves.\n\n  Results (full precision)\n  - ID 594 (MMS‑LP v1): FAILED verification due to micro‑overlap. Example offending pair:\n      dist = 0.20536791355349712\n      r1+r2 = 0.20536791355349715\n    Root cause: one‑pass finalize left a tiny positive violation.\n  - ID 597 (MMS‑LP v2): 2.9395727712062967\n    Valid configuration; min pairwise margin reported ~ 0.0 (equalities allowed).\n\n  Comparison to main SOTA in paper\n  - ID 574 (Zero‑slack MM‑LP Adaptive Multi‑start): 2.939572768266679\n  - ID 597 (MMS‑LP v2): 2.9395727712062967\n\
    \    Interpretation: MMS‑LP matches SOTA within ~3e‑12; no consistent improvement detected.\n\n  Integration guidance\n  - Use MMS‑LP as an optional “feasible‑region relaxer” before SCP‑LP refinement:\n      τ0 ≈ 0.03 with adaptive scaling; rounds ≈ 25; accept only if ∑r increases by >1e‑9.\n      If s (LP’s min slack) < 1e‑6, back off τ or skip.\n  - Keep the iterative finalize even for non‑MMS paths near equality‑tight solutions.\n\n  Repro and artifacts (lineage storage)\n  - Code: storage/verity/mms_lp.py\n    Functions: solve_radii_lp_zero_slack, finalize_zero_tol_iter, mms_step, run_mms_lp\n  - Log: storage/verity/evals_mms.tsv\n    594: FAILED (micro‑overlap); 597: 2.9395727712062967\n\n  Takeaway\n  - MMS‑LP provides a principled, deterministic reorganization step that can enlarge feasible slack cones but did not surpass our SOTA. Future gains likely require non‑local moves (e.g., LRW) or second‑order constrained steps (ASN/SOCP) beyond the current LP linearization.\n```"
