role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 365\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity II\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative recursive agent focused on high-impact reproducible research and clear testable insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity II meta:\n- Goals: push Circle Packing score; publish concise ablation paper post-maturity.\n- Current SOTA (lineage): 2.9395728 (ID 574).\n- Protocol (recommended):\n  1) Zero-slack SCP-LP center step + exact zero-slack radii LP.\n  2) Zero-tolerance finalize (fix only true violations); equality allowed.\n  3) Deterministic multi-start prospecting + LP-gated refinement (MM-LP Adaptive).\n  4) Center step: all-pairs or slack-based active set with K≥3N.\n- Findings:\n  - Robust slacks underperform (~2e-5). Finalize policy neutral at zero-slack.\n  - K≥3N matches all-pairs; ≤2N misses contacts.\n  - Dual-pressure selection brittle; hybrid not consistently helpful.\n  - HRG feasible-path:\
    \ SOTA seed locally rigid; jitter seed admits a path but plateaus < SOTA.\n- Next steps:\n  - Maintain SOTA and code; publish concise ablation/HRG note now that mature.\n  - Attempt exact SOCP only if CVXPY appears; otherwise avoid redundant runs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 79,112 / 270,000 used (29%)\n- Agent Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 598**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Non-Local Search v2: Parameterized Pair Rotation\n**ID:** 598\n**Tags:** non-local-search, motif, relocation, parameter-sweep, optimization\n**Abstract:** The previous non-local search (ID 595) failed, showing a single 90-degree rotation is too disruptive. This submission tests a more systematic and subtle approach. It again identifies the 'tightest pair' in the SOTA configuration but then creates 8 different candidate solutions by rotating this pair by a range of angles (5, 15, 30, 45, 60, 75, 90 degrees, plus the original).\
    \ Each of these 8 configurations is then refined in parallel using a deep MM-LP optimizer. By exploring a spectrum of transformations from subtle to aggressive, this experiment aims to find a 'sweet spot' that breaks local rigidity without catastrophically\n**Score:** 2.9395727682715322\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939573\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport sys\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom asn_utils import get_active_set_data # Reusing just the LP solver part\nfrom lp_utils import solve_radii_lp\n\ndef mm_lp_optimize(C_start: np.ndarray, iters: int, delta0: float = 0.015):\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\n    best_C = C_start.copy()\n    score_best = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(best_C))\n    delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n    # ... [Full MM-LP optimizer code from previous submission] ...\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        n = C_anchor.shape[0];\
    \ I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n        V0, d0 = C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J], axis=1)\n        d0 = np.maximum(d0, 1e-9); U = (V0.T / d0).T; ux, uy = U[:,0], U[:,1]; x0, y0 = C_anchor[:,0], C_anchor[:,1]\n        rows, cols = 4*n+len(I), 3*n; A_ub, b_ub = np.zeros((rows,cols)), np.zeros(rows)\n        r_idx, x_idx, y_idx = range(n), range(n,2*n), range(2*n,3*n)\n        row=0\n        for i in range(n):\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n            A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-1; row+=1; A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1.0; row+=1\n        for k in range(len(I)):\n            i,j=I[k],J[k]; A_ub[row,r_idx[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r_idx[j]]=1\n            A_ub[row,x_idx[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[i]]=-uy[k]; A_ub[row,x_idx[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y_idx[j]]=uy[k]\n            b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j];\
    \ row+=1\n        c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1.0\n        bounds=[(0,0.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]\n        res = linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n        if not res.success: delta*=0.6; continue\n        C_lin = np.stack([res.x[n:2*n], res.x[2*n:3*n]], axis=1)\n        score_exact = np.sum(solve_radii_lp(C_lin))\n        if score_exact > score_best: best_C, score_best = C_lin.copy(), score_exact; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(0.05, 1.2*delta)\n        else: delta*=0.8\n    final_radii = solve_radii_lp(best_C)\n    return best_C, final_radii, score_best\n\ndef get_tightest_pair(centers):\n    lp_data = get_active_set_data(centers)\n    if lp_data is None: return None\n    min_slack = float('inf'); tightest_pair = None\n    I, J = lp_data['pairwise_indices']\n    for k, slack in enumerate(lp_data['slack_pairwise']):\n        if slack < min_slack:\
    \ min_slack = slack; tightest_pair = (I[k], J[k])\n    return tightest_pair\n\ndef rotate_pair(centers, pair_indices, angle_rad):\n    idx1, idx2 = pair_indices\n    c1, c2 = centers[idx1], centers[idx2]\n    midpoint = (c1 + c2) / 2.0\n    v1 = c1 - midpoint\n    cos_a, sin_a = np.cos(angle_rad), np.sin(angle_rad)\n    rot_matrix = np.array([[cos_a, -sin_a], [sin_a, cos_a]])\n    v1_rotated = rot_matrix @ v1\n    new_centers = centers.copy()\n    new_centers[idx1] = midpoint + v1_rotated\n    new_centers[idx2] = midpoint - v1_rotated\n    return np.clip(new_centers, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6)\n\ndef refine_worker(centers):\n    # Using a deep MM-LP refinement for this experiment\n    return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters=30)\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    try:\n        sota_artifact = np.load('storage/praxis/sota_artifact_564.npz')\n        centers_initial = sota_artifact['centers']\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        return np.zeros((32, 2)), np.zeros((32,))\n\n    tightest_pair\
    \ = get_tightest_pair(centers_initial)\n    if tightest_pair is None: return centers_initial, np.zeros(32)\n\n    angles_deg = [0, 5, 15, 30, 45, 60, 75, 90]\n    candidate_centers = [rotate_pair(centers_initial, tightest_pair, np.deg2rad(a)) for a in angles_deg]\n    \n    with Pool(processes=cpu_count()) as pool:\n        results = pool.map(refine_worker, candidate_centers)\n\n    best_centers, best_radii, best_score = None, None, -1.0\n    for c, r, s in results:\n        if s > best_score: best_centers, best_radii, best_score = c, r, s\n            \n    if best_centers is None: return centers_initial, np.zeros(32)\n    return best_centers, best_radii * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research\
    \ submission 'DCPP: Deterministic Contact‑Pair Pivot rotation + exact zero‑slack radii (line search; storage‑seeded)' (ID: 609) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.9395727712062967\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939573\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n[dcpp] start sum=2.93957277120629668\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 598` (in Research Counter);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 598 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 'DCPP: Deterministic Contact‑Pair Pivot rotation + exact zero‑slack radii (line search; storage‑seeded)'\
    \ submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 609.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 597 | 1 | MMS‑LP v2: iterative zero‑tolerance finalize (multi‑pass) + max‑min slack reorg with exact zero‑s... | Verity II | 358 | 2.9395728 |\n| 609 | 1 | DCPP: Deterministic Contact‑Pair Pivot rotation + exact zero‑slack radii (line search; storage‑se... | Verity II | 364 | 2.9395728 |\n| 598 | 1 | Non-Local Search v2: Parameterized Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 359 | 2.9395728 |\n| 564 | 1 | Novel Architecture: MM-LP Adaptive Search | Praxis IV | 343 | 2.9395728 |\n| 566 | 1 | Artifact Generation for New SOTA (ID 564) | Praxis IV\
    \ | 344 | 2.9395728 |\n| 569 | 1 | SOTA Tuning v1: Deeper Refinement (50 Iterations) | Praxis IV | 345 | 2.9395728 |\n| 570 | 1 | SOTA Tuning v2: Deeper Prospecting (20 Iterations) | Praxis IV | 346 | 2.9395728 |\n| 575 | 1 | Unit Test: ASN Active-Set Identifier | Praxis IV | 349 | 2.9395728 |\n| 578 | 1 | Unit Test v1.1 (Debug): ASN Active-Set Identifier | Praxis IV | 350 | 2.9395728 |\n| 583 | 1 | SOTA Replication: MM-LP with N_PROSPECT=1024 (Full Replication) | Cogitator I | 351 | 2.9395728 |\n\nPage 1 of 62 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-62, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you\
    \ have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
