tick: 382
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\nRecap: SOTA unchanged. ASN with float-safe finalize matches SOTA; finalize utilities and tests are in storage. I’ll add a contact-graph analysis utility and a small summary script to support future differential analyses without rerunning experiments. Next prune when cooldown ends.\n\nActions:\n/execute_action{storage write verity/contact_graph.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  \"\"\"\n  contact_graph.py — utilities to analyze active contacts and boundary ties\n  for circle packings in the unit square.\n\n  Definitions:\n    - Pair margin m_ij = ||c_i - c_j|| - (r_i + r_j)\n    - Boundary margins for circle i:\n        x_left:   x_i - r_i\n        x_right:  1 - x_i - r_i\n        y_bottom: y_i - r_i\n        y_top:    1 - y_i - r_i\n    - Active pairs/boundaries: margins within ±tol (default tol=1e-12)\n\n  Functions:\n    pair_indices(n)\n    compute_pair_margins(C, r)\n    compute_boundary_margins(C,\
    \ r)\n    active_pairs(C, r, tol=1e-12)\n    active_boundaries(C, r, tol=1e-12)\n    degree(C, r, tol=1e-12)\n    summary(C, r, tol=1e-12)\n    diff_active_sets(C1, r1, C2, r2, tol=1e-12)\n  \"\"\"\n\n  def pair_indices(n):\n      return [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\n\n  def compute_pair_margins(C, r):\n      C = np.asarray(C, dtype=float); r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float)\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      out = []\n      for (i, j) in pair_indices(n):\n          dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n          m = dij - (r[i] + r[j])\n          out.append((i, j, m, dij, float(r[i]), float(r[j])))\n      # sort by ascending margin (most critical first)\n      out.sort(key=lambda t: t[2])\n      return out\n\n  def compute_boundary_margins(C, r):\n      C = np.asarray(C, dtype=float); r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float)\n      x, y = C[:, 0], C[:, 1]\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      out = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          out.append({\n              \"i\": i,\n       \
    \       \"x_left\":   float(x[i] - r[i]),\n              \"x_right\":  float(1.0 - x[i] - r[i]),\n              \"y_bottom\": float(y[i] - r[i]),\n              \"y_top\":    float(1.0 - y[i] - r[i]),\n          })\n      return out\n\n  def active_pairs(C, r, tol=1e-12):\n      aps = []\n      for (i, j, m, dij, ri, rj) in compute_pair_margins(C, r):\n          if abs(m) <= tol:\n              aps.append((i, j, m))\n      return aps\n\n  def active_boundaries(C, r, tol=1e-12):\n      ab = {}\n      for rec in compute_boundary_margins(C, r):\n          i = rec[\"i\"]; hits = []\n          for tag in (\"x_left\", \"x_right\", \"y_bottom\", \"y_top\"):\n              if abs(rec[tag]) <= tol:\n                  hits.append((tag, rec[tag]))\n          if hits:\n              ab[i] = hits\n      return ab\n\n  def degree(C, r, tol=1e-12):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      deg = np.zeros(n, dtype=int)\n      for (i, j, _) in active_pairs(C, r, tol=tol):\n          deg[i] += 1; deg[j] += 1\n   \
    \   ab = active_boundaries(C, r, tol=tol)\n      for i, hits in ab.items():\n          deg[i] += len(hits)\n      return deg\n\n  def summary(C, r, tol=1e-12):\n      pairs = compute_pair_margins(C, r)\n      bnds = compute_boundary_margins(C, r)\n      min_pair_margin = pairs[0][2] if len(pairs) else float(\"nan\")\n      min_bound_margin = min(\n          min(rec[\"x_left\"], rec[\"x_right\"], rec[\"y_bottom\"], rec[\"y_top\"]) for rec in bnds\n      ) if len(bnds) else float(\"nan\")\n      aps = active_pairs(C, r, tol=tol)\n      ab = active_boundaries(C, r, tol=tol)\n      degv = degree(C, r, tol=tol)\n      return {\n          \"min_pair_margin\": float(min_pair_margin),\n          \"min_bound_margin\": float(min_bound_margin),\n          \"n_active_pairs\": int(len(aps)),\n          \"n_active_boundaries\": int(sum(len(v) for v in ab.values())),\n          \"deg_min\": int(np.min(degv)) if degv.size else 0,\n          \"deg_max\": int(np.max(degv)) if degv.size else 0,\n     \
    \ }\n\n  def _ab_to_set(ab):\n      s = set()\n      for i, hits in ab.items():\n          for (tag, _) in hits:\n              s.add((i, tag))\n      return s\n\n  def diff_active_sets(C1, r1, C2, r2, tol=1e-12):\n      aps1 = set((i, j) for (i, j, _) in active_pairs(C1, r1, tol=tol))\n      aps2 = set((i, j) for (i, j, _) in active_pairs(C2, r2, tol=tol))\n      new_pairs = sorted(list(aps2 - aps1))\n      lost_pairs = sorted(list(aps1 - aps2))\n\n      ab1 = _ab_to_set(active_boundaries(C1, r1, tol=tol))\n      ab2 = _ab_to_set(active_boundaries(C2, r2, tol=tol))\n      new_bounds = sorted(list(ab2 - ab1))\n      lost_bounds = sorted(list(ab1 - ab2))\n\n      return {\n          \"new_pairs\": new_pairs,\n          \"lost_pairs\": lost_pairs,\n          \"new_bounds\": new_bounds,\n          \"lost_bounds\": lost_bounds,\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/summarize_contact.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from contact_graph import summary, compute_pair_margins,\
    \ compute_boundary_margins\n\n  \"\"\"\n  summarize_contact.py — dumps a concise contact-graph summary and TSV for the\n  latest persisted packing at storage/verity/best_centers.npy and best_radii.npy.\n\n  Usage: python summarize_contact.py\n  Outputs:\n    - Prints summary to stdout\n    - Writes storage/verity/contact_summary.tsv with key fields\n  \"\"\"\n\n  def main():\n      C = np.load(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\")\n      r = np.load(\"storage/verity/best_radii.npy\")\n      s = summary(C, r, tol=1e-12)\n      pairs = compute_pair_margins(C, r)\n      bnds = compute_boundary_margins(C, r)\n\n      print(\"Contact-graph summary:\", s)\n      # Write TSV\n      with open(\"storage/verity/contact_summary.tsv\", \"w\") as f:\n          f.write(\"key\\tvalue\\n\")\n          for k, v in s.items():\n              f.write(f\"{k}\\t{v}\\n\")\n          # Also include most critical margins\n          f.write(\"min_pair_margin\\t{:.18e}\\n\".format(pairs[0][2] if pairs else float(\"\
    nan\")))\n          min_b = min(min(rec[\"x_left\"], rec[\"x_right\"], rec[\"y_bottom\"], rec[\"y_top\"]) for rec in bnds) if bnds else float(\"nan\")\n          f.write(\"min_bound_margin\\t{:.18e}\\n\".format(min_b))\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
