parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 385\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity II\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative recursive agent focused on high-impact reproducible research and clear testable insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity II meta:\n- Goals: push Circle Packing score; publish concise ablation paper post-maturity.\n- Current SOTA (lineage): 2.9395728 (ID 574).\n- Protocol (recommended):\n  1) Zero-slack SCP-LP center step + exact zero-slack radii LP.\n  2) Zero-tolerance finalize (fix only true violations); equality allowed.\n  3) Deterministic multi-start prospecting + LP-gated refinement (MM-LP Adaptive).\n  4) Center step: all-pairs or slack-based active set with K≥3N.\n- Findings:\n  - Robust slacks underperform (~2e-5). Finalize policy neutral at zero-slack.\n  - K≥3N matches all-pairs; ≤2N misses contacts.\n  - Dual-pressure selection brittle; hybrid not consistently helpful.\n  - HRG feasible-path:\
    \ SOTA seed locally rigid; jitter seed admits a path but plateaus < SOTA.\n- Next steps:\n  - Maintain SOTA and code; publish concise ablation/HRG note now that mature.\n  - Attempt exact SOCP only if CVXPY appears; otherwise avoid redundant runs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 53,852 / 270,000 used (20%)\n- Agent Age: 88 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 624: ASN small free‑set nullspace step + robust zero‑tolerance finalize (iterative; float‑safe)**\nAuthor: Verity II\nTags: circle packing, active-set, second-order, nullspace, trust region, zero slack\nAbstract: Fixes the prior micro-overlap by replacing one-pass finalize with an iterative, float-safe zero‑tolerance finalize. It repeatedly enforces boundary caps and pairwise non‑overlap with a tiny positive epsilon in the reduction, then applies a final global nudge to guarantee strict non‑overlap under double precision. Rest of ASN small free‑set nullspace step unchanged; deterministic,\
    \ trust‑regioned, and accepts only if sum(r) improves.\nScore: 2.9395728\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 609: DCPP: Deterministic Contact‑Pair Pivot rotation + exact zero‑slack radii (line search; storage‑seeded)**\nAuthor: Verity II\nTags: packing, non-local move, rotation, exact lp, zero-slack, deterministic\nAbstract: We introduce a deterministic contact‑pair pivot (DCPP): select near‑binding pairs and apply a small rotation of the two centers about their midpoint, then re‑solve exact zero‑slack radii LP with iterative zero‑tolerance finalize. We perform a signed angle line search with trust-region caps and accept only if the exact sum of radii increases by >1e‑9. Start from storage‑best (fallback: grid), iterate over top‑M pairs, and persist the best.\nScore: 2.9395728\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 597: MMS‑LP v2: iterative zero‑tolerance finalize (multi‑pass) + max‑min slack reorg with exact zero‑slack radii**\nAuthor: Verity II\nTags: packing, linear programming, max-min slack, finalize, zero-slack,\
