tick: 393
role: model
parts:
- text: "Sharpening implementation details, numerics, and a deterministic pilot pipeline with bisection/grids and tiny KKT solvers.\n\nCommon primitives\n- Near-contact graph G:\n  - Pair slack s_ij = ||c_i − c_j|| − (r_i + r_j); boundary slacks s_iL = x_i − r_i, s_iR = 1 − x_i − r_i, etc.\n  - Thresholds: κ_large = 3e−3, κ_mid = 1e−3, κ_small = 3e−4; ε_num = 1e−12.\n  - Unit normals n_ij = (c_i − c_j)/max(||c_i − c_j||, 1e−15). Boundary normals are ±e_x or ±e_y.\n- Trust region and boxes:\n  - τ grid: {0.03, 0.02, 0.01}, clip in ∞-norm; enforce boxes after applying Δ (clamp to [0,1]).\n- Gating and acceptance:\n  - After any ΔC, run exact zero-slack radii LP + iterative zero-tolerance finalize; accept if ΔΣr ≥ 1e−9 and min slack ≥ 0; else backtrack τ or abort.\n- Linear algebra:\n  - Equality-constrained ridge LS (KKT): solve [H Eᵀ; E 0] [v; λ] = [b; 0] with H = (AᵀA + αI). Cholesky with 1e−12 jitter; deterministic pivoting.\n  - Nullspace: QR on Eᵀ to get basis Z; then LS in reduced space\
    \ (ZᵀHZ)w = Zᵀb, Δ = Zw.\n\nIdea 3 — Cycle surgery QP via equality-constrained ridge LS with γ grid\n- Variables: v = [θ, t_x, t_y, α_1..α_m] for a cycle S of m nodes (4≤m≤7).\n- Motion map for node i ∈ S:\n  - Δc_i(v) = θ R_perp (c_i − c̄) + t + α_i n_i^out, with R_perp = [[0, −1],[1, 0]], c̄ = centroid of S.\n  - n_i^out: outward unit vector estimated as the normalized sum of normals toward neighbors u ∉ S with s_iu ≤ κ_large, plus boundary normals if near boundary; fall back to radial from c̄ if degenerate.\n- Internal equalities E_eq Δ(v) = 0:\n  - For each internal edge (i,j) in S (s_ij ≤ κ_mid): n_ij·(Δc_i − Δc_j) = 0.\n- External push inequalities linearized into LS target:\n  - For each (i,u) with u ∉ S and s_iu ≤ κ_large: desire n_iu·Δc_i ≥ γ.\n  - Build A_ext v = predicted pushes, target b_ext = γ·1.\n- Ridge LS with equality constraints:\n  - For a fixed γ, minimize ||A_ext v − b_ext||² + α||v||² subject to E_eq Δ(v) = 0. Choose α≈1e−6 to regularize small modes.\n  - Solve\
    \ via KKT or nullspace. Then compute Δc_i(v) and clip by τ.\n  - Check box violations; if violated, reduce τ and re-solve or reduce γ.\n- Discrete γ and θ grids:\n  - θ ∈ {−0.01, 0, +0.01} rad; γ ∈ {1.5e−3, 1.0e−3, 6e−4, 3e−4, 1e−4}.\n  - For each (θ, γ), solve LS→apply Δ on S→gate. Deterministic order of cycles: canonical lexicographic tuple, capped to first M=30 highest “cycle weight” (sum of 1/(s_ij+ε) on cycle edges).\n- Complexity: m≤7 → |v|≤(3 + 7) = 10 vars; KKT ≤ 10 + eqs (≤m) → O(10³) flops per try; safe.\n\nIdea 2 — Min-cut free-set Newton as equality-preserving outward push\n- Free-set F selection:\n  - Build weighted graph on circles (+ boundary nodes). Weights w_ij = 1/(s_ij+ε) for s_ij ≤ κ_large; boundary weights similarly.\n  - Greedy min-cut to size k∈{8,10,12}: start from argmax weighted degree; iteratively add the node that yields the largest cut-weight drop; enforce connectivity by including nearest neighbor if disconnection occurs; ties by index.\n- Variables: ΔC_F\
    \ ∈ R^(2k).\n- Equalities (tangency preservation inside F∪∂F):\n  - For edges (i,j) where i,j ∈ F or j in neighbor set ∂F with s_ij ≤ κ_mid: n_ij·(Δc_i − Δc_j) = 0; for boundary contacts of i ∈ F, use ±Δx_i = 0 or ±Δy_i = 0 accordingly.\n- Outward push to outside:\n  - For each (i,u) with i ∈ F, u ∉ F, s_iu ≤ κ_large: n_iu·Δc_i ≈ ≥ γ; collect rows in A_out.\n- Equality-constrained ridge LS with γ grid:\n  - For fixed γ ∈ {1e−3, 6e−4, 3e−4, 1e−4}, minimize ||A_out Δ − γ·1||² + α||Δ||² subject to E_eq Δ = 0; α≈1e−6.\n  - Compute Δ, clip by τ; apply only on F; gate. If reject, try smaller γ or smaller τ, then next F.\n- Complexity: 2k ≤ 24 vars; eq rows ≤ O(k + neighbors), manageable; deterministic.\n\nIdea 1 — Augmented-Lagrangian (ALM) / block-splitting with exact radii LP\n- Active set A_k: choose ≤5N smallest s_ij and all boundary contacts with s≤κ_mid.\n- Residual model at iterate k:\n  - Pair residuals r_ij(Δ) = max(0, r_i + r_j − n_ij·(Δc_i − Δc_j) − d_ij^0_lin), where d_ij^0_lin\
    \ is the linearized distance term relative to C^k; boundary residuals analogous and linear.\n- Center LS step:\n  - Form J from gradients of active residuals (only those with positive residuals at Δ=0); form u as those residuals at Δ=0.\n  - Solve (JᵀJ + λI) Δ = Jᵀu, clip by τ; re-evaluate residuals; optionally one Gauss-Newton relinearization within the same iteration if residual drop < 10%.\n- Radii/z update (optional split):\n  - r-update: exact zero-slack LP with caps equal to current g_ij(C) (linearized distances); z-update is trivial in linearized model (z ← g(C)).\n- Schedules: κ: 3e−3→1e−3→3e−4; τ: 0.03→0.02→0.01; λ: 1e−2→1e−3→1e−4; iterations ≤ 8.\n- Gate each accepted center move by exact LP + finalize; otherwise backtrack τ; early stop on 3 consecutive rejects at τ=0.01.\n\nDeterministic pilot pipeline (20-minute cap)\n- Seeds: storage-best and a tiny jitter (±8e−4, RNG fixed 2027).\n- Attempt budget: ≤40 total (per seed: ≤20).\n- Order per seed:\n  1) Cycle surgery on top\
    \ M=30 cycles, parameters (θ grid × γ grid) with τ grid outside loop; accept on first gain.\n  2) Min-cut free-set Newton with k=8,10,12 and γ grid; accept on first gain.\n  3) ALM: ≤6 iterations with schedules; accept if any step yields ΔΣr ≥ 1e−9.\n- Logging to TSV: move_type, seed_id, params (k, |S|, θ, γ, τ, λ), predicted target (γ), realized ΔΣr, min_slack_post, time_ms, accepted flag.\n- Persistence: save new best to storage/verity/best_* and append to evals_nonlocal.tsv.\n\nSafety/robustness notes\n- Normal recomputation: recompute n_ij after any accepted move; for pairs with dij < 1e−15, drop the edge from constraints to avoid instabilities.\n- Box proximity: if any center is within <1e−8 of the boundary, avoid pushing further outward along that boundary in equalities (set those equality rows carefully).\n- Equality selection: prefer only edges with s ≤ κ_mid for equalities; others belong to inequality LS target to avoid overconstraining.\n- Tie-breaking: sort edges/cycles/free-sets\
    \ lexicographically; fixed cycle ranking by summed inv-slack; fixed free-set size order (8→10→12); fixed θ grid order (−, 0, +).\n\nExpected outcomes\n- If the jam is due to a tightly knit motif, cycle surgery may produce micro-gains by coordinated outward motion that local pair pivots missed.\n- Min-cut free-set Newton can decompress a dense cluster by solving a slightly larger block while respecting tangencies.\n- ALM provides a smooth alternative that can accumulate small consistent motions; keep iterations few to stay within budget.\n\nIf no gains: publish negative-result note addendum with tables (attempt counts, ΔΣr histograms, min slack before/after), and archive the pipeline for future second-order attempts."
