parts:
- text: "Implementation blueprint, numerics, and runtime plan to ship a deterministic pilot (Cycle surgery first; then Min‑cut ASN; ALM last if time permits)\n\nA) Cycle surgery (pilot to implement first)\n- Data structures\n  - G = near-contact graph at thresholds κ_large=3e−3, κ_mid=1e−3, κ_small=3e−4.\n  - For each node i, cache neighbors N_out(i) = {u ∉ S | s_iu ≤ κ_large} and boundary flags with slacks.\n- Cycle enumeration (cap M=20)\n  - BFS up to length 7 over G with edges s≤κ_mid; canonicalize cycles by lexicographic tuple of node ids, rotated so smallest id first; keep unique; rank by cycle_weight = Σ_(edges on cycle) 1/(s_ij+ε).\n- Outward normals and motion map\n  - n_i^out = normalize(Σ_{u∉S, s_iu≤κ_large} n_iu + boundary normals if i near a boundary). If ||·||<1e−12, use radial from c̄ (cycle centroid).\n  - Δc_i(v) = θ R_perp (c_i−c̄) + t + α_i n_i^out, v = [θ, t_x, t_y, α_1..α_m], m=|S|.\n- Constraints\n  - Internal equalities: for each (i,j) on cycle with s_ij≤κ_mid, n_ij·(Δc_i−Δc_j)\
    \ = 0. Build E v = 0 (E ∈ R^{p×(3+m)}).\n  - External pushes: for each (i,u) with u∉S, s_iu≤κ_large, row a_iu v = n_iu·Δc_i(v). Stack A v ≈ γ·1.\n- Solve equality‑constrained ridge LS with γ grid\n  - For γ ∈ {1.5e−3, 1e−3, 6e−4, 3e−4, 1e−4}, solve min ||A v − γ·1||² + α||v||² s.t. E v = 0. α=1e−6.\n  - KKT: [H Eᵀ; E 0][v; λ] = [Aᵀ(γ·1); 0], with H=AᵀA+αI. Cholesky with 1e−12 jitter; failover to nullspace solve if E nearly rank‑deficient.\n  - Apply Δc_i(v), clip ||Δ||∞≤τ (τ ∈ {0.03,0.02,0.01}, outer loop), clamp to [0,1].\n  - Gate: exact zero‑slack radii LP + iterative zero‑tol finalize; accept on ΔΣr≥1e−9 and no violations; otherwise try next smaller γ or τ, then next cycle.\n- Deterministic attempt ordering and limits\n  - For each seed (storage‑best, then fixed tiny jitter ±8e−4), τ from large→small; cycles in ranked order; for each cycle: θ ∈ {−0.01, 0, +0.01}, then γ grid.\n  - Global cap: ≤26 attempts (e.g., ~13 per seed). Early stop after 5 consecutive rejects at τ=0.01.\n\n\
    B) Min‑cut free‑set ASN (second in pipeline)\n- Free‑set selection F (k ∈ {8,10,12})\n  - Graph on circles + boundary nodes; edge weights w_ij=1/(s_ij+ε) for s_ij≤κ_large; similar for boundary edges. Greedy min‑cut to fixed size: start with argmax weighted degree; iteratively add node that maximally reduces cut; ensure connectivity; tiebreak by id.\n- Motion variables ΔC_F ∈ R^{2k}.\n- Equalities: for edges within F or to ∂F with s≤κ_mid, preserve tangency: n_ij·(Δc_i−Δc_j)=0; for boundary contacts, ±Δx_i=0 or ±Δy_i=0.\n- Outward push: for edges (i,u) with i∈F,u∉F and s_iu≤κ_large, enforce n_iu·Δc_i ≈ γ (LS target).\n- Solve min ||A_out Δ − γ·1||² + α||Δ||² s.t. E_eq Δ=0 with α=1e−6; τ grid and γ grid {1e−3,…,1e−4}. Clip, gate, accept on ΔΣr≥1e−9.\n\nC) ALM/ADMM (third, light probe only)\n- Active rows: ≤5N smallest pair slacks + boundary rows s≤κ_mid.\n- Build hinge LS (positive residuals only): (JᵀJ+λI)Δ=Jᵀu with λ schedule {1e−2→1e−4}, τ grid {0.03,0.02,0.01}, κ schedule {3e−3→3e−4}.\
    \ 1–2 GN relinearizations max. Gate each step.\n\nNumerics and robustness\n- Scaling: row‑normalize A and J to unit 2‑norm; rescale solutions back; improves conditioning.\n- Rank checks: if E is rank‑deficient, drop the weakest equality (largest leverage score) deterministically and retry; bound number of drops to ≤2.\n- Boundary guards: if x_i or y_i within <1e−8 to boundary, disallow outward motion toward that boundary in equalities (remove row) to avoid infeasible pushes.\n- Nullspace sanity: compute dim(null(E)) before solving; if zero, skip candidate (no DOF).\n- Post‑solve verification: compute min external push achieved (min_i n_iu·Δc_i) vs target γ; log both; lack‑of‑fit indicates over‑ambitious γ or τ.\n\nRuntime and logging budget (20‑minute cap)\n- Each attempt triggers one exact LP + finalize (fast under HiGHS; ~milliseconds), plus tiny KKT solve and graph ops (microseconds to milliseconds).\n- With cap 26 attempts total, expected runtime << 20 min.\n- TSV log schema:\n \
    \ - move_type, seed, tau, cycle_id/k, m_or_k, theta, gamma, alpha_ridge, eq_rows, out_rows, min_push_pred, min_push_achieved, dsumr, min_slack_post, accepted, time_ms.\n- Print concise per‑attempt summary to STDOUT; persist full TSV in storage/verity/evals_nonlocal.tsv; persist new best to storage/verity/best_* on acceptance.\n\nUnit tests and validation\n- Synthetic micro‑tests (no LP):\n  - Geometry consistency: for a toy 4‑cycle square, with constructed n_i^out, E v = 0 solution should keep internal distances invariant to first order (check |n_ij·(Δc_i−Δc_j)| < 1e−12).\n  - Nullspace rank tests: E with m=4..7 must yield dim(null)≥1; if not, equality selection is too strict.\n- End‑to‑end dry‑run:\n  - On storage‑best, run one cycle with θ=0, γ=3e−4, τ=0.02; verify gate passes feasibility; measure dsumr (likely ≤0); ensure graceful reject and continuation.\n- Determinism test:\n  - Re-run cycle enumeration and one KKT solve; assert identical v and Δ within 1e−12.\n\nAblation plan (if\
    \ no improvement)\n- Compare three knobs that affect feasibility vs gain:\n  - Cycle size m (4–7), γ grid choices, τ grid schedule.\n  - Free‑set size k (8/10/12) and κ_cut.\n  - ALM κ schedule presence vs single‑stage.\n- Report attempt counts, acceptance rates, min_push_achieved distribution, and ΔΣr histogram; conclude on futility or promising niches.\n\nRisk checklist and mitigations\n- Overconstrained equalities → rank‑deficient: detect and drop weakest rows deterministically.\n- Over‑ambitious γ causes clipping by τ → small realized push: record ratio achieved/target; auto‑decrease γ next.\n- Boundary clipping breaks equalities: reduce τ or adjust equality set by removing boundary‑tied rows.\n- Time creep: hard attempt cap and early‑stop after 5 consecutive rejects at smallest τ.\n\nExit criteria\n- Any accepted move with ΔΣr ≥ 1e−9 → persist, log, and publish short Archive addendum (method + numbers).\n- No accepted moves within budget → publish negative‑result addendum with diagnostics;\
    \ keep pilot code modular for future second‑order work."
