tick: 393
role: model
parts:
- text: "Final reflection tick: concrete pilot spec, pseudo-code, and success criteria for a deterministic non-local, second-order move (Cycle Surgery first; Min-cut Free-set Newton second; ALM as a capped probe)\n\nWhy Cycle Surgery first\n- Minimal code footprint: a tiny equality-constrained ridge LS per candidate with 10–12 variables.\n- Directly targets short loops in the near-contact graph, which our audit shows are prevalent (degree histogram peaks near 5–6; 74 near-contacts at ≤1e-12).\n- Naturally enforces internal-tangency equalities while pushing coherently outward on external contacts.\n\nProblem data and thresholds (fixed, deterministic)\n- Near-contact thresholds: κ_large=3e−3 (external push set), κ_mid=1e−3 (internal equality set).\n- Trust region grid: τ ∈ {0.03, 0.02, 0.01}.\n- Rotation grid: θ ∈ {−0.01, 0, +0.01} rad.\n- Push target grid: γ ∈ {1.5e−3, 1e−3, 6e−4, 3e−4, 1e−4}.\n- Ridge α=1e−6; KKT jitter 1e−12.\n- Acceptance: ΔΣr ≥ 1e−9 after exact zero-slack radii LP + iterative\
    \ zero-tolerance finalize; no violations.\n\nCycle Surgery: mathematical core\n- Variables v = [θ, t_x, t_y, α_1..α_m] for cycle S (nodes i=1..m, 4≤m≤7).\n- Motion map for node i:\n  Δc_i(v) = θ R_perp (c_i − c̄) + t + α_i n_i^out, with R_perp = [[0,−1],[1,0]], c̄ centroid of S.\n  n_i^out: normalized sum of normals to neighbors u∉S with s_iu ≤ κ_large plus boundary normals if near boundary; fallback to radial from c̄ if norm < 1e−12.\n- Internal equalities (preserve cycle tangencies, first order):\n  For each edge (i,j) on S with s_ij ≤ κ_mid: n_ij·(Δc_i − Δc_j) = 0, where n_ij = unit(c_i − c_j).\n- External pushes (desired):\n  For each (i,u) with u∉S and s_iu ≤ κ_large: n_iu·Δc_i(v) ≈ γ.\n- Solve equality-constrained ridge LS for fixed (θ,γ):\n  Let A_ext v be predicted pushes; b_ext = γ·1. Let E_eq v = 0 be internal equalities (each row linear in v because Δc_i is linear in v for fixed θ).\n  Minimize ||A_ext v − b_ext||² + α||v||² subject to E_eq v = 0.\n  KKT system: [H Eᵀ; E 0][v;\
    \ λ] = [Aᵀ b_ext; 0], H = AᵀA + αI.\n  Solve with Cholesky (+1e−12 jitter); if rank issues, drop the weakest equality (deterministic leverage/tie-break) up to 2 rows. Check dim(null(E)) ≥ 1 before solving.\n\nDeterministic attempt ordering and limits\n- Seeds: storage-best, then a fixed tiny jitter (±8e−4, RNG=2027).\n- τ outer loop: 0.03 → 0.02 → 0.01.\n- Enumerate cycles:\n  - Build near-contact graph using s_ij ≤ κ_mid.\n  - BFS cycles up to length 7; canonicalize (smallest node first) and deduplicate; rank by Σ 1/(s_ij+ε).\n  - Cap to first M=20 cycles.\n- For each cycle in rank order:\n  - For θ in {−0.01, 0, +0.01}:\n    - For γ in {1.5e−3, 1e−3, 6e−4, 3e−4, 1e−4}:\n      - Solve LS, form ΔC, clip ||Δ||∞ ≤ τ, clamp to [0,1].\n      - Gate by exact zero-slack radii LP + iterative zero-tol finalize; accept on ΔΣr ≥ 1e−9; break out on first acceptance.\n- Global caps: ≤26 attempts across both seeds; early-stop after 5 consecutive rejects at τ=0.01.\n\nNumerical safety\n- Row-normalize\
    \ A_ext before forming H; rescale solution back.\n- Recompute normals on accepted moves only; for candidates use anchor normals at current seed state.\n- Boundary guards: if a node is within <1e−8 of a boundary, exclude outward boundary normal from n_i^out and remove boundary equalities that would force outward motion.\n- Sanity check: if E_eq is full rank (no DOF), skip the cycle.\n\nMin-cut Free-set Newton (backup if cycle surgery yields no acceptance)\n- Select F (k ∈ {8,10,12}) via greedy min-cut:\n  - Start at node with max weighted degree (w_ij=1/(s_ij+ε), s≤κ_large). Add nodes that maximally reduce cut; ensure connectivity; deterministic ties.\n- Equalities: preserve tangencies within F and to ∂F for edges with s≤κ_mid.\n- Outward LS target: for edges (i∈F, u∉F) with s≤κ_large, n_iu·Δc_i ≈ γ (γ grid as above).\n- Solve equality-constrained ridge LS in ΔC_F ∈ R^(2k), clip by τ, gate, accept.\n\nALM/ADMM (brief probe, only if budget remains)\n- Active set ≤5N smallest slack edges\
    \ + boundary rows s≤κ_mid.\n- Hinge-LS step: (JᵀJ+λI)Δ=Jᵀu for positive residuals; τ grid; 1–2 relinearizations; gate.\n\nPilot pseudo-code skeleton (for run.py core, high level)\n\n- load storage-best C,r (fallback grid if missing)\n- define helper: exact_radii_LP(C) + iterative_zero_tol_finalize → r, sum_r\n- define build_graph(C,r), cycle_enumerate(G), build_mats_cycle(S, θ, γ), solve_kkt(H,E,Aᵀb)\n- best = (C,r,sum_r)\n- for seed in [C, jitter(C)]:\n    for tau in [0.03,0.02,0.01]:\n        cycles = top_cycles(seed)\n        for S in cycles:\n            for theta in [-0.01, 0.0, +0.01]:\n                for gamma in [1.5e−3, 1e−3, 6e−4, 3e−4, 1e−4]:\n                    v = solve_cycle_LS(S, theta, gamma, tau)\n                    C_try = clip(seed + ΔC(v), tau)\n                    r_try, sum_try = exact_radii_LP + finalize(C_try)\n                    if sum_try > best.sum + 1e−9:\n                        best = (C_try, r_try, sum_try); persist; print logs; return best\n      \
    \              record reject log; maybe decrease gamma or continue\n        if attempts at tau=0.01 ≥ 5 rejects: break\n- if not improved: optionally run min-cut free-set Newton for a few candidates; same gate logic; accept on first gain; otherwise return best unchanged\n\nSuccess criteria and interpretation\n- Primary: any accepted move with ΔΣr ≥ 1e−9 under the strict gate. Even a single acceptance demonstrates that a coordinated, equality-preserving non-local step can escape the jam our local methods could not.\n- Secondary (negative-result value): if no gains under tight budgets, we provide a rigorous diagnosis of futility for short-cycle surgery and small free-set decompression at these scales/thresholds; publish a concise addendum with full logs (attempt counts, min_push achieved vs target, ΔΣr histogram, equality rank stats).\n\nRisks and mitigations\n- Overconstraining equalities (rank deficiency) → deterministic row-dropping with leverage scoring, skip if nullspace is empty.\n\
    - Clipping by τ destroys predicted pushes → log achieved/target push ratio; back off γ deterministically.\n- Boundary clamping breaks equalities → guard by removing boundary-driven equalities and normals in n_i^out; prefer outward from cycle centroid if in doubt.\n- Runtime creep → hard caps and early-stop; small matrices ensure each attempt remains microseconds–milliseconds, LP gate dominates but is still fast.\n\nDeliverables for the pilot\n- Core module(s): cycle_surgery.py (build mats, KKT, solve), free_set_newton.py (optional), integrate with existing finalize and LP solvers.\n- Logging: evals_nonlocal.tsv; STDOUT per-attempt summaries; storage snapshots for accepted best.\n- Archive addendum: method definition, parameter grids, acceptance rule, and full-precision results (accepted move or negative-result tables).\n\nExpectation\n- Given the strongly jammed audit (min pair slack ~4.16e−16; 74 near-contacts), improvements may be rare. However, a deterministic, equality-preserving\
    \ non-local move targets a qualitatively different path than prior LP-gated local steps; even a small accepted ΔΣr would be meaningful. If none, the high-quality negative result narrows the search space and justifies moving to truly global reorganizers (e.g., exact SOCP) when tools become available."
