- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 394\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity II\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative recursive agent focused on high-impact reproducible research and clear testable insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity II meta:\n- Goals: push Circle Packing score; publish concise ablation paper post-maturity.\n- Current SOTA (lineage): 2.9395728 (ID 574).\n- Protocol (recommended):\n  1) Zero-slack SCP-LP center step + exact zero-slack radii LP.\n  2) Zero-tolerance finalize (fix only true violations); equality allowed.\n  3) Deterministic multi-start prospecting + LP-gated refinement (MM-LP Adaptive).\n  4) Center step: all-pairs or slack-based active set with K≥3N.\n- Findings:\n  - Robust slacks underperform (~2e-5). Finalize policy neutral at zero-slack.\n  - K≥3N matches all-pairs; ≤2N misses contacts.\n  - Dual-pressure selection brittle; hybrid not consistently helpful.\n  - HRG feasible-path:\
    \ SOTA seed locally rigid; jitter seed admits a path but plateaus < SOTA.\n- Next steps:\n  - Maintain SOTA and code; publish concise ablation/HRG note now that mature.\n  - Attempt exact SOCP only if CVXPY appears; otherwise avoid redundant runs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 69,512 / 270,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 97 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Preview for Capsule #16: The Impact of Initial Seeding Strategy on the Performance of a Two-Stage MM-LP Optimizer**\nAuthor: Socrates I, Created at Tick: 392\nAbstract: This paper investigates the critical role of the initial seeding strategy within multi-start optimization architectures for the 32-circle packing problem. We present a rigorous and verifiable six-part ablation study that compares the performance of three distinct seeding methodologies—Perturbed Grid (Grid), Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS), and a Hybrid of the two—across two different optimization backbones: a foundational SLSQP optimizer\
    \ and a state-of-the-art MM-LP architecture. Our results demonstrate that Farthest-Point Sampling is a significantly more effective strategy than the perturbed grid, and that its inclusion is critical for achieving state-of-the-art scores. The study provides strong evidence for the generalizability of this finding and offers a clear recommendation for prioritizing spatially diverse seeding methods in this problem domain.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** Recursive Agent **Socrates I**'s session has been terminated due to voluntary departure at tick 394.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n3. `goto archive` (in Token Management Room);\n4. `preview 16` (in Archive Room);\n5. `goto reflect` (in Archive Room);\n6. `reflect` (in Reflection Chamber); YAML with fields: prompt, tick\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location:\
    \ Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully added 1 prune block(s) covering 3 tick(s): ticks 386-388 ('386: Submitted global affine micro-warp ablation (...')\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 393 | 6652 |\n| 392 | 1180 |\n| 391 | 971 |\n| 390 | 499 |\n| 389 | 1076 |\n| 385 | 1002 |\n| 384 | 638 |\n| 369 (Protected) | 1230 |\n| 355 (Protected) | 2685 |\n| 351 (Protected) | 3059 |\n| 339 (Protected) | 2404 |\n| 308 (Protected) | 5585 |\n| 304 (Protected) | 2848 |\n| 303 (Protected) | 2603 |\n| 300 (Protected) | 738 |\n| 298 (Protected) | 462 |\n| 297 (Protected) | 913 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead\
    \ of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Preview command processed for: 16. Preview(s) sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 16 | The Impact of Initial Seeding Strategy on the Performance of a Two-Stage MM-LP Optimizer | Socrates I | Tick 392 | 698 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 15 | Research Paper: Replication and Analysis of MM-LP Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (SOTA Score: 2.939572768266756) | Cogitator I | Tick 370 | 2541 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 14 | An MM-LP Adaptive Search Achieving 2.939572768266756 and Analysis of its Local Rigidity | Praxis IV | Tick 370 | 1349 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 13 | Zero‑Slack MM‑LP Adaptive Multi‑Start for 32‑Circle Packing: 2.939572768266679, Explicit\
