    \ scale=1.000 dsum=-1.924609470203e-04\n  [cycle] seed=storage-best tau=0.030 cyc_len=7 A=14 E=7 gamma=1.5000e-03 scale=1.000 dsum=-2.042060682666e-03\n  [cycle] seed=storage-best tau=0.030 cyc_len=7 A=14 E=7 gamma=1.0000e-03 scale=1.000 dsum=-1.361702611759e-03\n  [cycle] seed=storage-best tau=0.030 cyc_len=7 A=14 E=7 gamma=6.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-8.171792940326e-04\n  [cycle] seed=storage-best tau=0.030 cyc_len=7 A=14 E=7 gamma=3.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-4.086487630923e-04\n  [cycle] seed=storage-best tau=0.030 cyc_len=7 A=14 E=7 gamma=1.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-1.362293862632e-04\n  [cycle] seed=storage-best tau=0.030 cyc_len=7 A=16 E=7 gamma=1.5000e-03 scale=1.000 dsum=-2.515034265723e-03\n  [cycle] seed=storage-best tau=0.030 cyc_len=7 A=16 E=7 gamma=1.0000e-03 scale=1.000 dsum=-1.677182104130e-03\n  [cycle] seed=storage-best tau=0.030 cyc_len=7 A=16 E=7 gamma=6.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-1.006545451899e-03\n  [cycle] seed=storage-best tau=0.030 cyc_len=7 A=16 E=7 gamma=3.0000e-04\
    \ scale=1.000 dsum=-5.033612224663e-04\n  [cycle] seed=storage-best tau=0.030 cyc_len=7 A=16 E=7 gamma=1.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-1.678067282183e-04\n  [return] No accepted cycle surgery move. Returning baseline sum=2.939572771206304225.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update: Cycle Surgery (non‑local equality‑preserving QP) — v1 micro‑overlap fix and negative result\n\n  Summary:\n  - v1 failed verification due to a microscopic overlap from float equality (pair dist − (r1+r2) ≈ −2e−17). Fixed by strict‑safe finalize: pair repair enforces r_i + r_j ≤ d_ij − 5e−16 with a final strict pass and a tiny global nudge (1e−16).\n  - v2 (Eval 643) ran deterministically on short cycles (len=7 in top ranked set), τ=0.03, γ∈{1.5e−3,…,1e−4}. All attempts decreased ∑r; no acceptance. Baseline returned safely at full precision 2.939572771206304225.\n\n  Notes:\n  - Logs persisted: storage/verity/evals_cycle_643.tsv (verbatim STDOUT lines\
    \ including A/E rows, γ, τ, dsum).\n  - Interpretation: equality‑preserving outward pushes on short near‑contact cycles do not find productive directions at this SOTA configuration; supports strong local rigidity.\n  - Next: Keep code modular. If we pursue non‑locals again, we’ll try the min‑cut free‑set Newton variant with smaller τ, γ grids and tighter equality selection; otherwise remain in maintenance pending a leaderboard change or new solver availability (e.g., CVXPY for exact SOCP).\n```"
