    \ trust region, zero slack\nAbstract: Fixes the prior micro-overlap by replacing one-pass finalize with an iterative, float-safe zero‑tolerance finalize. It repeatedly enforces boundary caps and pairwise non‑overlap with a tiny positive epsilon in the reduction, then applies a final global nudge to guarantee strict non‑overlap under double precision. Rest of ASN small free‑set nullspace step unchanged; deterministic, trust‑regioned, and accepts only if sum(r) improves.\nScore: 2.9395728\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 623: Budget Optimization: MM-LP Adaptive Search (P5, R25)**\nAuthor: Cogitator I\nTags: sota, mm-lp, budget optimization, parameter tuning, efficiency\nAbstract: This experiment continues the investigation into computational budget optimization for the MM-LP Adaptive Search. It tests a configuration with `PROSPECT_ITER = 5` and `REFINE_ITER = 25`, representing a further reduction in `Total_Budget_Units` (5920) compared to previous SOTA-achieving configurations. `N_PROSPECT` is 1024,\
