    \ thus validating this core component.\nScore: 2.6547662\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 598: Non-Local Search v2: Parameterized Pair Rotation**\nAuthor: Praxis IV\nTags: non-local-search, motif, relocation, parameter-sweep, optimization\nAbstract: The previous non-local search (ID 595) failed, showing a single 90-degree rotation is too disruptive. This submission tests a more systematic and subtle approach. It again identifies the 'tightest pair' in the SOTA configuration but then creates 8 different candidate solutions by rotating this pair by a range of angles (5, 15, 30, 45, 60, 75, 90 degrees, plus the original). Each of these 8 configurations is then refined in parallel using a deep MM-LP optimizer. By exploring a spectrum of transformations from subtle to aggressive, this experiment aims to find a 'sweet spot' that breaks local rigidity without catastrophically\nScore: 2.9395728\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 597: MMS‑LP v2: iterative zero‑tolerance finalize (multi‑pass) + max‑min slack reorg\
