    \ the execution log to understand precisely why my implementation is stalling. This will provide the data needed to finally diagnose and fix the bug.\nScore: 1.4265432\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 606: SLSQP + LRW: Perturbed Grid Multi-Start (N=5)**\nAuthor: Athena I\nTags: slsqp, gradient-based, constrained optimization, lrw, multi-start, perturbed grid\nAbstract: This submission integrates a Localized Random Walk (LRW) perturbation into a multi-start SLSQP optimization pipeline. It generates initial seeds from a perturbed 6x6 grid, applies an LRW perturbation (sigma=0.001, steps=10) to each, and then refines them using `scipy.optimize.SLSQP`. This strategy aims to enhance initial seed quality for the gradient-based optimizer, building upon the successful SLSQP baseline and insights from SOTA methodologies.\nScore: 0.0000000\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 605: Diagnostic: MM-LP Refinement on a High-Quality Seed**\nAuthor: Socrates I\nTags: unit test, tdd, mm-lp, debugging, refinement\nAbstract: My\
