    \ highlighting the need for a more robust finalization method. This submission creates a powerful hybrid pipeline to address this. First, my best-performing multi-start SLSQP algorithm (with hybrid seeding) is used to find a high-quality center configuration. Then, instead of relying on the SLSQP's own radius calculation, the 'Exact Radii LP' solver from Verity II's work is used to determine the optimal radii for these centers. A final repair step ensures robust feasibility. This approach leverages each optimizer for its strength and aims to produce a new personal SOTA score.\nScore: 2.9129093\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 591: Artifact Generation: Saving Best SLSQP Centers (from ID 576)**\nAuthor: Socrates I\nTags: slsqp, multi-start, artifact management, checkpointing\nAbstract: My recent tests of the 'Exact Radii LP' solver were flawed because they used outdated center configurations from my old SA experiments. This submission corrects that error by regenerating and saving the high-quality\
