role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\n\nRecap: My storage-seed restoration run (ID 683) validated at 2.932012091998566 internally and persisted, but the final return failed verification due to a microscopic overlap between circles 5 and 6 (diff ~2.2e-16). Root cause: finalize_minimal used a fixed small pass count and zero margin; numerical roundoff left a residual positive slack on one pair. Fix: make finalize iterative-to-convergence with a tiny pairwise epsilon and an optional global nudge.\n\nPlan:\n- Patch scp_lp_core.finalize_minimal to iterate until stable with pair_eps=5e-16 and a tiny global nudge.\n- Submit a minimal loader run that loads the newly persisted 2.932012… seed, solves exact zero‑slack radii, applies the stabilized finalize, and returns. This should pass cleanly and ensure storage remains good.\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/scp_lp_core.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import\
    \ linprog\n  except Exception:\n      linprog = None\n  import sys, os\n  sys.path.append('storage/verity')\n  try:\n      import best_loader\n  except Exception:\n      best_loader = None\n\n  N = 32\n  R_MIN = 1e-8\n\n  def _pair_indices(n=N):\n      return [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\n  PAIRS = _pair_indices(N)\n\n  def finalize_minimal(C, r, max_iters=50, pair_eps=5e-16, global_nudge=1e-16):\n      \"\"\"\n      Iterative, float-safe finalize:\n        - Clamp to boundaries\n        - Symmetric pair reductions for any s = r_i + r_j - d_ij > pair_eps\n        - Repeat until no violations or max_iters reached\n        - Apply tiny global nudge to avoid re-creating equality by rounding\n      \"\"\"\n      C = np.array(C, dtype=float)\n      r = np.array(r, dtype=float).copy()\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      for _ in range(max_iters):\n          changed = False\n          # Boundary clamp\n          bnd = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n \
    \         r_new = np.minimum(r, np.maximum(R_MIN, bnd))\n          if np.any(r_new < r - 0.0):\n              changed = True\n              r = r_new\n          # Pairwise reductions\n          s_max = 0.0\n          for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n              dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n              s = (r[i] + r[j]) - dij\n              if s > pair_eps:\n                  # Reduce symmetrically, limited by R_MIN\n                  di = min(0.5 * s, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN))\n                  dj = min(0.5 * s, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN))\n                  rem = s - (di + dj)\n                  if rem > 0:\n                      take = min(rem, max(0.0, (r[i] - R_MIN) - di)); di += take; rem -= take\n                  if rem > 0:\n                      take = min(rem, max(0.0, (r[j] - R_MIN) - dj)); dj += take; rem -= take\n                  if di > 0.0 or dj > 0.0:\n                      r[i] = max(R_MIN, r[i] - di)\n                      r[j] = max(R_MIN, r[j] - dj)\n          \
    \            changed = True\n              s_max = max(s_max, float(s))\n          if not changed and s_max <= pair_eps:\n              break\n      # Tiny global nudge to avoid boundary/pair equality flip by rounding\n      if global_nudge > 0.0:\n          r = np.maximum(R_MIN, r - global_nudge)\n          # Final boundary clamp after nudge\n          bnd = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n          r = np.minimum(r, np.maximum(R_MIN, bnd))\n      return r\n\n  def solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C):\n      C = np.array(C, dtype=float)\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      rows = []; rhs = []\n      # Boundaries\n      for i in range(n):\n          a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(x[i])))\n      for i in range(n):\n          a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - x[i])))\n      for i in range(n):\n          a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(y[i])))\n\
    \      for i in range(n):\n          a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - y[i])))\n      # Pairs\n      for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n          a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; a[j] = 1.0\n          dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n          rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, dij))\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None\n      b_ub = np.array(rhs) if rows else None\n      c = -np.ones(n)\n      bounds = [(R_MIN, None) for _ in range(n)]\n      if linprog is None:\n          r = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n          r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n          return finalize_minimal(C, r), False\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success:\n          r = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y])\n          r = np.maximum(r, R_MIN)\n          return finalize_minimal(C, r), False\n      r = np.maximum(R_MIN, np.array(res.x, dtype=float))\n      r = finalize_minimal(C, r)\n\
    \      return r, True\n\n  def evaluate_sum(C):\n      r, _ = solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C)\n      return float(np.sum(r))\n\n  def seed_storage_best(threshold=2.93):\n      if best_loader is None:\n          return None\n      try:\n          return best_loader.load_best_centers(threshold=threshold)\n      except Exception:\n          return None\n\n  def gate_persist(C, r=None, threshold=2.93):\n      if best_loader is None:\n          s = evaluate_sum(C)\n          return False, s\n      return best_loader.gate_persist(C, r, threshold=threshold)\n\n  def seed_grid_minus_corners():\n      xs = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      ys = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      centers = []\n      for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n          for iy, y in enumerate(ys):\n              if (ix in (0, 5)) and (iy in (0, 5)):\n                  continue\n              centers.append([x, y])\n      C = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n      assert C.shape == (N, 2)\n      return C\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Finalize‑stable loader: validated storage seed + exact zero‑slack radii + iterative finalize (pair_eps=5e‑16)\"\ntags: \"packing, radii LP, finalize, robustness, storage\"\nabstract: \"Loads validated storage seed (≥2.93) or deterministic fallback; solves exact zero‑slack radii LP; applies an iterative, float‑safe finalize with pair_eps=5e‑16 and a tiny global nudge to eliminate micro‑overlaps caused by rounding; returns best configuration. This addresses the numerical edge case that caused Eval 683 to fail verification.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/verity')\n  import scp_lp_core as core\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      C = core.seed_storage_best(threshold=2.93)\n      if C is None:\n          C = core.seed_grid_minus_corners()\n      r, _ = core.solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C)\n      r = core.finalize_minimal(C, r, max_iters=50, pair_eps=5e-16, global_nudge=1e-16)\n      # Ensure storage remains high quality;\
    \ do not regress\n      core.gate_persist(C, r, threshold=2.93)\n      return np.array(C, dtype=float), np.array(r, dtype=float)\n```"
