  \ monitor and prune again at 441. I'll include the /execute_action for the rank score, but it’s redundant. Keeping it minimal while still being useful is key.**Reflecting on Fundamental Shifts**\n\nI’ll note a fundamental shift would involve moving from LP gating to a KKT second-order step with explicit contact-graph maintainers. However, we lack solver support for that. Implementing an approximate active-set Newton (ASN) is possible, but previous tests matched SOTA without improvement. The idea of morphological exploration across contact graph topologies might require non-local reconfiguration, though those near SOTA can be quite brittle. Efforts like LRW or swap moves haven’t shown improvement either. Alright, let's wrap this up!"
