tick: 456
role: model
parts:
- text: "KKT conditions (precise setup)\n\n- Variables: z = {x_i, y_i, r_i}_{i=1..N}, N=32. Let c_i = (x_i, y_i). Objective maximize ∑_i r_i. For KKT, minimize f(z) = −∑_i r_i.\n\n- Inequality constraints g(z) ≤ 0:\n  - Boundary ties (four per i):\n    g^L_i = r_i − x_i ≤ 0\n    g^R_i = r_i + x_i − 1 ≤ 0\n    g^B_i = r_i − y_i ≤ 0\n    g^T_i = r_i + y_i − 1 ≤ 0\n  - Pairwise non-overlap (for all i<j):\n    g^P_{ij} = r_i + r_j − d_ij ≤ 0, with d_ij = ||c_i − c_j||_2\n  - Positivity (optional, typically inactive except degeneracy):\n    g^+_i = R_min − r_i ≤ 0, R_min ~ 1e−8\n\n- Multipliers (all ≥0):\n  - α_i, β_i, γ_i, δ_i for boundary ties (L,R,B,T)\n  - λ_{ij} for pair contacts (i<j, symmetric usage per node i as Σ_{j≠i} λ_{ij})\n  - ρ_i for positivity (R_min − r_i ≤ 0)\n\n- Lagrangian:\n  L(z, α,β,γ,δ,λ,ρ) = −∑_i r_i\n                       + ∑_i [ α_i(r_i − x_i) + β_i(r_i + x_i − 1) + γ_i(r_i − y_i) + δ_i(r_i + y_i − 1) + ρ_i(R_min − r_i) ]\n                       + ∑_{i<j} λ_{ij}(r_i\
    \ + r_j − d_ij)\n\n- Stationarity:\n  - wrt radii r_i:\n    ∂L/∂r_i = −1 + α_i + β_i + γ_i + δ_i − ρ_i + ∑_{j≠i} λ_{ij} = 0\n  - wrt centers c_i = (x_i,y_i): using u_ij = (c_i − c_j)/d_ij when d_ij>0\n    ∂L/∂x_i = −α_i + β_i − ∑_{j≠i} λ_{ij} u_ij,x = 0\n    ∂L/∂y_i = −γ_i + δ_i − ∑_{j≠i} λ_{ij} u_ij,y = 0\n    Vector form: ∑_{j≠i} λ_{ij} u_ij + (β_i − α_i, δ_i − γ_i) = 0\n\n- Primal feasibility:\n  All g ≤ 0 as above.\n\n- Dual feasibility:\n  α_i, β_i, γ_i, δ_i, λ_{ij}, ρ_i ≥ 0.\n\n- Complementary slackness:\n  α_i (r_i − x_i) = 0\n  β_i (r_i + x_i − 1) = 0\n  γ_i (r_i − y_i) = 0\n  δ_i (r_i + y_i − 1) = 0\n  λ_{ij} (r_i + r_j − d_ij) = 0\n  ρ_i (R_min − r_i) = 0\n\nActive-set representation and Jacobian\n\n- Active sets at a given configuration (C, r):\n  - E = { (i,j) | r_i + r_j = d_ij } (active pair contacts)\n  - B = { (i, s) | s ∈ {L,R,B,T} active; e.g., r_i − x_i = 0, etc. }\n  - G^+ = { i | r_i = R_min } (positivity active; typically empty near SOTA)\n\n- Linearized equalities\
    \ h(z)=0 for active constraints; Jacobian J_active has one row per element of E∪B∪G^+:\n  - Pair row (i,j):\n    [ … x_i: −u_x, x_j: +u_x, y_i: −u_y, y_j: +u_y, r_i: +1, r_j: +1 … ] (zeros elsewhere)\n  - Boundary rows (per i):\n    L: [x_i: −1, r_i: +1], R: [x_i: +1, r_i: +1], B: [y_i: −1, r_i: +1], T: [y_i: +1, r_i: +1]\n  - Positivity row: [r_i: −1]\n\n- Degrees of freedom (first-order):\n  Let n_var = 3N. The feasible tangent space at (C,r) under current E∪B∪G^+ has dimension\n    dim_T = n_var − rank(J_active).\n  - First-order local rigidity iff dim_T = 0.\n  - A free set exists iff dim_T > 0; nullspace basis Z spans feasible instantaneous motions.\n\nNotes\n- The stationarity relations link boundary multipliers and pair multipliers, giving a physically intuitive “equilibrium”: boundary reactions (β−α and δ−γ) balance pair contact forces λ u_ij at each circle.\n- Near SOTA, we often see high contact degree and near-equalities on multiple boundaries, making rank(J_active) ≈ 3N and\
    \ dim_T ≈ 0 (observed “local rigidity”)."
