parts:
- text: "Active‑set updates (practical rules)\n\nGoal: keep the working set E∪B (and rarely G+) close to the true active set while preventing chattering and overconstraining.\n\n- Slack definitions at (C,r):\n  - Pair slack s^P_{ij} = d_ij − (r_i + r_j)\n  - Boundary slacks s^L_i = x_i − r_i; s^R_i = 1 − x_i − r_i; s^B_i = y_i − r_i; s^T_i = 1 − y_i − r_i\n  - Positivity slack s^+_i = r_i − R_min\n\n- Tolerances (deterministic constants):\n  - tol_add = 5e−13, tol_drop = 2e−12, tol_mult = 1e−10\n  - Hysteresis: add if s < −tol_add; drop only if s > +tol_drop (or multiplier tiny)\n  - Limit per iteration: add at most A_max = 8 constraints; drop at most D_max = 6 constraints (prefer dropping first)\n\n- Add rules (after evaluating r_exact and finalize on trial):\n  - Form violation list V = {constraints with s < −tol_add}, sorted by ascending s, tie‑broken by (type, index).\n  - Add the first min(A_max, |V|) to the set; for pairs, also ensure no duplicates and consistent (i<j) indexing.\n\
    \  - If adding makes J rank‑deficient (detected below), revert the last few additions until full row rank is restored.\n\n- Drop rules (before solving KKT at the next iteration):\n  - Candidate to drop if:\n    - multiplier ≈ 0: λ_{ij} < tol_mult for two consecutive accepted steps (keep a streak counter), or\n    - slack recovery: s > +tol_drop for two consecutive accepted steps.\n  - Drop up to D_max such candidates, prioritizing those with the largest positive slack.\n  - Never drop positivity (G+) unless r_i > R_min + 1e−6 persistently.\n\n- Cycling safeguards:\n  - Maintain an “age” per constraint (steps since last add/drop). Disallow flipping a constraint within age < 3.\n  - If the same constraint flips 3 times in 10 steps, freeze it for 10 steps (do-not-touch).\n\n- Size control:\n  - If |E∪B| > 3N + 12, prune to 3N by dropping the smallest‑multiplier constraints first (subject to hysteresis).\n\n- Degenerate cases:\n  - If d_ij ≈ 0 (coincident centers) ever occurs (shouldn’t\
    \ with finalize), immediately resolve by a tiny separating move along any fixed axis and re‑solve exact LP; reinit E around that pair.\n\n\nIntegration into MM‑LP Adaptive (Stage B refiner)\n\n- Triggering:\n  - Use SCP‑LP until plateau: no improvement over 5 iterations with α backtracking tried → switch to KKT‑Newton refiner.\n  - Or enter KKT directly when rank(J_active) at the SCP‑LP incumbent is within 2 of 3N (near‑rigid).\n\n- Refiner loop (per elite seed):\n  1) Initialize E,B from constraints with |s| ≤ 5e−13; compute J, rank, dim_T.\n  2) Solve Option A QP (null‑space ascent); if robust multipliers available and KKT well‑conditioned, try Option B.\n  3) Globalize with trust region + backtracking on exact radii LP objective; finalize; accept only if Δ∑r ≥ 1e−9.\n  4) Update active set using rules above; recompute diagnostics; adapt τ_c, τ_r (increase ×1.2 on accept, decrease ×0.6 on reject).\n  5) Stop after either:\n     - 10 consecutive rejects,\n     - 25 total iterations,\n\
    \     - improvement < 5e−10 over last 5 accepts.\n  6) If the first 5 iterations yield no accept, fall back to SCP‑LP for 5 iterations; then retry KKT once. If still no accept, terminate refiner for this seed.\n\n- Determinism:\n  - Fixed ordering of constraints (pairs lexicographic by (i,j); boundaries in L,R,B, T order).\n  - Fixed tolerances, τ schedules, α list, linear solver options, tie‑breakers in objective.\n  - Persist best incumbent to storage/verity/best_* only if score ≥ current best and ≥ 2.93 (guard).\n\n\nDiagnostics and logging\n\n- Structural properties each iteration:\n  - rank(J) via SVD with τ_rank = 1e−12; dim_T = 3N − rank(J)\n  - cond(JJ^T) (or of normal equations) as conditioning proxy\n  - min, median, max slacks per type; count of near‑contacts (# with |s| ≤ 1e−12)\n  - complementarity residuals: mean/max of |λ·s| over active constraints\n  - stationarity residuals:\n      r_i: |−1 + α_i + β_i + γ_i + δ_i − ρ_i + Σ_j λ_ij|\n      c_i: ||(β_i − α_i, δ_i − γ_i)\
    \ − Σ_j λ_ij u_ij||\n  - acceptance ratio over sliding window (last 10 steps)\n\n- Logging plan:\n  - TSV per run: iter, rank, dim_T, cond, Δsum_r, sum_r, τ_c, τ_r, #adds, #drops, min_slack_pair, min_slack_bound, min_mult, max_mult.\n  - Snapshot best C,r every accept (np.save with monotone filename), plus final.\n  - On failure modes (singular KKT, no accept in 10 tries), write a short reason code.\n\n- Health checks:\n  - After accept, re‑solve exact LP at higher internal precision if available; assert finalize yields nonnegative slacks with safety epsilon (e.g., pairs ≥ 5e−16 after nudge).\n\n\nRisks and mitigations\n\n- Ill‑conditioning near co‑linear/contact clusters:\n  - Mitigate with row scaling of J, Tikhonov η on (1,1) block, and trust‑region clipping.\n  - Detect via cond > 1e12; if triggered, reduce τ and use Option A only (skip curvature).\n\n- Micro‑overlaps from FP error:\n  - Always run iterative zero‑tolerance finalize with pair margin = 5e−16 and a tiny global nudge\
    \ (1e−16) before acceptance tests.\n\n- Active‑set mis‑specification:\n  - Use hysteresis thresholds; limit adds/drops per iteration; prefer drops when rank inflation occurs.\n  - If repeated infeasibility or singular KKT, clear E additions from the last step and rebuild from slack ≤ 5e−13.\n\n- Nonconvexity and step rejection streaks:\n  - Globalization via backtracking on the true (exact LP) objective; on repeated rejects, fall back to SCP‑LP for a few steps to re‑shape geometry.\n\n- Multiplier estimation (for Option B):\n  - If LP solver duals not available, prefer Option A. Only form H when a stable NNLS fit yields λ ≥ 0 with small residual; otherwise skip curvature.\n\n- Box violations:\n  - Clip centers to [0,1] after step; re‑solve exact LP; if many clippings occur, reduce τ_c.\n\nThis blueprint slots cleanly into our pipeline: MM‑LP Stage B calls KKT‑Newton refiner under deterministic schedules, uses exact radii LP + finalize as the merit, and retains all guards already in place\
    \ (storage gating, persistence policy, and logging)."
