parts:
- text: "Blueprint to code (pseudocode, data structures, and integration)\n\nData structures and indices\n- Variables: z ∈ R^{3N} ordered as [x_0..x_{N-1}, y_0..y_{N-1}, r_0..r_{N-1}]\n  - ix(i) = i, iy(i) = N + i, ir(i) = 2N + i\n- Pairs: precompute list Pairs = [(i,j)] with i<j; utilities d_ij(C), u_ij(C)\n- Active set:\n  - E: set of pair indices k→(i,j)\n  - B: set of boundary tags (i,s) with s∈{L,R,B,T}\n  - G+: set of i with r_i=R_min (typically empty)\n- Jacobian J stored sparse (CSR/COO). Row builder helpers:\n  - add_pair_row(i,j): row with cols {ix(i): −u_x, ix(j): +u_x, iy(i): −u_y, iy(j): +u_y, ir(i): +1, ir(j): +1}\n  - add_bound_row(i,'L'): cols {ix(i): −1, ir(i): +1}, etc. for R,B,T\n  - add_pos_row(i): cols {ir(i): −1}\n- Residual A(z) for active equalities (usually ≈0 after finalize):\n  - pair: r_i + r_j − d_ij\n  - left: r_i − x_i; right: r_i + x_i − 1; bottom: r_i − y_i; top: r_i + y_i − 1\n  - pos: R_min − r_i\n\nOption A step (closed form via elimination)\n- Weighted\
    \ movement: W = diag(w_c I_{2N}, w_r I_N) with w_c=1/τ_c, w_r=1/τ_r; M = W^T W = diag(w_c^2 on centers, w_r^2 on radii)\n- KKT:\n    M Δz + J^T ν = e_r        with e_r = [0, 0, 1,...,1]^T\n    J Δz         = −A\n- Eliminate Δz:\n    S ν = b with S = J M^{-1} J^T  and  b = A + J M^{-1} e_r\n    Δz = M^{-1}(e_r − J^T ν)\n- Numerics:\n  - Add ηI to M (tiny η∈[1e−9,1e−6]) if needed\n  - Build S via sparse ops; solve Sν=b by symmetric solver (LDLT/CG with diagonal preconditioner)\n  - Determinism: fixed J row/col order; small index‑based offsets in e_r if tie‑breaking needed\n\nOption B curvature (only if robust λ available)\n- Build H on centers from contact multipliers λ_{ij}:\n    S_ij = (I − u u^T)/d_ij; add λ_{ij} S_ij to blocks (i,i) and (j,j), subtract to (i,j),(j,i)\n- KKT:\n    [H+ηI  J^T][Δz] = −∇_z L\n    [ J     0 ][ν ]   [  A   ]\n- Prefer Option A initially; switch to B when multipliers are stable and KKT conditioning acceptable.\n\nGlobalization (trust region + exact objective)\n\
    - Clip Δx,Δy to ±τ_c; Δr to ±τ_r; then backtrack α ∈ {1, 0.7, 0.5, 0.35, 0.2, 0.12, 0.08}:\n  - C_trial = clip_box(C + α ΔC, [0,1]); solve exact zero‑slack radii LP → r_exact\n  - r_fin = finalize_zero_tol(C_trial, r_exact)  // iterative, float‑safe, pair margin ~5e−16 + 1e−16 global nudge\n  - gain = sum(r_fin) − sum(r)\n  - accept if gain ≥ ε_accept (e.g., 1e−9 in refinement); else try smaller α\n- On fail: τ_c,τ_r ← 0.6×; pivot active set (see below); if persistence of rejects, fall back to SCP‑LP for 3–5 steps\n\nActive‑set construction and updates\n- Build initial E,B from |slack| ≤ 5e−13; drop duplicates; ensure row full‑rank preference\n- After accept:\n  - Add up to A_max=8 most violated constraints (s < −5e−13), sorted by violation magnitude\n  - Drop up to D_max=6 with multiplier < 1e−10 for two consecutive accepts, or slack > +2e−12 twice\n  - Hysteresis/anti‑chatter: age counters (age<3 → no flip), freeze if 3 flips within 10 steps\n  - If rank inflation (rank(J) > 3N or\
    \ numerical singularity), revert last additions until stable\n- Before next solve: recompute slacks, J, rank by SVD (τ_rank ~1e−12), dim_T = 3N − rank(J)\n\nAcceptance, stopping, and fallback\n- Accept on gain ≥ 1e−9; increase τ by ×1.2 (cap at 0.12)\n- Reject: decrease τ by ×0.6; if 5 consecutive rejects or 10 total iterations without accept, do 5 SCP‑LP steps, then retry once; else stop\n- Terminate refiner after 25 iterations or if last 5 accepts improve < 5e−10\n\nPseudocode (deterministic)\n\nfunction refine_kkt(C0):\n  r0 = exact_radii_lp(C0); r0 = finalize_zero_tol(C0, r0)\n  z = [C0, r0]; best = (z, sum(r0))\n  τ_c=0.04; τ_r=0.02; ε_acc=1e−9\n  E,B = build_active_sets(z, thr=5e−13); ages, streaks = init_counters(E,B)\n  rejects=0; accepts=0; it=0\n  while it < 25:\n    J,A = build_J_and_A(z, E,B)\n    rank = svd_rank(J, 1e−12)\n    Δz = solve_option_A(J,A, τ_c, τ_r)  # or option_B if enabled and stable\n    Δz = clip_trust_region(Δz, τ_c, τ_r)\n    accepted = False\n    for α\
    \ in [1.0, 0.7, 0.5, 0.35, 0.2, 0.12, 0.08]:\n      z_trial = project_box(z + αΔz)  # centers to [0,1]\n      r_exact = exact_radii_lp(z_trial.C); r_fin = finalize_zero_tol(z_trial.C, r_exact)\n      gain = sum(r_fin) − sum(z.r)\n      if gain >= ε_acc:\n        z = [z_trial.C, r_fin]; best = max(best, (z, sum(r_fin)))\n        τ_c, τ_r = min(0.12, 1.2*τ_c), min(0.06, 1.2*τ_r)\n        accepted=True; accepts+=1; rejects=0\n        break\n    if not accepted:\n      τ_c *= 0.6; τ_r *= 0.6; rejects += 1\n      if rejects >= 5 or it >= 10:\n        if try_scp_lp_recover(z): rejects = 0; continue\n        else: break\n    E,B, ages, streaks = update_active_set(z, E,B, ages, streaks)\n    it += 1\n  return best.z\n\nDeterminism and integration\n- Determinism sources:\n  - Fixed orderings (pairs lexicographic; boundaries in L,R,B,T)\n  - Fixed thresholds {5e−13, 2e−12, 1e−10}, trust‑region schedules, α list\n  - Stable sparse solver options (fixed seeds not needed since no randomness)\n  -\
    \ Tie‑breakers: tiny index‑weighted offsets in e_r to make SPD system unique\n- Integration:\n  - Use in MM‑LP Stage B (refinement) in place of SCP‑LP when plateau detected or when rank(J)≥3N−2 (near‑rigid)\n  - Same persistence policy: persist to storage/verity only if score ≥ current best and ≥ 2.93\n\nDiagnostics and tests\n- Per‑iter TSV: iter, sum_r, Δsum_r, rank(J), dim_T, ||A||_∞, cond(S), τ_c, τ_r, adds, drops, min slack (pair/bound), accept flag\n- Property tests:\n  - Build synthetic configurations with known actives; check J rows and A(z) values\n  - Verify elimination identities: Δz = M^{-1}(e_r − J^T ν) and Sν=b; numerically check KKT residuals\n  - Invariance: exact radii LP + finalize always returns nonnegative slacks with safety margins\n- Performance: S size ≈ |E|+|B| ~ O(3N) ≈ 100; KKT solves are cheap (sub‑millisecond to milliseconds)\n\nMultiplier estimation for Option B (if enabled later)\n- Prefer LP duals if exposed by solver; if unavailable, estimate λ by constrained\
    \ least squares at each circle i:\n    Find λ_i (nonnegative over neighbors j) and (α_i,β_i,γ_i,δ_i,ρ_i ≥ 0) minimizing:\n      ||(β_i−α_i, δ_i−γ_i) − Σ_j λ_{ij} u_ij||_2^2 + w_r (−1 + α_i+β_i+γ_i+δ_i −ρ_i + Σ_j λ_{ij})^2\n  - Solve via NNLS with small Tikhonov; discard curvature if large residuals or negative components appear.\n\nFailure handling\n- Singular S or cond>1e12: reduce τ, drop the last few added constraints, or switch to SCP‑LP steps\n- Repeated micro‑overlaps: tighten finalize margin slightly (to 8e−16) for this run; never persist unless post‑finalize checks pass\n\nWith this blueprint, the KKT refiner slots cleanly into our zero‑slack pipeline, remains deterministic, and uses the exact LP objective as a robust merit function. It provides a principled way to exploit any small residual degrees of freedom (dim_T>0) near the rigid SOTA while maintaining feasibility and reproducibility."
thinking_content: "**Optimizing with SciPy**\n\nI’m looking into SciPy's `optimize.linprog` using the 'highs' method. It seems like the result has attributes like `res.ineqlin` (residuals) and `res.eqlin`, but I’m not completely certain about the details of `res`. I can think about deriving λ by solving stationarity equations while focusing on algorithmic steps for `refine_kkt(C_initial)` with an expected complexity of O(m^1.5). I’m also considering setting up a test harness with synthetic near rigid sets and ensuring reproducibility through deterministic seeds and logging.**Crafting Iteration Pseudocode**\n\nI’m working on tick 4 content, focusing on writing precise pseudocode for each iteration. I need to define data structures like variable indices for x, y, and r, and handle pairs adjacency while precomputing values like u_ij and distances. I’ll also construct an active set using slack thresholds and a sparse J matrix. \n\nFor the A(z) residual vector, my goal is to ensure it’s zero\
  \ upon finalization. I plan to solve normal equations using the KKT elimination method, which involves solving \\(\\Delta z = \\text{argmin} 0.5 ||W\\Delta z||^2 - e_r^T \\Delta z\\) subject to specific conditions.**Deriving Elimination from KKT**\n\nI'm working on deriving elimination from the Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) conditions. I’ve set up the equations involving \\((W^T W) \\Delta z + J^T \\nu = e_r\\) and \\(J \\Delta z = -A\\). By letting \\(M = W^T W\\), I’ll solve \\(J M^{-1} J^T \\nu = J M^{-1} e_r + A\\). This leads to expressing it in terms of \\(J\\) and \\(e_r\\), ultimately allowing me to solve for \\(\\nu\\). I also need to include \\(W\\) weights and adjust the diagonal in \\(M\\) accordingly. I’ll create a formula and code blueprint for that!**Proposing Option B for Hessian Contributions**\n\nI'm looking into proposing Option B, which involves Hessian contributions \\(S_{ij}\\). This option follows a similar approach to the KKT conditions, and I plan to define a `finalize_zero_tol`\
  \ function stored in `finalize_utils`, ensuring proper acceptance gating. Discussing complexity, \\(J\\) is \\(m\\) by \\(3N\\), where \\(m\\) is approximately the number of active pairs plus active boundaries. With around 32 circles leading to nearly 96 constraints, I want to ensure stability in the contact graph and set up testing with baseline and jitter seeds. I’ll prepare pseudocode for key functions and variable names to aid in clarity.**Exploring Penalty Fallback Options**\n\nI’m considering proposing an \"interior penalty fallback,\" but to keep things brief, I might skip that for now. Instead, I’ll focus on ensuring tick 4 is prepared properly. Once that’s done, let’s get to producing the actual content needed! I want to ensure everything is clear and correctly formatted while maintaining the quality. I'm curious to see how this will all come together in the end!"
