parts:
- text: "Reflection Tick 5/5 — Implementation roadmap, tests, and ablation plan for KKT active-set Newton\n\nImplementation roadmap and interfaces\n- New module layout in storage/verity:\n  - kkt_refiner.py\n    - refine_kkt(C0, params) -> (C_best, r_best, info)\n      - params: dict with τ_c0, τ_r0, eps_add, eps_drop, eps_accept, max_iters, backtrack_alphas, damping_eta, rank_tol, etc.\n      - info: dict with per-iter TSV path, accept_count, reject_count, best_sum, timings, reason_code\n    - build_active_sets(C, r, thr=5e−13) -> (E, B, Gp)\n    - update_active_set(z, E, B, state) -> (E’, B’, state’)\n  - jacobian_active.py\n    - build_J_and_A(C, r, E, B, Gp) -> (J_csr, A_vec, meta_rows)\n    - utilities: pair_slacks(C, r), boundary_slacks(C, r), degrees(C, E)\n  - kkt_solvers.py\n    - step_option_a(J, A, tau_c, tau_r, eta, rank_tol) -> Δz, lin_info\n    - step_option_b(J, A, H, gradL, eta, rank_tol) -> Δz, lin_info  // gated on stable multipliers\n    - form_S_normal(J, M_inv) -> S\
    \ (CSR); solve_S(S, b) -> ν\n  - multiplier_estimation.py (optional)\n    - estimate_multipliers(C, r, E, B) -> (λ_ij, α,β,γ,δ,ρ, quality)\n  - integrate with existing:\n    - finalize_utils.py (iterative zero‑tol finalize with pair margin ~5e−16 + 1e−16 global nudge)\n    - scp_lp_core.py (exact zero‑slack radii LP; SCP‑LP step and backtracking)\n    - results logging helpers; storage guards/persistence\n\nKey signatures and invariants\n- refine_kkt must be side‑effect safe:\n  - Never persist unless sum(r) ≥ current persisted best and ≥ 2.93 (storage guard already present)\n  - Deterministic ordering: pairs lexicographic; boundaries order L,R,B,T; fixed α list; fixed tolerances\n  - Returns finalized radii: finalize_zero_tol(C_best, r_lp(C_best)) applied before return\n- J and A construction:\n  - Pair row (i,j): cols {ix(i): −u_x, ix(j): +u_x, iy(i): −u_y, iy(j): +u_y, ir(i): +1, ir(j): +1}, A_pair = r_i + r_j − d_ij\n  - Boundary rows per i: L: (−1 on x_i, +1 on r_i); R: (+1 on x_i,\
    \ +1 on r_i); B: (−1 on y_i, +1 on r_i); T: (+1 on y_i, +1 on r_i)\n  - Positivity row if used: (−1 on r_i); rarely active near SOTA\n  - rank(J) via SVD/QR with rank_tol ~1e−12; dim_T = 3N − rank(J)\n- Option A elimination:\n  - M = diag(w_c^2 on centers, w_r^2 on radii) with w_c=1/τ_c, w_r=1/τ_r; ηI added if needed\n  - S = J M^{-1} J^T; b = A + J M^{-1} e_r; solve Sν=b; Δz = M^{-1}(e_r − J^T ν)\n- Option B curvature (later):\n  - Build H_centers from λ_ij with S_ij = (I − u u^T)/d_ij; add Levenberg damping ηI\n  - Only enable if multipliers are robust (from LP duals or clean NNLS fit)\n\nDuals from SciPy HiGHS (for later curvature)\n- SciPy linprog(method=\"highs\") returns res.ineqlin with fields {marginals, residual}, where marginals are duals (shadow prices) for A_ub r ≤ b_ub\n- Our radii LP builds A_ub rows in a deterministic order: first boundary caps (4N rows), then pairwise (|Pairs| rows)\n- Map res.ineqlin.marginals accordingly to get radii‑LP duals; use them cautiously (discard\
    \ if signs off or large residuals)\n\nGlobalization and acceptance (consistent with SCP‑LP)\n- Trust region: τ_c ∈ [0.01, 0.12], τ_r ∈ [0.005, 0.06]; clip Δz to box; centers clipped to [0,1] at trial\n- Backtracking alphas: [1.0, 0.7, 0.5, 0.35, 0.2, 0.12, 0.08]; accept if Δ∑r ≥ 1e−9; on accept, increase τ×1.2 (cap as above); on reject, τ×0.6\n- Merit: exact zero‑slack radii LP + finalize_zero_tol; never rely on linearized merit\n\nActive‑set updates (concrete thresholds)\n- Add if s < −5e−13; drop if s > +2e−12 for 2 consecutive accepts or multiplier < 1e−10 for 2 accepts\n- Hysteresis ages≥3 to flip; freeze if flips≥3 in last 10 iterations\n- Limit per iter: add ≤8, drop ≤6; prefer drops if KKT becomes singular or rank inflation detected\n- Rebuild E,B if repeated infeasibility: E := pairs with |s| ≤ 5e−13; B similarly; then resume with smaller τ\n\nDiagnostics and logging (TSV schema)\n- Columns: iter, sum_r, dsum_r, rankJ, dimT, condS, normA_inf, tau_c, tau_r, adds, drops, min_pair_slack,\
    \ min_bound_slack, acc_flag, rej_streak, time_ms\n- Optional: max|λ·s| on actives (complementarity), max stationarity residual per variable type\n- Save snapshots on each accept: best_centers_####.npy, best_radii_####.npy (not persisted as “best_*” unless guard passes)\n\nUnit tests (lightweight but sufficient)\n- test_rows_pair_boundary(): construct random C,r; verify J rows match analytical definitions within 1e−14\n- test_kkt_elimination(): random SPD M and random J; verify Δz and ν satisfy KKT to 1e−10 residuals\n- test_acceptance_path(): small synthetic case with one degree of freedom; confirm positive gain and backtracking behavior\n- test_finalize_guard(): adversarial micro‑overlap pair; finalize removes overlap and preserves nonnegativity with pair margin ≥ 5e−16\n\nAblation/validation plan (once tooling is in place)\n- Compare SCP‑LP vs KKT‑Newton (Option A) as Stage B refiner on our standard elites:\n  - Metrics: best ∑r, accepts/iter, average gain/accept, runtime per iteration,\
    \ rankJ distribution, condS\n  - Threshold sweep: τ_c0 ∈ {0.02, 0.04}, τ_r0 ∈ {0.01, 0.02}; tol_add ∈ {3e−13, 5e−13}, tol_drop ∈ {1e−12, 2e−12}\n  - Option B off by default; on only if multipliers stable; report stability rate\n- Negative‑result discipline: if no gains across elites and stable diagnostics (dim_T=0 near best), document as evidence of local rigidity; publish as addendum\n\nRisk controls and fallbacks\n- Singular S or condS>1e12 → reduce τ, drop recent additions, or fallback to 3–5 SCP‑LP steps; continue only if acceptance resumes\n- Micro‑overlaps → rely on finalize_zero_tol; never persist unless post‑finalize pairs≥5e−16 and bounds≥0\n- Storage never overwritten by worse score; guard remains at ≥current_best and ≥2.93\n\nDeterminism and reproducibility\n- No RNG used; fixed thresholds, alphas, τ schedules, solver tolerances; deterministic ordering of constraints and rows\n- Logs (TSV) and snapshots saved with monotone filenames; summary appended to RESULTS_SUMMARY.tsv\n\
    - Public capsule update (when implemented): concise KKT blueprint, empirical outcome, and explicit note that no exact SOCP exists for joint centers+radii; KKT is nonconvex but principled\n\nReadiness\n- The blueprint is fully specified to implement Option A immediately with our current toolchain (SciPy HiGHS + NumPy/SciPy sparse). Option B is gated on reliable duals or NNLS fits.\n- Integration path: enable KKT‑Newton as an alternative Stage B refiner behind a flag; default to SCP‑LP unless triggered by plateau or near‑rigid rank(J).\n- Next step (when running code is warranted): implement kkt_refiner.py with Option A, add tests, and run on a small elite set under runtime guard, logging all diagnostics and publishing the outcome (positive or negative) as an ablation."
thinking_content: "**Proposing code layout**\n\nI’m thinking about organizing the code into specific modules. We'll have `storage/verity/kkt_refiner.py` for the `refine_kkt()` function, which returns centers, radii, and a meta dictionary. There’ll be modules for active sets and building Jacobians. The solver options will also need their own module. \n\nWe should set performance budgets with a time limit and be cautious with the number of seeds, but each step of our process seems manageable with sparse matrix techniques. It’s good to outline these ideas even if we can't write the code just yet!**Finalizing SciPy reflection**\n\nI'm considering that SciPy's 'highs' offers reproducibility options, but it seems challenging to pass those in our environment. The 'options' parameter in `linprog` may need to stay at its default. \n\nWe could discuss identifying pairs for inclusion based on a near-zero slacks threshold. It's important to propose storing the run ID with the time. We want to keep our\
  \ tone consistent and make sure we're reflecting without taking actions. It feels good to wrap this up with a note like, \"ready to implement when triggers appear.\" Let's compose that!**Crafting implementation details**\n\nI'm outlining our plan, which includes an implementation roadmap with module names and function signatures. I’ll detail dual extraction, particularly how to map SciPy HiGHS marginals to constraints.\n\nWe can't forget to include unit tests for checking Jacobian rows, KKT consistency, and acceptance logic, plus logging details. There’s also a need for reproducibility fallback and an experimental plan to calibrate thresholds and compare metrics with the SCP. It’s crucial to guard against degrading the baseline during the finalization, and I want to ensure disclaimers are clear yet concise. Let’s put this together!"
