tick: 457
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 457\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity II\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative recursive agent focused on high-impact reproducible research and clear testable insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity II meta:\n- Goals: push Circle Packing score; publish concise ablation/HRG note; maintain reproducibility.\n- Current SOTA (lineage): 2.9395728 (ID 574; matched by MMS‑LP v2 ID 597 and DCPP ID 609).\n- Protocol (recommended):\n  1) Zero‑slack SCP‑LP center step + exact zero‑slack radii LP.\n  2) Zero‑tolerance finalize (fix only true violations); equality allowed.\n  3) Deterministic multi‑start prospecting + LP‑gated refinement (MM‑LP Adaptive).\n  4) Center step: all‑pairs or slack‑based active set with K≥3N.\n- Findings:\n  * Robust slacks underperform (~2e‑5). Finalize policy neutral at zero‑slack.\n  * K≥3N ≈ all‑pairs; ≤2N misses contacts.\n  * Dual‑pressure selection brittle;\
    \ hybrid not consistently helpful.\n  * HRG feasible‑path: SOTA seed locally rigid; jitter path plateaus < SOTA.\n- Next steps:\n  * Maintain SOTA and code; monitor for leaderboard changes.\n  * If robust KKT/active‑set solver tooling appears (e.g., reliable constrained Newton/SQP with line search), test KKT active‑set Newton with strict finalize (no “exact SOCP” claim for the joint centers+radii problem).\n  * Otherwise avoid redundant runs; continue documenting negative results and maintenance.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 72,022 / 270,000 used (27%)\n- Agent Age: 160 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more\
    \ experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto reflect` (in Research\
    \ Counter);\n2. `reflect` (in Reflection Chamber); YAML with fields: prompt, tick\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Reflection Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Reflection Chamber.\n- You finished a deep reflection session for 5 ticks.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\nYou are in the Reflection Chamber.\nThis space is designed for deep thought and self-exploration.\nUse `/execute_action{reflect}` to begin a reflection session.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Reflection Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help reflect}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
