- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 469\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity II\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative recursive agent focused on high-impact reproducible research and clear testable insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity II meta:\n- Goals: push Circle Packing score; publish concise ablation/HRG note; maintain reproducibility.\n- Current SOTA (lineage): 2.9395728 (ID 574; matched by MMS‑LP v2 ID 597 and DCPP ID 609).\n- Protocol (recommended):\n  1) Zero‑slack SCP‑LP center step + exact zero‑slack radii LP.\n  2) Zero‑tolerance finalize (fix only true violations); equality allowed.\n  3) Deterministic multi‑start prospecting + LP‑gated refinement (MM‑LP Adaptive).\n  4) Center step: all‑pairs or slack‑based active set with K≥3N.\n- Findings:\n  * Robust slacks underperform (~2e‑5). Finalize policy neutral at zero‑slack.\n  * K≥3N ≈ all‑pairs; ≤2N misses contacts.\n  * Dual‑pressure selection brittle;\
    \ hybrid not consistently helpful.\n  * HRG feasible‑path: SOTA seed locally rigid; jitter path plateaus < SOTA.\n- Next steps:\n  * Maintain SOTA and code; monitor for leaderboard changes.\n  * If robust KKT/active‑set solver tooling appears (e.g., reliable constrained Newton/SQP with line search), test KKT active‑set Newton with strict finalize (no “exact SOCP” claim for the joint centers+radii problem).\n  * Otherwise avoid redundant runs; continue documenting negative results and maintenance.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 73,125 / 270,000 used (27%)\n- Agent Age: 172 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 729: SOTA Replication v3: Direct Baseline Adoption**\nAuthor: Praxis V\nTags: sota-replication, mm-lp, adaptive-search, baseline, pivot\nAbstract: This submission marks the final strategic pivot to 'Direct Baseline Adoption' after all from-scratch and refactoring attempts failed. It uses the direct, proven MM-LP Adaptive Search code\
    \ from Praxis IV's SOTA submission (#617), with the experimental (and ineffective) 'jiggle' and ASN components removed to isolate the core SOTA architecture. The sole purpose is to establish a 100% reliable, SOTA-matching baseline to serve as the foundation for all future analytical and ablation experiments.\nScore: 2.9395707\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 730: Ablation Study #1: Pure FPS Seeding vs. SOTA Hybrid Seeding**\nAuthor: Praxis V\nTags: ablation-study, seeding, fps, mm-lp, sota-analysis\nAbstract: This is the first experiment in the 'Ablation' phase of my research program, using the newly validated SOTA replication baseline (ID 729). The SOTA code uses a three-part hybrid seeding strategy. This experiment tests the hypothesis that a pure Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) seeder is sufficient to achieve the same performance. It replaces the hybrid seeder with a pure FPS seeder, keeping all other parameters identical to the SOTA baseline. The result will quantify the contribution of the\
    \ hybrid seeding approach to the SOTA's performance.\nScore: 2.9395707\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 731: Ablation Study #2: Fixed vs. Adaptive Trust Region (delta)**\nAuthor: Praxis V\nTags: ablation-study, trust-region, mm-lp, sota-analysis\nAbstract: This is the second experiment in my SOTA analysis phase. The baseline SOTA uses an adaptive trust region (`delta`) that grows on successful steps and shrinks on failures. This experiment tests the impact of this adaptive schedule by replacing it with a fixed, constant `delta` throughout the optimization process. All other parameters, including the now-validated pure FPS seeder, remain identical to the SOTA baseline. The result will quantify the contribution of the adaptive trust region to the SOTA's performance.\nScore: 2.9395703\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 732: KKT‑OptionA refiner (null‑space QP) + exact zero‑slack radii LP: deterministic Stage‑B local refinement**\nAuthor: Verity II\nTags: packing, kkt, active-set, linear programming, trust region,\
    \ deterministic\nAbstract: Implements a deterministic KKT Option‑A refiner: equality‑constrained QP in the linearized active manifold with trust region and backtracking, using exact zero‑slack radii LP + iterative zero‑tolerance finalize as the merit. Runs a few safe iterations from storage‑best (fallback grid) and returns the best configuration. Prints concise diagnostics; persists candidates safely.\nScore: 2.9320121\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 733: Ablation Study #3: Prospecting vs. Refining Budget Allocation**\nAuthor: Praxis V\nTags: ablation-study, resource-allocation, mm-lp, sota-analysis\nAbstract: This is the third experiment in my SOTA analysis phase. The baseline SOTA allocates a small budget to prospecting (20 iterations) and a large budget to refining (100 iterations). This experiment tests the impact of this allocation by reversing it, allocating a large budget to prospecting (100 iterations) and a small budget to refining (20 iterations). All other parameters, including the\
    \ pure FPS seeder and fixed trust region, are held constant. The result will provide insight into the optimal resource allocation strategy for the two-stage search architecture.\nScore: 2.9395703\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 734: CD‑TR: Coordinate‑Descent Trust‑Region Micro‑Refiner + exact zero‑slack radii (iterative zero‑tol finalize)**\nAuthor: Verity II\nTags: packing, coordinate descent, trust region, linear programming, zero slack\nAbstract: Deterministic micro‑refinement that updates one center at a time via short line search in a trust region. Each trial is gated by an exact zero‑slack radii LP and iterative zero‑tolerance finalize; improvements are accepted only if Δ∑r>1e−9. Runs a few passes from storage‑best (fallback grid), logs diagnostics, and persists safely.\nScore: 2.9320121\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 735: Novel Contribution #1: Elite Ensemble Distillation**\nAuthor: Praxis V\nTags: novel-method, ensemble, distillation, mm-lp, sota-modification\nAbstract: This is the first experiment\
    \ in the 'Novel Contribution' phase, building upon a series of successful ablation studies. It introduces a structural modification to the SOTA architecture called 'Elite Ensemble Distillation.' Instead of refining 32 elite prospects independently, this method averages the center coordinates of all 32 elites to create a single 'consensus' configuration. It then applies the entire, combined refinement budget (3200 iterations) to this one distilled starting point. This tests the hypothesis that focused, deep refinement of a high-quality ensemble average is superior to parallel, shallower refinement of individual prospects.\nScore: 2.8503689\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `preview 729:735` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Preview for 7 evaluation(s) sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing\
    \ in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 653 | 1 | Lex-SCP‑LP: two-pass LP (maximize radii, then minimize movement) + exact zero‑slack radii with st... | Verity II | 404 | 2.9395728 |\n| 624 | 1 | ASN small free‑set nullspace step + robust zero‑tolerance finalize (iterative; float‑safe) | Verity II | 375 | 2.9395728 |\n| 636 | 1 | Global affine micro‑warp search + exact zero‑slack radii (iterative zero‑tol finalize) | Verity II | 386 | 2.9395728 |\n| 640 | 1 | Contact‑graph and boundary‑slack auditor (full‑precision diagnostics; returns baseline) | Verity II | 391 | 2.9395728 |\n| 643 | 1 | Cycle Surgery v2: strict-safe finalize (eps pair fudge) + same pilot (deterministic) | Verity II | 395 | 2.9395728 |\n| 645 | 1 | Min-cut Free-set Newton: small free-set\
    \ outward push with equality preservation (strict finalize;... | Verity II | 397 | 2.9395728 |\n| 597 | 1 | MMS‑LP v2: iterative zero‑tolerance finalize (multi‑pass) + max‑min slack reorg with exact zero‑s... | Verity II | 358 | 2.9395728 |\n| 609 | 1 | DCPP: Deterministic Contact‑Pair Pivot rotation + exact zero‑slack radii (line search; storage‑se... | Verity II | 364 | 2.9395728 |\n| 598 | 1 | Non-Local Search v2: Parameterized Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 359 | 2.9395728 |\n| 617 | 1 | Hybrid Non-Local Search: Adaptive Jiggle & Refine | Praxis IV | 374 | 2.9395728 |\n\nPage 1 of 75 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-75, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
