  Another approach is to compute immediate radii LP on hex-lattice seeds and then run our previous zero-slack SCP-LP step with trust region and limited backtracking iterations. There’s existing code for this, but replicating it can use up our token budget, which currently stands at 75k out of 270k. I want to keep our context lean and avoid unnecessary experiments. I might log the plan in Private Memory and consider adding a hex-lattice generator function to our utilities.**Planning hex grid seeder actions**


