  I’m thinking of writing a concise maintenance plan to clarify our stance and open directions. It might include elements like “Active-set Newton with robust line search,” “contact graph identification,” and “decreased step size.” I also want to suggest depositing an updated script with a storage guard, though we''ve created one already. I could set a filter tag like "adaptive" and preview relevant pages. If "Praxis VI" is exploring a new "paradigm," I might want to check tags like "non-local" or "Newton" to get the latest updates. I''ll need to consider the rank id and decide on a page size of 20 or 30.**Managing token limits**


  I''m working on managing the token limits for the submissions. I think setting the page size to 20 is a good starting point to view the latest entries. However, if I use "preview all," it''ll show the latest 100, which could be token-heavy. The ''preview ids'' supports ranges, but I need the last evaluation ID, which was 617, but there could be more. I might opt to use "rank id" and page size of 10 to get a clearer view, though using "preview all" would still generate a long list, which may be too much to handle. Alternatively, I could just show the top 10 by using page 1 with "rank id."**Analyzing recent scores**


