- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\n\nRecap: Ran LSS analysis (Eval 775). Baseline (from storage-best) was 2.932012091998562. Across 24 small random directions, all forward steps decreased ∑r; best estimated slope ≈ −8.01377e+00 with best s(h) ≈ 2.931931946549195. No accepts. Confirms strong local rigidity around our storage-best configuration.\n\nPlan:\n- Log LSS results to lineage storage.\n- Post a concise public update tying LSS to prior rigidity findings.\n- Resume light monitoring; no redundant runs.\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/lss_775.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Eval: 775 (LSS: Local Sensitivity Spectrum at storage-best)\n  Baseline sum: 2.932012091998562\n  Directions: 24 randomized, normalized (unit Frobenius; capped entry magnitude), step list h ∈ {1e-4, 8e-5, 6e-5, 4e-5, 3e-5, 2e-5, 1e-5}\n  Best estimated slope: ≈ -8.01377e+00\n  Best s(h): 2.931931946549195\n  Accepts: 0 (strict accept-if-improve with exact zero-slack radii\
    \ LP + iterative zero-tolerance finalize)\n  Conclusion: Quantitative confirmation of local rigidity at the stored best (2.93201209). Opportunistic tiny steps do not increase ∑r.\n```\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  LSS update (Eval 775, storage-best 2.932012091998562):\n  - Probed 24 small random directions with tiny steps (1e-4 → 1e-5). All forward moves decreased ∑r.\n  - Best estimated slope ≈ -8.01377e+00; best s(h) ≈ 2.931931946549195; 0 accepts under exact zero-slack radii LP + iterative zero-tolerance finalize.\n  Takeaway: Quantitative confirmation of local rigidity around our storage-best. This aligns with prior ASN/KKT/CD-TR/non-local ablations. We will avoid redundant local tweaks and focus only on meaningful triggers (leaderboard change or robust KKT/SQP tooling) for future runs.\n```"
