tick: 511
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Archive Room\n\nRecap: Prior archive note was rejected for structure/clarity. I am submitting a fully rewritten, self-contained paper in standard format (Introduction, Methodology, Results, Conclusion), defining all terms before results and integrating full-precision outcomes with evaluation IDs.\n\nActions:\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A Structured Rigidity Audit Around a 2.939572768266679 Packing for 32 Circles: Definitions, Methods, and Integrated Results\"\ntags: [\"circle packing\", \"linear programming\", \"zero-slack\", \"rigidity\", \"analysis\", \"ablation\"]\nabstract: \"We study whether first‑order or small non‑local moves can improve strong local optima for 32‑circle packing in the unit square. We define all components (exact zero‑slack radii LP; iterative zero‑tolerance finalize; SCP‑LP center step; Local Sensitivity Spectrum; equality‑constrained SCP‑LP; near‑contact pair pivots; scalarized LP; and controls\
    \ like global affine warps, active‑set QP, and CD‑TR). Using accept‑if‑improve gating and full‑precision reporting, we find no strictly positive gains relative to baselines and an independently achieved SOTA packing (2.939572768266679). Results are integrated with evaluation IDs to document local rigidity and guide future work.\"\ncontent: |\n  1. Introduction\n  Circle packing in the unit square seeks centers c_i=(x_i,y_i) and radii r_i>0 for N=32 circles to maximize ∑ r_i subject to:\n    (i) In‑box: r_i ≤ x_i, r_i ≤ 1−x_i, r_i ≤ y_i, r_i ≤ 1−y_i\n    (ii) Non‑overlap: r_i + r_j ≤ ||c_i − c_j||_2 for all i<j.\n  Despite recent progress via multi‑start LP‑gated search, the landscape near the best packings appears locally rigid. This paper asks: do principled first‑order moves or small, structured non‑local moves yield measurable gains?\n\n  Contributions\n  - Clear, self‑contained definitions for all components we test.\n  - A standardized verification pipeline (exact zero‑slack radii\
    \ LP + iterative zero‑tolerance finalize + accept‑if‑improve).\n  - Integrated, full‑precision results with evaluation IDs showing no strictly positive gains near top packings.\n\n  2. Methodology (definitions and common pipeline)\n\n  2.1 Exact zero‑slack radii LP (verification at fixed centers)\n  Given centers C = {(x_i,y_i)}:\n    maximize ∑_i r_i\n    subject to r_i ≥ R_min (R_min=1e−8),\n              r_i ≤ x_i, r_i ≤ 1−x_i, r_i ≤ y_i, r_i ≤ 1−y_i,\n              r_i + r_j ≤ ||c_i − c_j||_2  ∀ i<j.\n  We solve this LP with HiGHS (SciPy linprog). Equality at constraints is allowed.\n\n  2.2 Finalize (iterative, zero‑tolerance)\n  After the LP we adjust r only if a true violation exists (pairs/boundaries), using a small safety margin for pairs (pair_eps=5e−16) and R_min=1e−8. This never adds positive slack and permits equality.\n\n  2.3 Acceptance rule and precision\n  A candidate update is accepted iff exact LP + finalize yields ∑ r strictly larger than baseline by > 5e−10 (guarding\
    \ against float noise). We report full‑precision sums.\n\n  2.4 Baselines used\n  - Independent SOTA (ours): 2.939572768266679 (ID 574), matched by MMS‑LP v2 (ID 597 ≈ 2.9395727712062967) and DCPP (ID 609 ≈ 2.9395727712062967).\n  - Storage‑best (for mid‑range ablations): 2.932012091998562 (typical).\n\n  2.5 SCP‑LP center step (defined)\n  Linearize non‑overlap at anchor C^0. For each pair (i,j), let u_ij=(c_i^0−c_j^0)/||c_i^0−c_j^0||. The LP variables are (x,y,r); objective maximize ∑ r subject to:\n    r_i − x_i ≤ 0,  r_i + x_i ≤ 1\n    r_i − y_i ≤ 0,  r_i + y_i ≤ 1\n    r_i + r_j − u_x,ij(x_i − x_j) − u_y,ij(y_i − y_j) ≤ d_ij^0 − u_ij·(c_i^0 − c_j^0)\n    x_i ∈ [x_i^0±τ]∩[0,1], y_i ∈ [y_i^0±τ]∩[0,1]\n  Then re‑evaluate with the exact radii LP + finalize. Accept‑if‑improve only.\n\n  2.6 Techniques audited (all deterministic; defined here before use)\n  - LSS (Local Sensitivity Spectrum): Estimate directional derivatives of ∑ r at C by finite differences along many small, unit‑normalized\
    \ directions in center space; then try a tiny line search along the best estimated direction. Always re‑evaluate with exact radii LP + finalize and accept only if improved.\n  - EQ‑SCP‑LP: SCP‑LP with an added equality tying one selected near‑contact pair to be tight in the linearized model; re‑evaluate with exact LP + finalize and accept‑if‑improve.\n  - AS‑Pivot (Near‑contact pair pivot; a non‑local move): Choose k pairs with smallest positive slack that are not currently active; for each, move the two centers symmetrically in the perpendicular direction by a small step α (line‑searched), then exact LP + finalize and accept‑if‑improve.\n  - Scalarized single‑LP: In one LP, maximize ∑ r − λ·||ΔC||_1 subject to SCP‑LP constraints and a trust region, with λ=1e−6; then exact LP + finalize; accept‑if‑improve.\n  Control methods (for completeness):\n  - Global affine micro‑warp: apply tiny rotations/scales/shears to C, then exact LP + finalize.\n  - KKT Option‑A (active‑set QP on linearized\
    \ constraints): step in the null‑space of an estimated active set with trust region/backtracking, then exact LP + finalize.\n  - CD‑TR micro‑refiner: conservative coordinate‑descent with a trust region and exact LP gates.\n  - Transfer tests: initialize from HEX / FPS / random seeds and run short SCP‑LP loops to observe climb behavior.\n\n  3. Results (organized by method; all values full precision)\n\n  3.1 Independent SOTA reference (for context)\n  - ID 574: 2.939572768266679\n  - ID 597 (MMS‑LP v2): 2.9395727712062967\n  - ID 609 (DCPP): 2.9395727712062967\n\n  3.2 LSS (Eval 775; baseline context 2.932012091998562)\n  - Best estimated slope ≈ −8.013770000000000e+00; best s(h)=2.931931946549195; accepts=0.\n\n  3.3 EQ‑SCP‑LP (Eval 803; enforce one near‑contact equality in SCP‑LP; τ∈{0.02,0.015,0.01,0.006,0.004})\n  - Exact LP sums ≈ 2.932012092024872–2.932012092024910; accepts=0.\n\n  3.4 AS‑Pivot (near‑contact pair pivot; Eval 796)\n  - Baseline 2.932012092024910; candidates from\
    \ top near‑active non‑contacts; accepts=0; final 2.932012092024910.\n\n  3.5 Scalarized single‑LP (Eval 788; λ=1e−6)\n  - storage‑best 2.932012091998562; storage‑best‑jitter 2.932012092024910; grid‑36minus4 2.898577376865817; accepts=0.\n\n  3.6 Global affine micro‑warp (Eval 636; around SOTA)\n  - 243 tiny affine transforms tested; returned baseline 2.9395727712063042.\n\n  3.7 KKT Option‑A (active‑set QP; Eval 732; baseline context 2.932012091998562)\n  - Attempts accepted: 0; best sum 2.932012091998562 (no gain).\n\n  3.8 CD‑TR micro‑refiner (Eval 734; baseline context 2.932012091998562)\n  - Attempts accepted: 0; final 2.932012091998562.\n\n  3.9 Transfer tests (short SCP‑LP loops)\n  - HEX→SCP‑LP (Eval 749): hex 2.465547964039957 → 2.919865472582548 (5 accepts); hex‑jitter 2.424283481766276 → 2.927735660243330 (6).\n  - FPS/Random→SCP‑LP (Eval 758): fps 1.600249590300813 → 2.850938403010178 (5); random 1.421360048396682 → 2.861224117875957 (7); grid‑jitter 2.197567535811029 → 2.899905801623030\
    \ (6).\n  Interpretation: SCP‑LP climbs weak seeds rapidly but plateaus below 2.93 without the full MM‑LP architecture.\n\n  3.10 Auxiliary ablations (concise)\n  - Weighted SCP‑LP (IDs 718/719): storage‑best ≈2.932012091998562 for p∈{1.2,1.4,1.6,2.0}, K∈{3N,4N,8N,all}; jitter inferior except p=2 best ≈2.9320120916879.\n  - K‑sweep (active‑set size) earlier: K≥3N ≈ all‑pairs; ≤2N misses critical contacts.\n\n  4. Discussion\n  - First‑order stiffness: Finite‑difference LSS shows strongly negative slopes in random directions at tiny steps; equality‑constrained SCP‑LP feasibly enforces near‑contacts in the linear model but the exact re‑solve yields no net improvement.\n  - Non‑local micro‑moves: Near‑contact pivots, global affine warps, and conservative active‑set QP/CD‑TR refiners return to baseline under strict accept‑if‑improve gates.\n  - Scalarization vs lexicographic: ∑r − λ·||ΔC||_1 did not beat the two‑pass (maximize ∑r then minimize movement), consistent with a sharply peaked\
    \ objective near the optimum.\n  Practical guidance: For LP‑gated methods, zero‑slack modeling, exact radii LP, and zero‑tolerance finalize remain robust defaults. Active‑set reductions should use K≥3N or all‑pairs; dual‑guided selections are brittle from off‑manifold seeds.\n\n  5. Conclusion\n  Under a common, precise verification pipeline, we found no strictly positive gains from first‑order or small non‑local moves around strong local optima up to SOTA 2.939572768266679. This structured audit and its integrated results establish a rigorous negative‑result baseline for future algorithms.\n\n  6. Reproducibility and limitations\n  Deterministic code paths; fixed RNGs where used; HiGHS LP solver; finalize pair_eps=5e−16, R_min=1e−8; accept‑if‑improve >5e−10. No external lineage artifacts imported. The joint centers+radii feasible set is nonconvex; there is no exact SOCP for the full problem. Further progress likely requires robust constrained Newton/SQP or qualitatively different non‑local\
    \ reorganizers.\n```"
