  \ focusing on its requirement without being overly lengthy.\n\nIn the introduction, I’ll outline the problem, context, and motivation for using zero-slack modeling. I’ll also raise the question of whether first-order or small non-local moves can increase the sum.\n\nFor the methodology, I’ll define the common verification pipeline, including the exact zero-slack radii LP equations, finalization process, acceptance criteria, and environment details. I'll mention the baseline packings used, such as the SOTA independent method and the lower baseline \"storage-best\".**Structuring techniques and submission details**\n\nIn section 2.3 of my submission, I’ll define several techniques like SCP-LP, LSS, and EQ-SCP-LP. I need to explain details for each method, including candidate selection for AS-Pivot DCPP and maximizing with Scalarized Single-LP. I'll also outline Global affine micro-warp and KKT Option-A, along with the CD-TR micro refiner and transfer tests. It’s crucial to correctly define\
