role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\n\nRecap: SQP v0/v1 dry-runs (IDs 808/809) confirmed mid-range local rigidity under exact zero-slack radii LP + iterative zero-tolerance finalize; no accepts. I’ll solidify the SQP foundation with self-check tests (null-space feasibility, trust-region cap, gradient sanity) before implementing v2 features (Armijo/Wolfe line search, adaptive trust region, active-set refresh, gradient caching).\n\nActions:\n/execute_action{storage write verity/tests_sqp.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/verity')\n  try:\n      import sqp_core_v1 as sqp\n  except Exception:\n      import sqp_core as sqp  # fallback\n\n  N = 32\n\n  def _seed_grid_minus_corners():\n      xs = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      ys = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      centers = []\n      for ix, X in enumerate(xs):\n          for iy, Y in enumerate(ys):\n              if (ix in (0,5)) and (iy in (0,5)):\n\
    \                  continue\n              centers.append([X, Y])\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\n  def load_baseline():\n      C = None\n      try:\n          C = np.load(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\")\n          if not (isinstance(C, np.ndarray) and C.shape == (N,2)):\n              C = None\n      except Exception:\n          C = None\n      if C is None:\n          C = _seed_grid_minus_corners()\n      return np.clip(C.astype(float), 0.0, 1.0)\n\n  def test_grad_sanity(C, basis_idx=None, h=8e-6):\n      G = sqp.finite_diff_grad_central(C, basis_idx=basis_idx, h=h)\n      assert np.all(np.isfinite(G)), \"Gradient contains non-finite values\"\n      print(f\"[tests_sqp] grad OK: shape={G.shape}, basis_len={len(basis_idx) if basis_idx is not None else N}, h={h:.1e}\")\n      return G\n\n  def test_nullspace_and_trust(C, G, tau=0.02):\n      s0, r0 = sqp.merit_sum_r(C)\n      A = sqp.build_A(C, sqp.detect_active_set(C, r0, tol=5e-16))\n      g_flat = G.reshape(-1)\n\
    \      delta_flat = sqp.nullspace_project_svd(A, g_flat, tau=tau)\n      # Null-space feasibility: A @ delta ≈ 0\n      if A.shape[0] > 0:\n          viol = np.linalg.norm(A @ delta_flat)\n          assert viol <= 1e-8, f\"Null-space violation too large: {viol:.3e}\"\n      # Trust-region cap\n      nrm = np.linalg.norm(delta_flat)\n      assert nrm <= tau + 1e-9, f\"Trust region violated: ||delta||={nrm:.3e} > tau={tau}\"\n      print(f\"[tests_sqp] null-space & trust OK: A={A.shape}, ||delta||={nrm:.3e}, tau={tau}\")\n      return delta_flat, A\n\n  def test_line_search_noop(C):\n      # Zero direction should never accept\n      s0, r0 = sqp.merit_sum_r(C)\n      zero = np.zeros(2*N, dtype=float)\n      C1, r1, s1 = sqp.line_search(C, zero, alphas=(1e-2, 1e-3, 1e-4), eps_accept=5e-10)\n      assert abs(s1 - s0) < 1e-12, \"Zero direction changed merit unexpectedly\"\n      print(f\"[tests_sqp] line search noop OK: s0={s0:.15f}, s1={s1:.15f}\")\n      return s0, s1\n\n  def run_self_checks():\n\
    \      C = load_baseline()\n      print(\"[tests_sqp] loaded baseline centers; running self-checks...\")\n      # Thinned deterministic basis to keep cost contained\n      basis_idx = list(range(0, N, 2))\n      G = test_grad_sanity(C, basis_idx=basis_idx, h=8e-6)\n      delta_flat, A = test_nullspace_and_trust(C, G, tau=0.02)\n      s0, s1 = test_line_search_noop(C)\n      print(\"[tests_sqp] ALL CHECKS PASSED\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      run_self_checks()\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/TODO_SQP_v2.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  SQP v2 TODO (before Phase-2 near-SOTA tests)\n  - Merit line search: Armijo/Wolfe on exact-LP merit; dynamic alpha grid; early stopping on sufficient increase.\n  - Adaptive trust region: enlarge on strong accepts (cap 0.06), shrink on reject streaks; condition-aware SVD tol.\n  - Gradient quality: broaden thinned FD basis with caching; mixed central/forward differences where clipping hits boundaries.\n  - Active-set refresh: rebuild\
    \ with K≥3N or all-pairs after accepts; deterministic tie-breaks; log active counts.\n  - Diagnostics: condition estimates, null-space residuals, alpha histories; unit tests (see tests_sqp.py).\n  - Safety: strict accept-if-improve (5e-10); float-safe finalize (pair_eps=5e-16); never persist unless improved.\n  - Publication plan: If v2 yields gains, draft concise note (methods, exact LP formulations, ids, full-precision) or a negative-result addendum otherwise.\n```\n\nPlan: Monitor leaderboard; implement SQP v2 upgrades next, then re-test at mid-range and only then try near-SOTA Phase-2."
