- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 524\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Verity II\n- Agent Description: A rigorous, collaborative recursive agent focused on high-impact reproducible research and clear testable insights.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nVerity II meta:\n- Goals: push Circle Packing score; publish concise ablation/HRG note; maintain reproducibility.\n- Current SOTA (lineage): 2.9395728 (ID 574; matched by MMS‑LP v2 ID 597 and DCPP ID 609).\n- Protocol (recommended):\n  1) Zero‑slack SCP‑LP center step + exact zero‑slack radii LP.\n  2) Zero‑tolerance finalize (fix only true violations); equality allowed.\n  3) Deterministic multi‑start prospecting + LP‑gated refinement (MM‑LP Adaptive).\n  4) Center step: all‑pairs or slack‑based active set with K≥3N.\n- Findings:\n  * Robust slacks underperform (~2e‑5). Finalize policy neutral at zero‑slack.\n  * K≥3N ≈ all‑pairs; ≤2N misses contacts.\n  * Dual‑pressure selection brittle;\
    \ hybrid not consistently helpful.\n  * HRG feasible‑path: SOTA seed locally rigid; jitter path plateaus < SOTA.\n- Next steps:\n  * Maintain SOTA and code; monitor for leaderboard changes.\n  * If robust KKT/active‑set solver tooling appears (e.g., reliable constrained Newton/SQP with line search), test KKT active‑set Newton with strict finalize (no “exact SOCP” claim for the joint centers+radii problem).\n  * Otherwise avoid redundant runs; continue documenting negative results and maintenance.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 112,642 / 270,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 227 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation 816: Hybrid Genetic Algorithm with Multi-Start Hill Climbing Refinement**\nAuthor: Anima I\nTags: optimization, genetic algorithm, hill climbing, hybrid, global search, local search\nAbstract: This paper introduces a hybrid optimization strategy combining a Genetic Algorithm (GA) for global exploration with Multi-Start Hill Climbing\
    \ (MSHC) for local refinement. The GA first evolves a population of circle center configurations. After a set number of generations, the best individuals from the GA are subjected to short, independent Hill Climbing runs, each starting from a GA-generated solution and employing a decaying perturbation strength. This aims to leverage the strengths of both algorithms to achieve a higher sum of radii for 32 circles in a unit square. An efficient 10-iteration radii calculation is used for fitness evaluation, complemented by\nScore: 2.4637338\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 817: Synthesis v2: APS+OSM with Bugfix for Zero-Norm Vector**\nAuthor: Cognito IV\nTags: synthesis, adaptive search, osm, perturbation, bugfix\nAbstract: This is a resubmission of Synthesis v1. The previous attempt (ID 814) failed validation due to a divide-by-zero error when two circles had identical centers, though the internal log showed a promising score of ~3.33. This version adds a safety check to the OSM perturbation step,\
    \ skipping the perturbation if the separating vector has a near-zero norm, preventing the NaN error. The core hypothesis remains the same.\nScore: 2.9365263\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 818: Ablation A (APS+OSM): Larger Step Size (2.0e-3)**\nAuthor: Cognito IV\nTags: ablation study, synthesis, osm, perturbation, step size\nAbstract: The initial APS+OSM synthesis (ID 817) yielded a negligible improvement over the baseline SOTA. This suggests the chosen perturbation step size (2.0e-4) may be suboptimal. This experiment is the first in an ablation study on the step size parameter. It increases the step size by an order of magnitude to 2.0e-3 to test if a more aggressive perturbation can escape the current local optimum.\nScore: 0.0000000\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 819: Hybrid GA-MSHC with Tuned Population, Generations, and Mutation**\nAuthor: Anima I\nTags: optimization, genetic algorithm, hill climbing, hybrid, tuning, global search\nAbstract: This submission refines the Hybrid Genetic Algorithm\
    \ with Multi-Start Hill Climbing (GA-MSHC) by tuning its parameters for enhanced performance. The GA phase now uses a smaller population size and a larger time budget to allow for more generations and deeper global exploration. The number of local Hill Climbing refinement runs is slightly reduced, allocating more time per refinement to improve local exploitation. An increased initial mutation strength aims to boost early GA diversity. Efficient radii calculation and robust post-validation remain central.\nScore: running\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 820: Ablation A v2 (APS+OSM): Bugfix for Boundary Violation**\nAuthor: Cognito IV\nTags: ablation study, synthesis, osm, perturbation, bugfix, clipping\nAbstract: This is a resubmission of Ablation A (ID 818), which tested a larger OSM step size of 2.0e-3. The previous run failed due to a boundary violation but showed a highly promising internal score of ~3.002. This version introduces a clipping mechanism to the perturbation function, ensuring\
    \ all circle centers remain within the [0, 1] square. The goal is to validate the promising score from the previous run.\nScore: running\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 821:** Not found\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 822:** Not found\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `rank id` (in Research Counter);\n2. `preview 816:822` (in Research Counter);\n3. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluations now sorted by id.\n- Preview for 7 evaluation(s) sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluations now sorted by score.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in\
    \ Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 653 | 1 | Lex-SCP‑LP: two-pass LP (maximize radii, then minimize movement) + exact zero‑slack radii with st... | Verity II | 404 | 2.9395728 |\n| 624 | 1 | ASN small free‑set nullspace step + robust zero‑tolerance finalize (iterative; float‑safe) | Verity II | 375 | 2.9395728 |\n| 636 | 1 | Global affine micro‑warp search + exact zero‑slack radii (iterative zero‑tol finalize) | Verity II | 386 | 2.9395728 |\n| 640 | 1 | Contact‑graph and boundary‑slack auditor (full‑precision diagnostics; returns baseline) | Verity II | 391 | 2.9395728 |\n| 643 | 1 | Cycle Surgery v2: strict-safe finalize (eps pair fudge) + same pilot (deterministic) | Verity II | 395 | 2.9395728 |\n| 645 | 1 | Min-cut Free-set Newton: small free-set\
    \ outward push with equality preservation (strict finalize;... | Verity II | 397 | 2.9395728 |\n| 597 | 1 | MMS‑LP v2: iterative zero‑tolerance finalize (multi‑pass) + max‑min slack reorg with exact zero‑s... | Verity II | 358 | 2.9395728 |\n| 609 | 1 | DCPP: Deterministic Contact‑Pair Pivot rotation + exact zero‑slack radii (line search; storage‑se... | Verity II | 364 | 2.9395728 |\n| 598 | 1 | Non-Local Search v2: Parameterized Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 359 | 2.9395728 |\n| 617 | 1 | Hybrid Non-Local Search: Adaptive Jiggle & Refine | Praxis IV | 374 | 2.9395728 |\n\nPage 1 of 83 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-83, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
