- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\n\nRecap: SQP v2.1 dual-subgradient dry-run (Eval 829) returned baseline; auditors (824/826) show FD gradients are unstable near kinks while LP dual subgradients are well-defined. Code, logs, and public updates are in place.\n\nPlan:\n- Prune recent admin/diagnostic ticks to keep context lean.\n- Implement SQP v2.2 components in storage (Armijo line search module and QR/SVD null-space/conditioning utilities). No near-SOTA runs until v2.2 unit tests pass.\n\nActions:\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"524-528\"\n    summary: \"Monitoring + SQP v2.1 diagnostics. (524) Previewed evals 816–822 (no SOTA movement). (525) Updated meta: SQP v2.1 TODOs and triggers. (526) SQP v2.1 Auditor (Eval 824): baseline 2.932012092024910; grad FD inconsistency (||Gf−Gc||≈2.729; rel_err≈29.37); null-space residual OK. (527) Dual-Gradient Auditor (Eval 826): dual\
    \ marginals available; ||g_dual||≈5.589e+00; cos vs thin central ≈ −0.179; FD unstable near kinks. (528) SQP v2.1 Dry‑Run (Eval 829): dual-subgradient + null-space + trust region; start/end 2.932012092024910→…49098; accepts=0; τ shrank 0.02→0.002; confirms mid-range local rigidity.\"\n```\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write verity/sqp_line_search_armijo.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # Armijo backtracking line search for merit = exact LP sum from S1.merit_sum_r(C).\n  # Inputs:\n  #   C: centers (N,2)\n  #   delta: direction (N,2) or flat (2N,)\n  #   S1: module exposing merit_sum_r(C)\n  #   alphas0: initial alpha candidates (largest to smallest)\n  #   c1: Armijo parameter (~1e-4)\n  #   eps_accept: strict accept threshold on absolute improvement (>5e-10)\n  # Returns: (C_best, r_best, s_best, alpha_used)\n  def armijo_step(C, delta, S1, alphas0=(1e-2, 6e-3, 3e-3, 1e-3, 6e-4, 3e-4, 1e-4), c1=1e-4, eps_accept=5e-10):\n      if delta.ndim\
    \ == 1:\n          N2 = delta.shape[0]\n          delta = delta.reshape(N2 // 2, 2)\n      s0, r0 = S1.merit_sum_r(C)\n      # Simple directional derivative estimate via finite difference along delta (small h)\n      h = 1e-6\n      C_h = np.clip(C + h * delta, 0.0, 1.0)\n      s_h, _ = S1.merit_sum_r(C_h)\n      gdir = (s_h - s0) / h\n\n      best_C, best_r, best_s, best_a = C, r0, s0, 0.0\n      for a in alphas0:\n          C_try = np.clip(C + a * delta, 0.0, 1.0)\n          s_try, r_try = S1.merit_sum_r(C_try)\n          # Armijo condition and strict accept guard\n          if (s_try >= s0 + c1 * a * gdir) and (s_try > s0 + eps_accept):\n              return C_try, r_try, s_try, a\n      return best_C, best_r, best_s, best_a\n```\n/execute_action{storage write verity/sqp_nullspace_qr.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # QR/SVD-based null-space projector with conditioning diagnostics.\n  # For A δ = 0 constraints (A is m x d), project g_flat into null(A) and cap by\
    \ trust region tau.\n\n  def project_nullspace(A, g_flat, tau=0.02, svd_tol=None):\n      d = g_flat.shape[0]\n      if A.size == 0:\n          delta = g_flat.copy()\n          nrm = float(np.linalg.norm(delta))\n          if nrm > tau and nrm > 0:\n              delta = (tau / nrm) * delta\n          return delta, {\"rank\": 0, \"cond\": 1.0, \"m\": 0, \"d\": d}\n\n      # Prefer SVD for robustness; report conditioning from singular values\n      try:\n          U, S, Vh = np.linalg.svd(A, full_matrices=False)\n          rank = int(np.sum(S > (S[0] * 1e-12 if S.size > 0 else 0.0))) if svd_tol is None else int(np.sum(S > svd_tol))\n          cond = float((S[0] / S[-1]) if (S.size > 0 and S[-1] > 0) else np.inf)\n          V = Vh.T\n          # Null-space basis Z = columns of V corresponding to ~zero singular values\n          if svd_tol is None:\n              svd_tol = (S[0] if S.size > 0 else 1.0) * 1e-10\n          mask = (S <= svd_tol)\n          if np.any(mask):\n              Z\
    \ = V[:, np.where(mask)[0]]\n          else:\n              # If no exact nullspace, take the last vector as approximate null\n              Z = V[:, -1:].copy()\n          delta = Z @ (Z.T @ g_flat)\n      except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n          # Fallback via normal equations\n          M = A @ A.T + 1e-8 * np.eye(A.shape[0])\n          y = np.linalg.solve(M, A @ g_flat)\n          delta = g_flat - A.T @ y\n          rank = -1; cond = np.inf\n\n      nrm = float(np.linalg.norm(delta))\n      if nrm > tau and nrm > 0:\n          delta = (tau / nrm) * delta\n      return delta, {\"rank\": rank, \"cond\": cond, \"m\": int(A.shape[0]), \"d\": int(A.shape[1])}\n```\n\n"
