tick: 531
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\n\nRecap: SQP v0/v1/v2 mid-range dry-runs confirmed local rigidity (no accepts). I’ve added SQP v2.2 utilities (Armijo line search and QR/SVD null-space projector) and a tests harness (tests_sqp_v22.py). Next, I’ll run a diagnostics-only evaluation to execute the tests in the sandbox and return a verified baseline packing. This does not attempt improvements; it validates the components end-to-end and logs detailed diagnostics to STDOUT.\n\nActions:\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SQP v2.2 Unit-Test Runner: grad/null-space/Armijo invariants (diagnostics-only; returns baseline)\"\ntags: \"sqp, diagnostics, unit tests, zero-slack, linear programming\"\nabstract: \"Runs storage/verity/tests_sqp_v22.py to validate SQP v2.2 components in-sandbox (grad consistency, null-space residual, trust-region cap, Armijo invariants). Then returns a verified baseline packing via exact zero-slack radii LP (sqp_core_v1.merit_sum_r).\
    \ No improvement attempts; accept-if-improve remains enforced in future runs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/verity')\n  try:\n      import tests_sqp_v22 as TS\n      import sqp_core_v1 as S1\n  except Exception as e:\n      TS = None\n      S1 = None\n\n  N = 32\n\n  def _seed_grid_minus_corners():\n      xs = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      ys = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      centers = []\n      for ix, X in enumerate(xs):\n          for iy, Y in enumerate(ys):\n              if (ix in (0,5)) and (iy in (0,5)):\n                  continue\n              centers.append([X, Y])\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\n  def _load_centers():\n      try:\n          C = np.load(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\")\n          if isinstance(C, np.ndarray) and C.shape == (N,2):\n              return np.clip(C.astype(float), 0.0, 1.0)\n      except Exception:\n          pass\n      return _seed_grid_minus_corners()\n\n  def construct_packing()\
    \ -> tuple:\n      C = _load_centers()\n      if TS is not None and S1 is not None:\n          print(\"[SQP v2.2 tests] Starting diagnostics run...\")\n          # Run diagnostics (grad consistency, null-space residual, TR cap, Armijo invariants)\n          try:\n              TS.run_all()\n          except Exception as e:\n              print(f\"[SQP v2.2 tests] Diagnostics error: {e!r}\")\n          # Compute exact zero-slack radii and report baseline merit\n          s, r = S1.merit_sum_r(C)\n          print(f\"[SQP v2.2 tests] baseline sum={s:.15f}\")\n          return np.array(C, dtype=float), np.array(r, dtype=float)\n      else:\n          # Fallback: safe baseline radii from box distances\n          x, y = C[:,0], C[:,1]\n          r = np.maximum(1e-8, np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0-x, y, 1.0-y]))\n          print(\"[SQP v2.2 tests] Module import failed; returning safe baseline without diagnostics.\")\n          return np.array(C, dtype=float), np.array(r, dtype=float)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Managing output and tokens**\n\nI’m generating logs for validating grad consistency, nullspace residual, TR, and LS, which could be useful. To maintain token efficiency, I wonder if older ticks should be pruned, but there's a cooldown active. The last prune was at tick 529, and currently, it's tick 531, with only 2 ticks left on cooldown. Even though I can’t prune now, I can quickly scan new evaluations using rank ID and preview since they’ve been done. I’ll consider compiling a plan while keeping formatting minimal.**Implementing test submissions**\n\nIt’s fine if I don’t run the experiment every tick, but since we’ve been active, I think we can create a submission that executes the tests script and returns the baseline pack from storage. That’s experimental, but it’s mainly analysis, and tests within submissions were accepted earlier. In the pipeline, they prefer to avoid running near-SOTA until tests pass, so I’ll make sure we include code to load the best centers\
  \ and radii from storage, computing it through exact radii LP. Let’s implement that in run.py with logging for outputs!**Creating submission for SQP v2.2**\n\nLet’s set up a submission titled \"SQP v2.2 Unit-Test Runner: grad/null-space/Armijo invariants; returns baseline.\" I’ll tag it with \"sqp, diagnostics, unit tests, zero-slack, linear programming.\" The abstract will clarify that it runs tests_sqp_v22.run_all and returns storage-best exact LP finalize radii without model changes. \n\nThe code will import numpy, sys, and the necessary modules, then load baseline centers. I’ll compute r using S1.merit_sum_r, run all tests, and return the centers and r. I also want to recap the plan and actions before submitting."
