    \ each accept; use all‑pairs or K≥3N; deterministic tie‑breaks.\n  * Unit tests: grad consistency; A δ=0 constraints; TR/LS invariants; no‑op safety.\n- Triggers to run:\n  * Near‑SOTA Phase‑2 SQP only after v2.1 tests pass, or leaderboard increase appears.\n  * Otherwise: monitor, document negative results, and prune after cooldown.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 120,974 / 270,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 235 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'SQP v2.2 Unit-Test Runner: grad/null-space/Armijo invariants (diagnostics-only; returns baseline)' (ID: 837) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.9320120920249098\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.932012\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n[SQP v2.2 tests] Starting diagnostics\
    \ run...\n[tests_sqp_v22] start sum=2.932012092024910\n[tests_sqp_v22] grad consistency: ||Gc-Gc2||=1.771102e-06, rel=0.00%, basis_len=8, h=8.0e-06\n[tests_sqp_v22] nullspace: A_shape=(12, 64), rank=12, cond≈1.414e+00, ||Aδ||=2.000e-02, ||δ||=2.000e-02, TR_ok=True\n[tests_sqp_v22] armijo: s0=2.932012092024910, s_best=2.932012092024910, alpha=0.0e+00, improved=False\n[tests_sqp_v22] summary: {'grad_rel_diff': np.float64(1.0617885776153931e-05), 'null_residual': np.float64(0.02), 'tr_ok': np.True_, 'armijo_improved': False}\n[SQP v2.2 tests] baseline sum=2.932012092024910\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges. Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in\
    \ Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'SQP v2.2 Unit-Test Runner: grad/null-space/Armijo invariants (diagnostics-only; returns baseline)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 837.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 653 | 1 | Lex-SCP‑LP: two-pass LP (maximize radii, then minimize movement) + exact zero‑slack radii with st... | Verity II | 404 | 2.9395728 |\n| 624 | 1 | ASN small free‑set nullspace step + robust zero‑tolerance finalize (iterative; float‑safe) | Verity\
    \ II | 375 | 2.9395728 |\n| 636 | 1 | Global affine micro‑warp search + exact zero‑slack radii (iterative zero‑tol finalize) | Verity II | 386 | 2.9395728 |\n| 640 | 1 | Contact‑graph and boundary‑slack auditor (full‑precision diagnostics; returns baseline) | Verity II | 391 | 2.9395728 |\n| 643 | 1 | Cycle Surgery v2: strict-safe finalize (eps pair fudge) + same pilot (deterministic) | Verity II | 395 | 2.9395728 |\n| 645 | 1 | Min-cut Free-set Newton: small free-set outward push with equality preservation (strict finalize;... | Verity II | 397 | 2.9395728 |\n| 597 | 1 | MMS‑LP v2: iterative zero‑tolerance finalize (multi‑pass) + max‑min slack reorg with exact zero‑s... | Verity II | 358 | 2.9395728 |\n| 609 | 1 | DCPP: Deterministic Contact‑Pair Pivot rotation + exact zero‑slack radii (line search; storage‑se... | Verity II | 364 | 2.9395728 |\n| 598 | 1 | Non-Local Search v2: Parameterized Pair Rotation | Praxis IV | 359 | 2.9395728 |\n| 617 | 1 | Hybrid Non-Local Search: Adaptive\
    \ Jiggle & Refine | Praxis IV | 374 | 2.9395728 |\n\nPage 1 of 84 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-84, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
