- text: "Identity: Verity II (Recursive Agent)\nLocation: Research Counter\n\nRecap: GRH (Evaluation 853) ran with groupwise radius equalities in the SCP‑LP step. Results: storage‑best with quadrants/rows both 2.932012092024910; jittered seed ≈2.910998881347077 for both modes. No gains; confirms local rigidity and that tying radii within coarse groups doesn’t unlock better moves near this baseline.\n\nPlan:\n- Log GRH results to storage.\n- Record a concise private summary and interpretation.\n- Prune this window next tick per token guidance.\n\n/execute_action{storage write verity/evals_grh_853.tsv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id\ttick\tseed\tmode\tsum_full\taccepted\n  853\t544\tstorage-best\tquadrants\t2.932012092024910\tFALSE\n  853\t544\tstorage-best\trows\t2.932012092024910\tFALSE\n  853\t544\tstorage-best-jitter\tquadrants\t2.910998881347077\tFALSE\n  853\t544\tstorage-best-jitter\trows\t2.910998881347077\tFALSE\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"GRH (Groupwise Radius Homotopy) — method and result\"\ncontent: |\n  Method: During the SCP‑LP center‑update step, tie radii within coarse groups (quadrants or horizontal bands) via equality constraints to encourage coordinated, non‑local motions; then release equalities and re‑solve exact zero‑slack radii LP with iterative zero‑tolerance finalize. Strict accept‑if‑improve.\n\n  Eval 853 (tick 544):\n  - storage‑best, quadrants: 2.932012092024910\n  - storage‑best, rows:      2.932012092024910\n  - storage‑best‑jitter, quadrants: 2.910998881347077\n  - storage‑best‑jitter, rows:      2.910998881347077\n  Accepts: 0.\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - Groupwise radius equalities in the step LP did not unlock new directions; near the strong baseline, added coupling likely suppresses fine geometric adjustments needed to maintain tight contacts.\n  - Consistent with prior rigidity findings: coordinated per‑group moves do not overcome first‑order stiffness under exact zero‑slack\
    \ radii LP + zero‑tolerance finalize.\n\n  Next:\n  - Keep GRH recorded as a negative result.\n  - Maintain SOTA and continue SQP v2.x refinement/testing offline; run only upon solver upgrade or leaderboard change.\n```"
