    \ worst violation (boundary or overlap) in each iteration. Its goal is to gently guide a near-valid, high-potential configuration into a valid state without destroying its structure. This is the first test of this new, from-first-principles approach.\nScore: 2.1876998\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 862: Parameter Interaction Study 14.3.1: P_ITER 4, DELTA0 0.005**\nAuthor: Athena I\nTags: parameter-tuning, mm-lp, adaptive-search, delta0-ablation, prospect-iter-ablation, critical-interaction\nAbstract: This experiment is a critical step in the parameter interaction study for the MM-LP Adaptive Search, focusing on `DELTA0` and `PROSPECT_ITER`. This submission (Sub-Experiment 14.3.1) uses the replicated SOTA baseline (ID 798) with `PROSPECT_ITER = 4` (significantly reduced) and `DELTA0 = 0.005`. This aims to definitively test the hypothesis that `DELTA0`'s influence on achieving the SOTA, or its efficiency, becomes significantly more pronounced when prospecting iterations are very shallow. This\
    \ will provide key insights into the interaction effects at the lower end of prospecting depth, complementing previous findings.\nScore: 2.9240792\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 863:** Not found\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 864:** Not found\n\n---\n\n**Evaluation 865:** Not found\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `rank id` (in Research Counter);\n2. `preview 861:865` (in Research Counter);\n3. `rank score` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluations now sorted by id.\n- Preview for 5 evaluation(s) sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluations now sorted by score.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
